            34 => 
            array (
                'id' => 203,
                'lang_code' => 'en',
            'name' => 'Information Technology (IT) Leadership Skills',
            'description' => '<p>Information Technology leadership is the group of senior executives in an organization responsible for the information technology (IT) infrastructure and applications that enable and drive the overarching business strategy and goals. The top IT leader is most frequently referred to as the chief information officer.</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>There are many different styles of IT leadership, including servant leadership and paternalistic leadership. Examples of important leadership skills include soft (interpersonal) skills, hard skills and the ability to inspire employees to leverage IT to improve processes.</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>This course designed for Information Technology managers looking to develop their IT leadership skills.&nbsp; It is a highly practical course, focusing on the leadership skills that have the biggest impact on business performance and career success.&nbsp;</p>',
                'duration' => '5',
                'days_content' => '["<ul>\\n\\t<li>How CIOs optimize time and activity</li>\\n\\t<li>Secrets of successful CIOs</li>\\n\\t<li>Leadership opportunities for IT professionals</li>\\n\\t<li>Building and maintaining reputation</li>\\n\\t<li>Developing a personal brand</li>\\n</ul>\\n","<ul>\\n\\t<li>Assessing your style of leadership</li>\\n\\t<li>Recognizing leadership styles in others</li>\\n\\t<li>Influencing strategies for the different leadership styles</li>\\n\\t<li>Corporate politics &mdash; the inside track</li>\\n\\t<li>Developing successful political networks</li>\\n</ul>\\n","<ul>\\n\\t<li>A model for high performing IT teams</li>\\n\\t<li>Understanding your team&rsquo;s dynamics</li>\\n\\t<li>Building and motivating IT teams</li>\\n\\t<li>Developing staff in real time</li>\\n\\t<li>Organizing IT teams to maximize performance</li>\\n</ul>\\n","<ul>\\n\\t<li>The process of innovation and the creative mind-set</li>\\n\\t<li>Techniques to foster innovation</li>\\n\\t<li>The importance of technology in innovation</li>\\n\\t<li>Selecting the best innovation ideas</li>\\n\\t<li>Lanterns to the future &mdash; creating technology vision</li>\\n</ul>\\n","<ul>\\n\\t<li>T leaders at board level &mdash; what CEOs look for</li>\\n\\t<li>The responsibilities of IT corporate leadership</li>\\n\\t<li>A process model for IT to business alignment</li>\\n\\t<li>Technology governance structures</li>\\n\\t<li>IT&rsquo;s brand &ndash; aligning reality and perception</li>\\n</ul>\\n"]',
                'related_courses' => '[154,142]',
                'category_id' => 41,
                'online' => 0,
                'created_at' => '2025-04-03 12:43:33',
                'updated_at' => '2025-04-03 12:43:33',
            ),
            35 => 
            array (
                'id' => 205,
                'lang_code' => 'en',
                'name' => 'Digital Leadership Programme',
                'description' => '<p>When organisations operating at a faster speed, it must use entrepreneurial thinking to generate innovative ideas that create value for customers, design digital or IT-enabled services quickly using advanced technologies, and build organizational capability to deliver such services to meet customer expectations.</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>Faster design and delivery of these digital services requires agility within the IT system and business architectures under the co-leadership of IT and business executives. This is in essence the definition of digital leadership&mdash;a process that is essential to developing and sustaining a culture of innovation by bringing ideas to fruition quickly using an agile IT and business architecture.</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>Digital leadership is a strategic use of a company&rsquo;s&rsquo; digital assets to achieve business goals. This can be dealt with both organizationally and at an individual level. Looking at it from an individual level, this is often carried out by those responsible for overseeing the digital assets.</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>Digital leadership ensures that your workers eliminate tasks that wasted time in the past. With the automation of some of these tasks, employees can spend more time on important matters like talking to prospects and attending to customers.</p>

<p>You will become a digitally informed, empowered leader and know how to prepare and help your organization respond more effectively to technology-driven change!</p>',
                'duration' => '5',
                'days_content' => '["<ul>\\n\\t<li>The Context for Digital</li>\\n\\t<li>What is digital transformation?</li>\\n\\t<li>Why does it matter</li>\\n\\t<li>What does success look like?</li>\\n\\t<li>Barriers to success</li>\\n\\t<li>Digital Transformation Roadmap</li>\\n\\t<li>Customer Centricity</li>\\n\\t<li>Think Big, Start Small, Scale Fast</li>\\n</ul>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n","<ul>\\n\\t<li>Understanding the business risks</li>\\n\\t<li>Types of digital transformation projects</li>\\n\\t<li>Key business drivers for digital transformation</li>\\n\\t<li>Emerging technologies and how they are used</li>\\n\\t<li>Gartner&rsquo;s Hype Cycle</li>\\n\\t<li>Stages of transformation</li>\\n\\t<li>Where digital transformation fits within your organisation</li>\\n</ul>\\n","<ul>\\n\\t<li>Understanding your own business readiness</li>\\n\\t<li>Create a digitally ready culture</li>\\n\\t<li>Barriers to change</li>\\n\\t<li>Influencing stakeholders</li>\\n\\t<li>Stakeholder engagement</li>\\n\\t<li>Areas ripe for transformation</li>\\n\\t<li>Collaborative working</li>\\n\\t<li>Getting buy-in across the organisation</li>\\n\\t<li>Building teams for transformation</li>\\n</ul>\\n","<ul>\\n\\t<li>Developing your Digital transformation strategy</li>\\n\\t<li>Innovation &amp; digitally disruptive business models</li>\\n\\t<li>Challenging existing business models</li>\\n\\t<li>Planning your digital transformation</li>\\n\\t<li>Running a digital project</li>\\n\\t<li>Executing your transformation</li>\\n\\t<li>Tools &amp; methodologies for implementing digital transformation</li>\\n\\t<li>Review and measuring results</li>\\n\\t<li>Build your action plan</li>\\n</ul>\\n","<ul>\\n\\t<li>Building Momentum for Change</li>\\n\\t<li>Enabling the Culture for Digital</li>\\n\\t<li>Embedding Change and Taking Personal Action</li>\\n\\t<li>Reflection and personal pledges</li>\\n</ul>\\n"]',
                'related_courses' => '[203,142]',
                'category_id' => 41,
                'online' => 0,
                'created_at' => '2025-04-03 12:43:33',
                'updated_at' => '2025-04-03 12:43:33',
            ),
            36 => 
            array (
                'id' => 209,
                'lang_code' => 'en',
                'name' => 'Leading Organizational Resilience Programme',
                'description' => '<p>In highly volatile and uncertain times, organizations need to develop a resilience capacity which enables them to cope effectively with unexpected events, bounce back from crises, and even foster future success.&nbsp;</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>Organizational resilience is the ability to survive a crisis, and thrive in a world of uncertainty. It isn&rsquo;t just about getting through crises. A truly resilient organization has two other important capabilities &ndash; the foresight and situation awareness to prevent potential crises emerging, and an ability to turn crises into a source of strategic opportunity.</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>An organizational resilience approach will encourage you to look beyond risk management towards a more holistic view of your business health and success. A resilient organization should not only survive over the long term, but should also flourish &ndash; passing the test of time.</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p><strong>Leading Organizational Resilience Programme,</strong> will teach you how to anticipate, prepare for, and respond and adapt to incremental change and sudden disruptions in order to survive and prosper. You will learn from facilitators who have experience as thought leaders, key influencers in industry and subject matter experts.</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>',
                'duration' => '5',
            'days_content' => '["<h6>Introduction to organisational Resilience</h6>\\n\\n<h6>&nbsp;</h6>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>What is Organizational Resilience and why is it important to leadership?&nbsp;</li>\\n\\t<li>Exploring the latest strategic tensions quadrant framework</li>\\n\\t<li>Reviewing your organization&rsquo;s current perceptions of performance</li>\\n\\t<li>Identifying where to focus attention through personal and peer review</li>\\n</ul>\\n","<h6>&nbsp;</h6>\\n\\n<h6>Organization&rsquo;s future resilience profile&nbsp;</h6>\\n\\n<h6>&nbsp;</h6>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>What does your organization&rsquo;s future resilience profile need to be?</li>\\n\\t<li>What does this mean for your organization?</li>\\n\\t<li>What leadership mind set is required to develop Organizational Resilience?&nbsp;</li>\\n\\t<li>Reviewing the changes necessary and the leadership actions needed to fulfil these</li>\\n\\t<li>Action planning and next steps through personal and peer review</li>\\n</ul>\\n","<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<h6>Practical implemntation techniques</h6>\\n\\n<h6>&nbsp;</h6>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Identify the 16 key elements that define a resilient organization, and appreciate how they can be prioritized in the context of your business</li>\\n\\t<li>Determine practical implementation techniques to help you embed resilient principles</li>\\n\\t<li>Recognize combinations of circumstances and issues that can be catalysts for failure or success</li>\\n\\t<li>Use the BSI Online Benchmark Assessment tool to assess your organization against the 16 key elements of resilience</li>\\n</ul>\\n","<h6>&nbsp;</h6>\\n\\n<h6>Understand the five Main Principles of Organisational Resilience</h6>\\n\\n<h6>&nbsp;</h6>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Leadership &ndash; Setting the priorities, commitment and allocating resources</li>\\n\\t<li>Culture &ndash; A resilient culture is built on principles of empowerment, purpose and trust</li>\\n\\t<li>People &ndash; Enhancing business resilience through people selection (HR)</li>\\n\\t<li>Systems &ndash; Globalization and systems enable resilience</li>\\n\\t<li>Settings &ndash; Resilient Virtual Organisation, workplace resilience equals workplace agility</li>\\n</ul>\\n","<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<h6>Business Continuity Management and Resilience</h6>\\n\\n<h6>&nbsp;</h6>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>What is BCM?</li>\\n\\t<li>International Standards and BCM</li>\\n\\t<li>Business impact analysis</li>\\n\\t<li>Developing a BCM team</li>\\n</ul>\\n"]',
                'related_courses' => '[142,154,233,150]',
                'category_id' => 41,
