            40 => 
            array (
                'id' => 213,
                'lang_code' => 'en',
                'name' => 'Leading with Resilience',
                'description' => '<p>In any working environment where employees are vulnerable or feel overwhelmed, resilient leadership is instrumental in preventing pressures and demands from building up to breaking point.</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>Resilient leadership is a key enabler to build and maintain workplace wellbeing and resilience. It is the fuel of healthy high performance within teams.<br />
&nbsp;</p>

<p>Resilience is the human capacity to meet adversity, setbacks and trauma, and then recover from them in order to live life fully.</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>Resilient leaders have the ability to sustain their energy level under pressure, to cope with disruptive changes and adapt. They bounce back from setbacks. They also overcome major difficulties without engaging in dysfunctional behaviour or harming others,&nbsp;They maintain a positive attitude and a strong sense of opportunity during periods of turbulence. When faced with ambiguity, a resilient leader finds ways to move forward and avoids getting stuck.</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p><strong>Leading with Resilience programme</strong> will provide managers with practical strategies, tactics and tools to effectively influence, inspire and support resilience and minimise stress at work.</p>',
                'duration' => '5',
                'days_content' => '["<ul>\\n\\t<li>Key Aspects of Resilience</li>\\n\\t<li>Understanding the Importance of Resilience to Achieve Success</li>\\n\\t<li>The resilient Leader Role in Turbulent Times</li>\\n\\t<li>The Difference between Resilience and Change Management</li>\\n\\t<li>Reflecting and Clarifying our Strengths and Growth Areas</li>\\n</ul>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>The Leader&rsquo;s Role in Improving Organization and People&rsquo;s Adaptive Capabilities</li>\\n\\t<li>The Implications of Resilience for Leadership</li>\\n\\t<li>The Importance of Anticipating Change</li>\\n\\t<li>Indicators to Measure and Anticipate the Forces of Change</li>\\n\\t<li>Trusting and Engaging in Constructive Conflict</li>\\n</ul>\\n","<ul>\\n\\t<li>The Importance of Employee Engagement</li>\\n\\t<li>The Key Drivers in the Service Profit Chain</li>\\n\\t<li>The Necessity for Leaders to be Confident and Resilient</li>\\n\\t<li>Bringing Focus and Priorities to Action</li>\\n\\t<li>Empowering Teams to be Action-Oriented</li>\\n</ul>\\n","<ul>\\n\\t<li>Ability to Create, Engage and Nurture Social Change</li>\\n\\t<li>Social Media, Whistle Blowing and Breaking the Brand Bullying</li>\\n\\t<li>Social Entrepreneurship and Its Importance for Leaders</li>\\n\\t<li>Developing the Resilience to Thrive in Change</li>\\n</ul>\\n","<ul>\\n\\t<li>How the Brain Develops Resilience</li>\\n\\t<li>Harnessing the Brain&rsquo;s Neuroplasticity to Recover Resilience</li>\\n\\t<li>Using Mindfulness to Foster Self Awareness</li>\\n\\t<li>How Neuroscience is Revolutionizing our Thinking About Feelings</li>\\n\\t<li>How Positive Emotions Build Resilience</li>\\n\\t<li>Assessing your Capabilities for Resilient Performance</li>\\n</ul>\\n","<ul>\\n\\t<li>Signs of Resilience Mastery</li>\\n\\t<li>Developing Resilient Managers</li>\\n\\t<li>Developing a More Resilient Organization</li>\\n\\t<li>Challenges of Resilience for Executives</li>\\n\\t<li>Leadership Growth Plan and Resilience Mastery</li>\\n</ul>\\n"]',
                'related_courses' => '[211,209,142,154]',
                'category_id' => 41,
                'online' => 0,
                'created_at' => '2025-04-03 12:43:34',
                'updated_at' => '2025-04-03 12:43:34',
