            64 => 
            array (
                'id' => 241,
                'lang_code' => 'en',
                'name' => 'Building Task Leadership Skills',
                'description' => '<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>True leaders realize there is always room for improvement. Recognizing that you are a task-oriented leader means you have already taken the important first steps to analyzing your own leadership style. Being task-oriented is useful in many situations. However, an exceptional leader continually adjusts and adapts his leadership style to match the specific needs of the organization.&nbsp;</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>The&nbsp;<strong>Building Task leadership skills</strong>&nbsp; training course focuses on the utilisation of productive practices that enables a person to become more self-confident and communicate in a confident manner. This is vital to achieving effective and successful project work, establish priorities and meet deadlines.&nbsp;This is crucial because the level of competition in nowadays business environments requires an emphasis on practices that build a personal level of self-confidence and assists in the management of personal and workgroup tasks, priorities and projects.</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p><strong>This 10 days train</strong>ing course training course will introduce you to different models of leadership and practical tools to help you shape your personal style of leadership and make you a more effective leader.</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>',
                'duration' => '10',
                'days_content' => '["<h6><strong>Creating a Confident and Credible Image</strong></h6>\\n\\n<p><br />\\n&ndash; Where does self-confidence come from?<br />\\n&ndash; The comfort zone and its impact on business success.<br />\\n&ndash; Banishing the fear of speaking in public.<br />\\n&ndash; Self-perception and its impact on confidence.<br />\\n&ndash; How being confident can help you raise your profile?<br />\\n&ndash; Body language and its impact on credibility.</p>\\n","<h6><strong>Confident Communication to Groups</strong></h6>\\n\\n<p><br />\\n&ndash; How to run efficient and effective meetings?<br />\\n&ndash; How to prepare for and structure a business presentation?<br />\\n&ndash; How to get over the nerves of giving a business presentation?<br />\\n&ndash; Handling questions from senior leaders.<br />\\n&ndash; How to sell yourself and your organization and your ideas?<br />\\n&ndash; Developing rapport in business presentations.</p>\\n","<h6><strong>Confident Communicating to&nbsp;Get&nbsp;Results</strong></h6>\\n\\n<p><br />\\n&ndash; The power of using stories to get messages across.<br />\\n&ndash; Using analogies effectively.<br />\\n&ndash; Using evidence to win people over to your way of thinking.<br />\\n&ndash; Increasing your personal power and charisma.<br />\\n&ndash; When to be strong and when to play weak.<br />\\n&ndash; Inclusive/exclusive language and its effect on people.</p>\\n","<h6><strong>Communicating Passion</strong></h6>\\n\\n<p><br />\\n&ndash; The importance of passion.<br />\\n&ndash; Developing courage and confidence in conflict situations.<br />\\n&ndash; Beating your comfort zone and taking more risks.<br />\\n&ndash; Using our full range of communication.<br />\\n&ndash; Powerful closes that move people to action.<br />\\n&ndash; Become a magnetic personality.</p>\\n","<h6><strong>Enhancing your Profile within the Business</strong></h6>\\n\\n<p><br />\\n&ndash; How to conduct yourself to senior people?<br />\\n&ndash; How to sell change to people who don&rsquo;t want to change?<br />\\n&ndash; How to sell unpopular policies to team?<br />\\n&ndash; How to make yourself memorable?<br />\\n&ndash; Be a radiator, not a drain.<br />\\n&ndash; The speaking challenges.</p>\\n","<h6><strong>Introduction of Work Task Concepts</strong></h6>\\n\\n<p><br />\\n&ndash; Comprehending the role of self-management in managing tasks.<br />\\n&ndash; Overview and context of task management.<br />\\n&ndash; Identifying reasons for the current focus in business on managing tasks.<br />\\n&ndash; Comprehending how work is accomplished in organizations.<br />\\n&ndash; Identifying the role of strategic management in leadership of tasks.<br />\\n&ndash; Comprehending the role of organization type in task management.</p>\\n","<h6><strong>Importance of Planning in Management of Tasks</strong></h6>\\n\\n<p><br />\\n&ndash; Clarifying goals, objectives, assumptions and constraints in work.<br />\\n&ndash; Integrating a scope, work structure and management plan in assignments.<br />\\n&ndash; Learning to identify and manage stakeholders.<br />\\n&ndash; Identifying risk techniques that affect tasks, priorities and deadlines.<br />\\n&ndash; Comprehending how to develop clarity in purpose and objectives in task assignments.<br />\\n&ndash; Identifying the skills necessary to lead and manage work tasks.</p>\\n","<h6><strong>Setting Priorities &amp; Deadlines in our Time Management</strong></h6>\\n\\n<p><br />\\n&ndash; Using the manner, approaching work as an initial time management plan.<br />\\n&ndash; Planning for time management, scheduling and meeting deadlines.<br />\\n&ndash; Integrating time management into development of priorities.<br />\\n&ndash; Making the most from meetings, e-mails, interruptions and transition time.<br />\\n&ndash; Developing a personal plan, with a &lsquo;to do&rsquo; list and priorities.<br />\\n&ndash; Dealing with time wasters, procrastination and bosses.</p>\\n","<h6><strong>Skills Required to Deal with People in our Work Assignments</strong></h6>\\n\\n<p><br />\\n&ndash; Identifying skills required to obtain the help of others on tasks.<br />\\n&ndash; The importance of understanding our ways of working with others.<br />\\n&ndash; The importance of interpersonal skill in accomplishment of tasks.<br />\\n&ndash; Identifying interpersonal work styles of self and other.<br />\\n&ndash; Comprehending task flexibility and versatility in people leadership.<br />\\n&ndash; Learning how to work better with others to have productive work.</p>\\n","<h6><strong>Personally, Managing Tasks to Implement Change</strong></h6>\\n\\n<p><br />\\n&ndash; Learning techniques to use communication for success in tasks.<br />\\n&ndash; Comprehend the characteristics of proper communication.<br />\\n&ndash; Identifying methods to deal with human change patterns.<br />\\n&ndash; Building a personal plan to become more effective with self-management.<br />\\n&ndash; Dealing with some people who struggle with change.<br />\\n&ndash; Practicing techniques to help colleagues with change.</p>\\n"]',
