            98 => 
            array (
                'id' => 289,
                'lang_code' => 'en',
                'name' => 'Facilitation Skills for Trainers and Team Leaders',
                'description' => '<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>Training facilitation skills helps trainers, managers and team leaders improve their ability to engage everyone for better brainstorming and problems-solving efforts. By facilitating everyone&rsquo;s participation, problems are better understood, better decisions are made and more support for solutions is achieved. Plus, the facilitation skills developed in this interactive training session helps create more effective group dynamics and improve team efforts and cohesiveness.</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>Develop effective facilitation and group process skills in this interactive course designed for trainers, managers, team leaders and anyone required to facilitate group activities or discussions.</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>&nbsp;In this course, we focus on developing critical skills to engage audience participation and lead discussions the get maximum results. Participants learn skills to improve listening, paraphrasing and questioning techniques that achieve learning objectives efficiently.</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>Everyone leaves this facilitation skills training course with a better understanding of group dynamics and how to give presentations that focus groups for better understanding and application of principles.&nbsp;</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>',
                'duration' => '5',
                'days_content' => '["<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<h6><strong>What is facilitation?</strong></h6>\\n\\n<h6>&nbsp;</h6>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Facilitation vs. presenting training vs. team leader</li>\\n\\t<li>Team leaders as facilitators</li>\\n\\t<li>Types of facilitation</li>\\n\\t<li>What do facilitators do?</li>\\n\\t<li>Facilitation techniques</li>\\n</ul>\\n","<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<p><strong>Group dynamics and group functions</strong></p>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>How teams function</li>\\n\\t<li>How to help groups grow and be productive</li>\\n\\t<li>Brainstorming and problem solving techniques</li>\\n\\t<li>Help groups be more creative</li>\\n\\t<li>Consensus and other group decision making techniques</li>\\n</ul>\\n","<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<h6><strong>Facilitator issues</strong></h6>\\n\\n<h6>&nbsp;</h6>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Meeting planning and coordination tips</li>\\n\\t<li>Set a productive group climate</li>\\n\\t<li>Establish ground rules</li>\\n\\t<li>Help team members to be productive</li>\\n\\t<li>Clarify group and leader functions</li>\\n\\t<li>How to select team leaders in your organization</li>\\n\\t<li>Deal with difficult and angry group members</li>\\n</ul>\\n","<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<h6><strong>Resources- Facilitation Tool Kit</strong></h6>\\n\\n<h6>&nbsp;</h6>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Give Directions</li>\\n\\t<li>Give feedback</li>\\n\\t<li>Ask questions to solicit information and gain different points of view</li>\\n\\t<li>Listen actively</li>\\n</ul>\\n","<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<h6><strong>Using group problem solving techniques&nbsp;</strong></h6>\\n\\n<h6>&nbsp;</h6>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Gaining consensus for decision making&nbsp;</li>\\n\\t<li>Overcoming common group problems&nbsp;</li>\\n\\t<li>Increase participation and commitment&nbsp;</li>\\n\\t<li>Practice</li>\\n\\t<li>Developing Your Action Plan</li>\\n\\t<li>Clarify to understand and focus</li>\\n\\t<li>Coach to correct mistakes</li>\\n\\t<li>Increase participation and commitment</li>\\n\\t<li>Use charting to generate discussion and verify understanding</li>\\n\\t<li>Co-facilitation issues</li>\\n</ul>\\n"]',
                'related_courses' => '[283,279,299,281]',
                'category_id' => 5,
                'online' => 0,
                'created_at' => '2025-04-03 12:43:38',
                'updated_at' => '2025-04-03 12:43:38',
