            157 => 
            array (
                'id' => 360,
                'lang_code' => 'en',
                'name' => 'Improving Productivity through Quality Enhancement and Cost Reduction',
                'description' => '<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>Since improving productivity is vital in today&rsquo;s competitive world, a clear understanding of the term productivity is essential. Businesses have to operate in a highly competitive market place and whatever business you are in, it is imperative, especially in today&rsquo;s turmoil and economic situation, that a real focus is placed on methods to deliver superior quality through a process of enhanced productivity and at the same time reduce the costs by eliminating wasteful activities and failure.</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>There are so many &ldquo;theoretical&rdquo; ways or processes that could be implemented and indeed, have in many organizations. However, these do not always work and deliver the desired outcomes. &ldquo;Cost cutting&rdquo; is no longer the solution to sustainable profitability, the key to success is finding creative ways to prevent wasteful activities.</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>This course has been designed to examine the real issues and concentrate on areas that make a dynamic impact so that productivity can be improved, quality is enhanced and there is a constant philosophy of cost reduction through efficiency and diligence.</p>',
                'duration' => '5',
            'days_content' => '["<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<h6>Quality and Productivity and the Value Creation Process</h6>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Defining organisational vision and purpose</li>\\n\\t<li>Creating and measuring value for key stakeholders</li>\\n\\t<li>How quality and productivity drive value for customers and shareholders</li>\\n\\t<li>Business improvement through a focus on value creation and waste reduction</li>\\n\\t<li>They key components of a winning business model</li>\\n\\t<li>Choosing the right tools to manage performance &ndash; balanced scorecard and dashboards</li>\\n\\t<li>Using an effective performance management framework</li>\\n</ul>\\n","<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<h6>Principles of Effective Cost Management and Reduction</h6>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Defining and classifying business expenditure</li>\\n\\t<li>Understanding business cost behaviour</li>\\n\\t<li>Using cost-volume-profit analysis models</li>\\n\\t<li>Understanding gross margin and break-even</li>\\n\\t<li>An activity-based approach to understanding resource costs</li>\\n\\t<li>Effective profit improvement tactics</li>\\n\\t<li>Identifying areas of poor productivity and quality</li>\\n\\t<li>How quality and productivity problems affect profit and cash flow</li>\\n</ul>\\n","<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<h6>A Quality Based Approach to Waste and Cost Reduction</h6>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Lean &ndash; a focus on customer value and waste reduction</li>\\n\\t<li>Defining and identifying waste with value stream maps</li>\\n\\t<li>Understanding waste &ndash; &ldquo;Muda&rdquo; and the Eight Types of Waste</li>\\n\\t<li>Practical lessons from the Toyota Production System</li>\\n\\t<li>Using Six Sigma to eliminate quality variation</li>\\n\\t<li>Principles of Business Process Reengineering (BPR)</li>\\n\\t<li>Principles of Total Quality Management (TQM)</li>\\n</ul>\\n","<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<h6>Practical Business Improvement Methods</h6>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Waste reduction using the Toyota 5S approach</li>\\n\\t<li>Understanding the real DNA of Toyota&rsquo;s success</li>\\n\\t<li>Kaizen &ndash; a philosophy of continuous improvement and problem solving</li>\\n\\t<li>Choosing the right Key Performance Measures (KPM&rsquo;s)</li>\\n\\t<li>Practical problem-solving tools &ndash; Pareto analysis, Brainstorming and mind-mapping, Fishbone diagrams, and Using 5 Why&rsquo;s for root cause analysis</li>\\n</ul>\\n","<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<h6>Implementing Quality and Cost Reduction Initiatives</h6>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>A strategic approach to cost reduction</li>\\n\\t<li>Setting up a cost reduction programme</li>\\n\\t<li>Goals and questions around productivity</li>\\n\\t<li>Streamlining the organisation</li>\\n\\t<li>The psychology of resistance in humans</li>\\n\\t<li>8 steps to overcoming the barriers to change</li>\\n\\t<li>Personal action plan</li>\\n</ul>\\n"]',
                'related_courses' => '[348,342,361,432]',
                'category_id' => 8,
                'online' => 0,
                'created_at' => '2025-04-03 12:44:09',
                'updated_at' => '2025-04-03 12:44:09',
            ),
