ul>\\n\\t\\t<li>Recruitment Metrics</li>\\n\\t\\t<li>Retention Metrics</li>\\n\\t\\t<li>Compensation/Benefits Metrics</li>\\n\\t\\t<li>Training and Development Metrics</li>\\n\\t</ul>\\n\\t</li>\\n\\t<li>Reporting Methods and Examples: Charts and Graphs</li>\\n\\t<li>Workshop: Developing HR Reports Using Bar Charts, Pie Charts and Line Charts</li>\\n</ul>\\n","<h6><strong><strong><strong><strong><strong><strong>Employee Documentation and Record Keeping</strong></strong></strong></strong></strong></strong></h6>\\n\\n<h6>&nbsp;</h6>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Purpose and Objective of Record Keeping</li>\\n\\t<li>Employee Files: Legal Documents to Maintain</li>\\n\\t<li>Developing an Orientation Package: Documents to Provide to New Hires</li>\\n\\t<li>Policies, Procedures and Work Rules</li>\\n\\t<li>Developing an Organization&rsquo;s Employee Handbook\\n\\t<ul>\\n\\t\\t<li>Purpose of Handbook</li>\\n\\t\\t<li>Sections of the Handbook</li>\\n\\t\\t<li>Process of Developing Handbook</li>\\n\\t</ul>\\n\\t</li>\\n</ul>\\n"]',
