            378 => 
            array (
                'id' => 598,
                'lang_code' => 'en',
                'name' => 'Advanced Risk Assessment Techniques',
                'description' => '<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>Hazardous industries have a lot risks related to production and maintenance and companies/organizations have been aiming to understand the risk assessment techniques to reduce the possibility of accidents.</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>HAZOP (Hazard and Operability studies) are widely used in risk assessment techniques and the specifying the process of hazard analysis.</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>&nbsp;This course introduces the principles of Risk Assessments, Method Statements and Quality Plans.&nbsp;the course &nbsp;explains what a HAZOP is, when it should be used and the basic methodology used to conduct the risk assessment.&nbsp;</p>',
                'duration' => '5',
            'days_content' => '["<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<h6>Methodology of Risk Assessment</h6>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Concept of risk assessment and risk management</li>\\n\\t<li>Methods for assessment of risk</li>\\n\\t<li>3 types of risk assessment study- Qualitative , Semi-Quantitative and Quantitative</li>\\n\\t<li>Introduction to Cause- consequence analysis of risk</li>\\n</ul>\\n","<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<h6>HAZOP Techniques and Methodology</h6>\\n\\n<h6>&nbsp;</h6>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Importance and requirement of HAZOP study</li>\\n\\t<li>How to use HAZOP</li>\\n\\t<li>Requirements of Team leadership and hazard identification</li>\\n\\t<li>Case studies on HAZOP</li>\\n</ul>\\n","<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<h6>Cause-Consequence Analysis of Risk</h6>\\n\\n<h6>&nbsp;</h6>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Studies on fire , explosion and toxic gas releases and its drawbacks and prevention</li>\\n\\t<li>Effect of fire on people and environment</li>\\n\\t<li>Different types of explosion and its cause and prevention and its effects on people and environment</li>\\n\\t<li>Training on cause &ndash; consequence software</li>\\n</ul>\\n","<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<h6>Quantified Risk Assessment (QRA) and its Methodology</h6>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Methodology of &ldquo;QRA&rdquo;</li>\\n\\t<li>ETA(Event Tree Analysis) and its role and application in different industries for assessing the probability of the outcome</li>\\n\\t<li>FTA(Fault Tree Analysis) and its role and application in different industries for assessing the most severe conditons</li>\\n\\t<li>Difference between FTA and ETA</li>\\n\\t<li>Responsibilities of society and individual towards managing risk</li>\\n\\t<li>Training on QRA software</li>\\n</ul>\\n","<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<h6>Case Studies and Failure Analysis</h6>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Review of HAZOP case study, specifying the &ldquo;DO&rsquo;S&rdquo; and &ldquo;Don&rsquo;t&rdquo;</li>\\n\\t<li>Failure data analysis &ldquo; process of collecting and analysing data and cause of failure&rdquo;</li>\\n\\t<li>Methods for successful application of HAZOP case studies</li>\\n\\t<li>Case study and teaching on &ldquo;How to conduct a HAZOP meeting&rdquo;</li>\\n\\t<li>Review of the course and &ldquo;Question and Answer session&rdquo;</li>\\n</ul>\\n"]',
                'related_courses' => '[847,549,469,926]',
