                    472 => 
                    array (
                        'id' => 699,
                        'lang_code' => 'en',
                        'name' => 'Project Management Professional Bootcamp',
                        'description' => '<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>A project has a much higher chance of success if the strategy is clear and everyone involved knows the principles of running a project. All members of the team need clarity on their roles and what is needed from others to ensure plans are effective. This training will give you the skills to ensure you plan all of this.</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>Project Management Professional Bootcamp training &nbsp;course will lead you through the essentials of project management, why it is needed and what makes a project run well. The focus will be on techniques and actions needed to deliver high quality projects on time and budget.&nbsp;</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p><br />
Delegates will leave the day with a comprehensive overview of project management and practical skills and templates to help your organisation accomplish success.</p>',
                        'duration' => '5',
                        'days_content' => '["<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<h6><strong>&nbsp;</strong>Develop your Project Team and experience a Team Building Exercise</h6>\\n\\n<h6>&nbsp;</h6>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Comprehending the role of the project manager in business development.</li>\\n\\t<li>Recognise the behaviour of project stakeholders and how to manage them<strong>.</strong></li>\\n</ul>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<h6>&nbsp;Introducing the Project and introducing the Customer</h6>\\n\\n<h6>&nbsp;</h6>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Recognising your Customer and comprehending the different strategies in managing their expectation.</li>\\n\\t<li>Identifying and setting project team duties<strong>.</strong></li>\\n</ul>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n","<h6>Handling Multiple Projects</h6>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Characterising the keys to managing multiple projects and how to achieve this.</li>\\n\\t<li>How to identify and handle difficult personality kinds on multiple projects.</li>\\n\\t<li>How to handle and manage change when dealing with multiple project.</li>\\n\\t<li>Comprehending the steps in successfully delegating work on projects.</li>\\n</ul>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<h6>&nbsp;Prepare your project structure to reassure your customer on project delivery</h6>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Identifying the 10 critical elements of a good project management plan?</li>\\n\\t<li>Comprehending the difference between planning for small versus large complex projects?</li>\\n</ul>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n","<h6>Creating and Controlling the Project Plans</h6>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Comprehending the 11 factors that make a good schedule &hellip; what are they and how to manage them.</li>\\n\\t<li>Comprehending the common mistakes to avoid when making a project schedule.</li>\\n</ul>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<h6>Bootcamp Breakout 6: Create a schedule that your sponsor can understand.</h6>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>How to identify and manage risk in any projects.</li>\\n\\t<li>Comprehending when and where project contracts need to be used and how they should be managed.</li>\\n</ul>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<h6><strong>&nbsp;</strong>Present the risk back to your sponsor and understand financial implications.</h6>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Comprehend how to develop the project financial budget.</li>\\n\\t<li>Comprehend what critical project elements that constantly need monitoring.</li>\\n</ul>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n","<h6>&nbsp;Handling Change</h6>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Comprehend how to be active in managing change.</li>\\n\\t<li>Comprehend what to do if the project is behind schedule or over budget.</li>\\n\\t<li>What is the best way to manage a customer when change requires extra budget or time<strong>.</strong></li>\\n</ul>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<h6>Handle the Change</h6>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Comprehend the best way of interfacing with your stakeholders during meetings.</li>\\n</ul>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<h6>&nbsp;It is time to meet with the customer and tell them about the change.</h6>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Actions, Issues and Change &hellip; how to report on them.</li>\\n</ul>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n","<h6>&nbsp;Finishing the Project</h6>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Comprehend the best way to complete a project.</li>\\n\\t<li>Distinguish the best way of transitioning projects to the customer.</li>\\n\\t<li>Comprehend how to make the best use of lesson learnt.</li>\\n\\t<li>Comprehend how can to turn a complicated project into a big success.</li>\\n\\t<li>How well should the project manager know the customer and Comprehending why it is important.</li>\\n\\t<li>Comprehending strategies on how project managers can improve the relationship with their customers</li>\\n</ul>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n"]',
