culation of balanced fault levels and fault currents</li>\\n\\t<li>Introduction to symmetrical components</li>\\n</ul>\\n\\n<h4>&nbsp;</h4>\\n\\n<h6>Unbalanced Fault Calculations</h6>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Worked examples using symmetrical components</li>\\n</ul>\\n\\n<h4>&nbsp;</h4>\\n\\n<h6>Measuring Transformers</h6>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Why we need measuring transformers</li>\\n\\t<li>Principles and specifications CTs and VT</li>\\n</ul>\\n","<h6>Grading</h6>\\n\\n<h6>&nbsp;</h6>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Grading Exercises</li>\\n</ul>\\n\\n<h4>&nbsp;</h4>\\n\\n<h6>Electronic Relays</h6>\\n\\n<h6>Protection of Radial Networks</h6>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Principles of radial feeder protection</li>\\n\\t<li>Urban networks</li>\\n\\t<li>Overhead networks</li>\\n\\t<li>Distribution transformers</li>\\n</ul>\\n\\n<h4>&nbsp;</h4>\\n\\n<h6>Busbar protection</h6>\\n\\n<h6>Arc Suppression Coil Earthed System</h6>\\n","<h6>Transformer and Transformer-Feeder Protection</h6>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Transformer fault types and characteristics</li>\\n\\t<li>Protection applications to transformers and transformer feeders</li>\\n\\t<li>Differential protection</li>\\n</ul>\\n\\n<h4>&nbsp;</h4>\\n\\n<h6>Protection of Non-radial Networks</h6>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Directional overcurrent and earth fault protection</li>\\n\\t<li>Feeder unit protection and schemes</li>\\n\\t<li>Distance protection</li>\\n</ul>\\n\\n<h4>&nbsp;</h4>\\n\\n<h6>MV/LV systems with Generators</h6>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Operating requirements</li>\\n\\t<li>System and interface protection</li>\\n\\t<li>Generator protection</li>\\n</ul>\\n\\n<h4>&nbsp;</h4>\\n\\n<h6>Metropolitan systems</h6>\\n\\n<h6>Intertripping Techniques</h6>\\n"]',
