            44 => 
            array (
                'id' => 774,
                'lang_code' => 'en',
                'name' => 'Achieving CMMS Data Integrity',
            'description' => '<p>Many companies cannot adequately use their CMMS because its data is incorrect or outdated (very badly performed new data builds or straight upload of legacy data from old systems). The main reason for a lack of data integrity is a lack of standards and guides; the people involved do what they think is the right way, but everyone has different ideas).</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>Data and data management are at the heart of all HTM-oriented computerized maintenance management system (CMMS) software. After all, without accurate and complete data, a CMMS is not going to be of much use to the HTM department.</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>Achieving CMMS Data Integrity&nbsp;course shows the best practices in building the CMMS data during the pre-operational phase and how to carry out major clean ups of the equipment and spares data.</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>The course will help your team to adapt a structured approach to all aspects of new data builds to feel more in control for new builds or data transfer from legacy systems. Your team will learn skills and techniques to carry out critical reviews of the current CMMS Data to improve the data quality and integrity. The seminar will examine the latest ways to guide periodic quality checks.</p>',
                'duration' => '5',
                'days_content' => '["<h6>Methodology of CMMS Data Build</h6>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Understanding the problems related to data builds</li>\\n\\t<li>Structure of the CMMS data build</li>\\n\\t<li>Upgradation of CMMS model and reviews</li>\\n\\t<li>Working on MS Excel or MS Access</li>\\n\\t<li>Understanding the MS Access tables and reports</li>\\n</ul>\\n","<h6>Maintenance and Spares Coding</h6>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Understanding of the &ldquo;Equipment class&rdquo; and &ldquo;Failure class&rdquo;</li>\\n\\t<li>Understanding of the &ldquo;Shutdown and WO priority codes&rdquo;</li>\\n\\t<li>Developing the structure of the failure coding</li>\\n\\t<li>Training and exercises on Failure code structure</li>\\n</ul>\\n","<h6>Building Asset Register</h6>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Understanding the methodology of the build process</li>\\n\\t<li>Creating guides and standards for the program</li>\\n\\t<li>Understanding the conventions of name and number</li>\\n\\t<li>How to conduct quality checks and equipment attributes?</li>\\n\\t<li>Training on building equipment register</li>\\n</ul>\\n","<h6>Building Spares Database</h6>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Creation of guides and standards for the program</li>\\n\\t<li>Understanding the conventions of name and number</li>\\n\\t<li>How to conduct quality checks and equipment attributes?</li>\\n\\t<li>Training on building spares register</li>\\n</ul>\\n","<h6>Creation of the Product Management Data</h6>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Terminology of the program</li>\\n\\t<li>Concept of &ldquo;Maximo vs Sap&rdquo;</li>\\n\\t<li>Creation of generic strategy based on concepts of FMEA</li>\\n\\t<li>How to write effective tasks?</li>\\n\\t<li>Structure of the job plan</li>\\n\\t<li>How to link PMs to tags and quality checks and exercises</li>\\n\\t<li>Review of the course and &ldquo;Question and Answer session&rdquo;</li>\\n</ul>\\n"]',
                'related_courses' => '[472,528,784,781]',
