<h6>&nbsp;</h6>\\n\\n<h6>Presentation and Body Language</h6>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Relevance of Image</li>\\n\\t<li>Visual Language</li>\\n\\t<li>Body Language</li>\\n\\t<li>Significant Gestures</li>\\n\\t<li>Distracting Behaviour</li>\\n\\t<li>Colours</li>\\n\\t<li>On Set</li>\\n</ul>\\n","<h6>Creating a Showreel</h6>\\n\\n<h6>&nbsp;</h6>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Creating a Successful Showreel</li>\\n\\t<li>Resources</li>\\n\\t<li>Research Work</li>\\n\\t<li>Footage Type</li>\\n\\t<li>Branding</li>\\n\\t<li>Format and Structure</li>\\n</ul>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<h6>The Television Industry and Employment</h6>\\n\\n<h6>&nbsp;</h6>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Organisation</li>\\n\\t<li>Management of Personal Reputation</li>\\n\\t<li>Connectivity</li>\\n\\t<li>Contents Required for the Application</li>\\n\\t<li>Organisations</li>\\n</ul>\\n","<h6>Presenting as a Career</h6>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Requirements</li>\\n\\t<li>Agents</li>\\n\\t<li>Duties of an Agent</li>\\n\\t<li>Reasons for Hiring an Agent</li>\\n\\t<li>Reasons against Hiring an Agent</li>\\n\\t<li>Choosing a Good Agent</li>\\n</ul>\\n\\n<h6><br />\\nBuilding Confidence and Dealing with Rejection</h6>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Building Camera Confidence</li>\\n\\t<li>Things to Avoid and Things to Embrace</li>\\n\\t<li>Dealing with Rejection</li>\\n\\t<li>Secondary Opportunities</li>\\n\\t<li>Serendipity</li>\\n</ul>\\n"]',
