            233 => 
            array (
                'id' => 992,
                'lang_code' => 'en',
                'name' => 'Asset Protection and Security Management',
                'description' => '<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>The main aim of Asset protection and security management is to help make the business more successful. This can involve strategies that enhance confidence with shareholders, customers, and stakeholders, through to preventing damage to the business brand, actual losses, and business disruptions. Asset protection is a component of financial planning intended to protect one&#39;s assets from creditor claims.</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>Individuals and business entities use asset protection techniques to limit creditors&#39; access to certain valuable assets while operating within the bounds of debtor-creditor law. Asset protection is the basis for everything that a protection specialist does. It is the core function of the protection officer&rsquo;s job. Asset protection can have different meanings and functions depending on the approach to protecting the asset, its location, and even the type of asset. &nbsp;professionals involved in the protection of assets.</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>Asset Protection and Security Management trainin Course covers the fundamental aspects of security and security management providing a firm foundation for advanced development. For the experienced security practitioner, it provides the tools necessary for developing effective solutions and responses to the growing number of challenges encountered by today&#39;s security professionals.</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>',
                'duration' => '5',
                'days_content' => '["<h6>&nbsp;</h6>\\n\\n<h6>Roles, Responsibilities and Key Issues of Security Management</h6>\\n\\n<h6>&nbsp;</h6>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>\\n\\t<p>Introduction and a Review of International Standards&nbsp;</p>\\n\\t</li>\\n\\t<li>\\n\\t<p>Strategic and Operational Management, Roles &amp; Responsibilities</p>\\n\\t</li>\\n\\t<li>\\n\\t<p>Effective Security Management Styles</p>\\n\\t</li>\\n\\t<li>\\n\\t<p>Necessary understanding to identify, address and manage risk</p>\\n\\t</li>\\n\\t<li>\\n\\t<p>Crime Management and Prevention</p>\\n\\t</li>\\n\\t<li>\\n\\t<p>Manpower Management &ndash; 12 key principles</p>\\n\\t</li>\\n\\t<li>\\n\\t<p>Achieving organisational goals, targets and objectives</p>\\n\\t</li>\\n</ul>\\n","<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<h6>The Importance of Security Planning</h6>\\n\\n<h6>&nbsp;</h6>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>\\n\\t<p>Essential legislation, legal obligations, using minimum force</p>\\n\\t</li>\\n\\t<li>\\n\\t<p>Creating an organisational culture of Security</p>\\n\\t</li>\\n\\t<li>\\n\\t<p>Customer relations - Reputation of the Security Function</p>\\n\\t</li>\\n\\t<li>\\n\\t<p>Planning and Managing Security Projects</p>\\n\\t</li>\\n\\t<li>\\n\\t<p>Key Principles of Emergency Response Teams, the role of Security</p>\\n\\t</li>\\n\\t<li>\\n\\t<p>On-Scene Incident Management</p>\\n\\t</li>\\n</ul>\\n","<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<h6>Security Surveying - Threats to Assets</h6>\\n\\n<h6>&nbsp;</h6>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>\\n\\t<p>Understanding Loss</p>\\n\\t</li>\\n\\t<li>\\n\\t<p>Key Point Identification</p>\\n\\t</li>\\n\\t<li>\\n\\t<p>Access Control, Integrated Technologies and CCTV</p>\\n\\t</li>\\n\\t<li>\\n\\t<p>Security, Risk and Vulnerability Analysis</p>\\n\\t</li>\\n\\t<li>\\n\\t<p>When and how to conduct an effective Security Survey</p>\\n\\t</li>\\n\\t<li>\\n\\t<p>Intellectual Property, Data Protection and Cyber Security</p>\\n\\t</li>\\n\\t<li>\\n\\t<p>Security Survey Report, making Effective Recommendations</p>\\n\\t</li>\\n</ul>\\n","<h6>&nbsp;</h6>\\n\\n<h6>Principals of Asset Protection &ndash; Physical Security</h6>\\n\\n<h6>&nbsp;</h6>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>\\n\\t<p>Perimeter Security design principles</p>\\n\\t</li>\\n\\t<li>\\n\\t<p>Buildings Security design principles and Access Control</p>\\n\\t</li>\\n\\t<li>\\n\\t<p>Communication Strategies and Security Control Centres</p>\\n\\t</li>\\n\\t<li>\\n\\t<p>Managing Investigations &amp; Interviewing techniques</p>\\n\\t</li>\\n\\t<li>\\n\\t<p>Special Risks &ndash; Key issues of Terrorism</p>\\n\\t</li>\\n\\t<li>\\n\\t<p>Key Elements of Evacuation Planning</p>\\n\\t</li>\\n</ul>\\n","<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<h6>Security Operations Management</h6>\\n\\n<h6>&nbsp;</h6>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>\\n\\t<p>Managing Guarding Operations</p>\\n\\t</li>\\n\\t<li>\\n\\t<p>Crisis Management Plans, Procedures and Implementation</p>\\n\\t</li>\\n\\t<li>\\n\\t<p>Business Continuity Plans</p>\\n\\t</li>\\n\\t<li>\\n\\t<p>Mutual Aid &ndash; who else can or should be involved?</p>\\n\\t</li>\\n\\t<li>\\n\\t<p>Dealing with Social Media</p>\\n\\t</li>\\n\\t<li>\\n\\t<p>Personnel Security and protection of &ldquo;at risk&rdquo; individuals</p>\\n\\t</li>\\n</ul>\\n"]',
