            249 => 
            array (
                'id' => 1022,
                'lang_code' => 'en',
            'name' => 'Certified Information Security Manager (CISM) (Preparation Course)',
                'description' => '<p>The demand for skilled information security management professionals is on the rise. Certified Information Security Manager is a globally recognized standard established in 2002, which is one of the most highly sought after IT certifications.It can give you the knowledge and skills to provide effective security management and consulting services, as well as open doors for career progression.</p><p><br></p><p>Our intensive five-day training is based on the ISACA framework, which has five domain areas that relate to the role of a CISM. You will learn about each of these domains in detail, giving you the knowledge and skills to develop and manage a resilient information security program.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>This will give your management team the reassurance they need to feel confident in your organization’s information security. This course will prepare you with the knowledge and skills to complete the ISACA CISM exam, which will give you Certified Information Security Manager status.</p><p><br></p><p>This course is a preparation course, and designed to equip you with the necessary skills and knowledge to prepare for the certification, should you choose to pursue it in the future</p>',
                'duration' => '5',
                'days_content' => '["<p>&nbsp;</p><h6>Information security governance</h6><h6>&nbsp;</h6><ul><li>Learn how to establish and maintain a framework that aligns information security strategies with business objectives and applicable laws and regulations</li></ul>","<p><strong>Risk management</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li>Identify and manage information security risks to achieve business objectives</li></ul>","<p><strong>Information security program management</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li>Get the skills to design, develop and manage an information security program that implements the information security governance framework</li></ul>","<p><strong>Information security management</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li>Understand how you oversee and direct information security activities to execute the information security program</li></ul>","<p><strong>Response management</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li>Learn to develop and manage your capability to respond and recover from disruptive and destructive information security events</li></ul>"]',
                'related_courses' => '[823,825,827,843]',
                'category_id' => 15,
                'online' => 0,
                'created_at' => '2025-04-03 12:47:04',
                'updated_at' => '2025-04-03 12:47:04',
            ),
            250 => 
            array (
                'id' => 1023,
                'lang_code' => 'en',
            'name' => 'Certified Information Security Manager (CISM) (Preparation Course)',
                'description' => '<p>The demand for skilled information security management professionals is on the rise. Certified Information Security Manager is a globally recognized standard established in 2002, which is one of the most highly sought after IT certifications.It can give you the knowledge and skills to provide effective security management and consulting services, as well as open doors for career progression.</p><p><br></p><p>Our intensive five-day training is based on the ISACA framework, which has five domain areas that relate to the role of a CISM. You will learn about each of these domains in detail, giving you the knowledge and skills to develop and manage a resilient information security program.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>This will give your management team the reassurance they need to feel confident in your organization’s information security. This course will prepare you with the knowledge and skills to complete the ISACA CISM exam, which will give you Certified Information Security Manager status.</p><p><br></p><p>This course is a preparation course, and designed to equip you with the necessary skills and knowledge to prepare for the certification, should you choose to pursue it in the future</p>',
                'duration' => '5',
                'days_content' => '["<p><strong>Information security governance</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li>Learn how to establish and maintain a framework that aligns information security strategies with business objectives and applicable laws and regulations</li></ul>","<p><strong>Risk management</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li>Identify and manage information security risks to achieve business objectives</li></ul>","<p><strong>Information security program management</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li>Get the skills to design, develop and manage an information security program that implements the information security governance framework</li></ul>","<p><strong>Information security management</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li>Understand how you oversee and direct information security activities to execute the information security program</li></ul>","<p><strong>Response management</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li>Learn to develop and manage your capability to respond and recover from disruptive and destructive information security events</li></ul>"]',
                'related_courses' => '[824,826,828,844]',
                'category_id' => 15,
                'online' => 1,
                'created_at' => '2025-04-03 12:47:05',
                'updated_at' => '2025-04-03 12:47:05',
            ),
            251 => 
            array (
                'id' => 1024,
                'lang_code' => 'en',
                'name' => 'Agile Business Analysis Programme',
                'description' => '<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>The Agile Business Analysis defines improvements to business processes, assists decision-makers in gathering information to make decisions, helps quality assurance test solutions and products, designs user interfaces and even steps in as a product owner, scrum master, or project manager. The Agile way of working is becoming ever more popular in modern business. It&rsquo;s a smart way to work, and so it makes sense for you, the business analyst, to get to grips with how you can contribute to the success of Agile development projects.</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>Agile Business Analysis&nbsp;training course will help you do just that. Based on a true-to-life case study, you&rsquo;ll use your existing business analysis knowledge and techniques and practice applying the Agile approach within a business analysis scenario. You&rsquo;ll come away with a real understanding of how business analysis is applied within the context of the Agile philosophy. You&rsquo;ll not only explore the philosophy behind Agile, but the methods and techniques used within the business and the principles that guide this way of working. You&rsquo;ll also consider holistic and lean thinking, and how they can benefit your business.</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>The course provides participants with an understanding of the changing role of the business analyst, the tools and techniques best suited to Agile, and the timing for performing key tasks and events. Explanatory, demonstrations, and practice exercises will provide you with the experience needed to create user stories that meet business needs.</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>',
                'duration' => '5',
            'days_content' => '["<h6>&nbsp;</h6>\\n\\n<h6>Getting Started</h6>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Why Agile?</li>\\n\\t<li>Agile components (principles, methods &amp; techniques)</li>\\n\\t<li>Agile in the business context</li>\\n\\t<li>Lean Business Analysis Service, system and Lean thinking)</li>\\n</ul>\\n","<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<h6>Stakeholders and&nbsp; Building an Agile Team</h6>\\n\\n<h6>&nbsp;</h6>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Stakeholder groups</li>\\n\\t<li>Understanding the customer</li>\\n\\t<li>Agile BA role in stakeholder engagement and management</li>\\n\\t<li>The Team as a System</li>\\n\\t<li>The Business Analyst</li>\\n</ul>\\n","<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<h6>Agile Modelling</h6>\\n\\n<h6>&nbsp;</h6>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Purpose and principles behind Agile Modelling</li>\\n\\t<li>The hierarchy of models (business view to system component)</li>\\n\\t<li>Prioritisation using MoSCoW</li>\\n\\t<li>Agile Documentation</li>\\n\\t<li>Requirements Elaboration</li>\\n\\t<li>Decomposing and organizing business goals</li>\\n</ul>\\n","<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<h6>Agile Techniques</h6>\\n\\n<h6>&nbsp;</h6>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>User stories and roles</li>\\n\\t<li>The Product Backlog</li>\\n\\t<li>Writing User Stories</li>\\n\\t<li>Guidelines for Good Stories</li>\\n\\t<li>Acceptance Criteria</li>\\n\\t<li>Managing requirements with the solution backlog</li>\\n\\t<li>Estimating story points</li>\\n\\t<li>Managing the iterations (Planning, aligning, traceability, velocity)</li>\\n</ul>\\n","<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<h6>Agile BA Planning</h6>\\n\\n<h6>&nbsp;</h6>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>BA role in agile projects</li>\\n\\t<li>Storyboarding/scenarios/prototyping</li>\\n\\t<li>Creating a kanban board</li>\\n\\t<li>Scaling Agile</li>\\n\\t<li>Constraining factors</li>\\n\\t<li>The system of interest</li>\\n</ul>\\n"]',
                'related_courses' => '[946,1026,1038,1046]',
                'category_id' => 41,
                'online' => 0,
                'created_at' => '2025-04-03 12:47:05',
                'updated_at' => '2025-04-03 12:47:05',
            ),
