            319 => 
            array (
                'id' => 1102,
                'lang_code' => 'en',
                'name' => 'Artificial Intelligence in Finance and Open Banking',
            'description' => '<p>&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p> As Open Banking spreads across the globe, the unleashing of data will open up new market opportunities for both incumbents and startups, with the potential to radically transform the industry, creating new winners, losers, rewards and challenges.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Big data powered by artificial intelligence (AI) is dramatically reshaping the global financial services industry.&nbsp;Open Banking promises to transform it even further, as vast financial data sets are decoupled from incumbent&nbsp;institutions.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>AI in Finance and Open Banking training course will first take the participants through the basics of AI, and then explore the many opportunities it provides in the data-intensive industry of finance while flagging the pitfalls they may face in adoption.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>&nbsp;</p>',
                'duration' => '5',
            'days_content' => '["<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Introduction to AI and Data Basics&nbsp;</strong></p><h6><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">&nbsp;</span></h6><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Introduction to AI and ML concepts and features&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Recognizing the role of data science in AI and the usage of big data in model training&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Analyzing the complementation between AI and human intelligence and its role in solving business problems&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Discovering many applications of AI in finance&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Discussing ethical challenges and concerns of AI </span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Open Banking and Data Revolution&nbsp;</strong></p><h6><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">&nbsp;</span></h6><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Definition of Open Banking and its Impact on Consumers and Businesses</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Understanding regulatory frameworks and compliance requirements surrounding Open Banking&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Exploring types of Application Programming Interfaces (APIs) used in open banking&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Exploring the way open banking encourages innovation and competition among financial institutions&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Discussing data privacy and security considerations in open banking&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Analyzing opportunities and challenges associated with open banking</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">AI Applications in Financial Services&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Steps of developing an AI strategy for financial institution&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Exploring how to leverage AI in customer service:</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Chatbots&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Robo-advisors&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Personalized banking&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Discovering the application of AI for algorithm trading and portfolio management&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Understanding the way of using AI for fraud detection and prevention&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Exploring AI-driven risk assessment and management tools&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Discussing challenges in implementing AI in financial services </span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">AI-Driven Opportunities for Open Banking</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Discussing the advantages and opportunities AI provides for incumbent banks and new fintech entrants</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Discovering innovative applications of AI in Open banking:</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Blockchain&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Cryptocurrency&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Analyzing the integration of AI with open banking platforms for better analytics and insights&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Understanding the disruption in finance sector using data by key market players e.g. Amazon, Google, Apple, etc.</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Determining the role of regulations and Open Banking in limiting platform influence&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Discussing best practices and actions to face disruption by platforms </span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Ethical Considerations and Future Trends&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Discussing ethical considerations and legal challenges of using AI in finance and open banking&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Methods to avoid discrimination and privacy issues in data usage&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Discussing the level of consumer trust in the adoption of AI and open banking&nbsp; technologies</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Analyzing the impact of future trends on the finance industry&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">The final presentation of AI strategy in finance and open banking&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Summary, lesson learned and best practices </span></li></ul>"]',
                'related_courses' => '[1006,631,1088]',
                'category_id' => 34,
                'online' => 0,
                'created_at' => '2025-04-03 12:47:33',
                'updated_at' => '2025-04-03 12:47:33',
            ),
            320 => 
            array (
                'id' => 1104,
                'lang_code' => 'en',
                'name' => 'Key Account Management',
                'description' => '<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>Key Account Management (KAM) is systematic process of engaging and managing specific group of existing customers. It assists to define, understand and achieve a set of goals which mutually benefits organization and customers. The KAM process helps in engaging customers and nullify competition with respect to the customer account, where the ultimate goal is maximizing the revenue.</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>KAM is actually an approach to develop long term relationship with strategic important customers to optimize value and achieve mutually beneficial goals. These customers account for a significant volume of business and profit and hence require attention, effort, time and resources to grow and retain.</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>Key Account Management training course training&nbsp; will explore best practices and help delegates highlight where their skills and practices must be developed. In this Key Account Management course you will develop essential key account management skills, learning how to effectively manage your most valuable existing accounts, leading to improved customer satisfaction and increased customer loyalty.</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>The course shows participants how to build long-term, value-based relationships with large accounts, penetrate them for additional business, and maximize the revenue they generate while reducing the time and costs of managing them. The course also provides a strong focus on quantitative approaches to account qualification and account planning best practices.</p>',
                'duration' => '5',
            'days_content' => '["<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<h6>What is Key Account Management (KAM)?</h6>\\n\\n<h6>&nbsp;</h6>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>\\n\\t<p>Explaining Key Account Strategy</p>\\n\\t</li>\\n\\t<li>\\n\\t<p>Developing a Key Account Management (KAM) Strategy</p>\\n\\t</li>\\n\\t<li>\\n\\t<p>Why do it?</p>\\n\\t</li>\\n\\t<li>\\n\\t<p>What is involved?</p>\\n\\t</li>\\n\\t<li>\\n\\t<p>Who is involved?</p>\\n\\t</li>\\n\\t<li>\\n\\t<p>How do we execute a Key Account Management (KAM) strategy?</p>\\n\\t</li>\\n\\t<li>\\n\\t<p>Pitfalls and Traps to Avoid</p>\\n\\t</li>\\n</ul>\\n","<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<h6>Account analysis: defining and selecting KA</h6>\\n\\n<h6>&nbsp;</h6>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>\\n\\t<p>KAM: best-practice actions</p>\\n\\t</li>\\n\\t<li>\\n\\t<p>Account analysis insights</p>\\n\\t</li>\\n\\t<li>\\n\\t<p>Account analysis methods</p>\\n\\n\\t<ul>\\n\\t\\t<li>\\n\\t\\t<p>The single factor models</p>\\n\\t\\t</li>\\n\\t\\t<li>\\n\\t\\t<p>The portfolio models</p>\\n\\t\\t</li>\\n\\t\\t<li>\\n\\t\\t<p>The decision models</p>\\n\\t\\t</li>\\n\\t</ul>\\n\\t</li>\\n\\t<li>\\n\\t<p>Important &#39;KPIs&#39; for KA qualification</p>\\n\\n\\t<ul>\\n\\t\\t<li>\\n\\t\\t<p>Computing the cost per call</p>\\n\\t\\t</li>\\n\\t\\t<li>\\n\\t\\t<p>Break-even sales volume</p>\\n\\t\\t</li>\\n\\t\\t<li>\\n\\t\\t<p>Result based simulation</p>\\n\\t\\t</li>\\n\\t</ul>\\n\\t</li>\\n</ul>\\n","<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<h6>Understanding our Key Accounts, How they work and what they&nbsp;really&nbsp;want&nbsp;</h6>\\n\\n<h6>&nbsp;</h6>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>\\n\\t<p>Account Segmentation</p>\\n\\t</li>\\n\\t<li>\\n\\t<p>Understanding the Customer&rsquo;s Decision-making Process</p>\\n\\t</li>\\n\\t<li>\\n\\t<p>Understand What Drives the Customer</p>\\n\\t</li>\\n\\t<li>\\n\\t<p>How to Build Compelling Value Propositions for Each Type</p>\\n\\t</li>\\n\\t<li>\\n\\t<p>Understanding the Customer&rsquo;s Internal Politics and How to Harness Them</p>\\n\\t</li>\\n\\t<li>\\n\\t<p>Understanding the Macro-environment and How It Affects Each Customer</p>\\n\\t</li>\\n\\t<li>\\n\\t<p>How to Be Persuasive</p>\\n\\t</li>\\n\\t<li>\\n\\t<p>How to Develop Compelling Customer Propositions</p>\\n\\t</li>\\n</ul>\\n","<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<h6>Leading a Key Account Management (KAM) Team and Leading Ourselves&nbsp;</h6>\\n\\n<h6>&nbsp;</h6>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>\\n\\t<p>The Competencies and Characteristics of Great Key Account Managers</p>\\n\\t</li>\\n\\t<li>\\n\\t<p>The Skills Required to Manage Key and Global Accounts</p>\\n\\t</li>\\n\\t<li>\\n\\t<p>Recruiting Great Key Account Managers</p>\\n\\t</li>\\n\\t<li>\\n\\t<p>Personality Types of Great Key Account Managers</p>\\n\\t</li>\\n\\t<li>\\n\\t<p>Coaching and Mentoring Key Account Managers</p>\\n\\t</li>\\n\\t<li>\\n\\t<p>Communication and Persuasion Skills for Key Accounts</p>\\n\\t</li>\\n\\t<li>\\n\\t<p>Consultative Selling Skills</p>\\n\\t</li>\\n</ul>\\n","<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<h6>Implementing Your Key Account Management (KAM) Strategy&nbsp;</h6>\\n\\n<h6>&nbsp;</h6>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>\\n\\t<p>Building Trust</p>\\n\\t</li>\\n\\t<li>\\n\\t<p>Using Social Media in Each Segment</p>\\n\\t</li>\\n\\t<li>\\n\\t<p>Resourcing for Key Account Management (KAM)</p>\\n\\t</li>\\n\\t<li>\\n\\t<p>Account Objective Setting</p>\\n\\t</li>\\n\\t<li>\\n\\t<p>Putting Your Key Account Management (KAM) Plan Together</p>\\n\\t</li>\\n</ul>\\n"]',
                'related_courses' => '[883,444]',
                'category_id' => 10,
                'online' => 0,
                'created_at' => '2025-04-03 12:47:34',
                'updated_at' => '2025-04-03 12:47:34',
