            445 => 
            array (
                'id' => 1238,
                'lang_code' => 'en',
                'name' => 'Private Equity: Financing, Investing, and Value Creation',
                'description' => '<p>Private equity offers several advantages to companies and startups. It is favored by companies because it allows them access to liquidity as an alternative to conventional financial mechanisms, such as high-interest bank loans or listing on public markets. Certain forms of private equity, such as venture capital, also finance ideas and early-stage companies</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>Private Equity&nbsp;Training course, examines the role of private equity as a financing tool and as an investment opportunity. It explores the critical issues that the parties involved in a transaction&mdash;investors, lending banks, managers, entrepreneurs/shareholders, and advisors&mdash;will face during the investment process and negotiations.</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>Throughout the 10 Days program, you&rsquo;ll explore the types and economics of private equity and topics such as raising equity and debt, growth capital, leveraged buyouts, and distress. You&rsquo;ll also learn how to set up private equity firms and funds and discover career opportunities available in the industry.</p>',
                'duration' => '10',
                'days_content' => '["<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<h6>Types and Economics of Private Equity</h6>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Identify different private equity financing opportunities.</li>\\n</ul>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Determine the drivers of value creation in growth capital, development capital, leveraged buyouts, and distressed situations.</li>\\n</ul>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Describe other segments of financing and investment related to private equity.</li>\\n</ul>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Analyse the factors to take a private company public.</li>\\n</ul>\\n","<h3>&nbsp;</h3>\\n\\n<h6>Introduction to the Private Equity Industry</h6>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Examine the history of private equity.</li>\\n\\t<li>Explain the definition variations of private equity.</li>\\n\\t<li>Analyse the types of companies and their motivation for investing in private equity.</li>\\n\\t<li>Describe the various stages of private equity investing.</li>\\n</ul>\\n","<h3>&nbsp;</h3>\\n\\n<h6>Opportunity and Risks for Investors</h6>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Examine performance measurement of private equity funds.</li>\\n</ul>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Determine what makes different private equity asset classes attractive to investors.</li>\\n</ul>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Analyse the performance and sustainability of private equity funds.</li>\\n</ul>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Determine the impact of diversification on the asset.</li>\\n</ul>\\n","<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<h6>Private Equity Financing and Investment Process</h6>\\n\\n<h6>&nbsp;</h6>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Determine the different stages for setting up and managing a fund.</li>\\n\\t<li>Describe the investment process, including business plan development and fundraising.</li>\\n\\t<li>Examine the potential issues and focus of conducting due diligence.</li>\\n</ul>\\n","<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<h6>LBO Analysis and Valuation</h6>\\n\\n<h6>&nbsp;</h6>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Examine the principles of financial modeling.</li>\\n\\t<li>Demonstrate the steps of LBO analysis.</li>\\n\\t<li>Utilise the available valuation techniques.</li>\\n\\t<li>Discuss the process of negotiations.</li>\\n</ul>\\n","<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<h6>After the Deal</h6>\\n\\n<h6>&nbsp;</h6>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Demonstrate valuing an LBO.</li>\\n\\t<li>Examine managing an exit or alternative exit.</li>\\n</ul>\\n","<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<h6>Private Equity Through the Credit Crisis and Industry Evolution</h6>\\n\\n<h6>&nbsp;</h6>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Examine the impact of the credit crisis on the private equity industry.</li>\\n\\t<li>Analyse how private equity investors manage investments.</li>\\n\\t<li>Determine the ethical considerations in private equity investing.</li>\\n</ul>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n","<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<h6>Future of Private Equity</h6>\\n\\n<h6>&nbsp;</h6>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Examine the impact of recent trends on fundraising, investments, and performance.</li>\\n</ul>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Identify the structural differences between investments.</li>\\n</ul>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Determine, monitor and manage the developments in investing.</li>\\n</ul>\\n","<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<h6>Private Equity in Developing Markets</h6>\\n\\n<h6>&nbsp;</h6>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Describe the developments of private equity in emerging markets.</li>\\n\\t<li>Discuss the roles in private equity industry.</li>\\n</ul>\\n","<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<h3>&nbsp;</h3>\\n\\n<h6>Fund Organisation and Career Opportunities</h6>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Perform calculations for performance distribution.</li>\\n</ul>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Explain the differences between private equity firms and private equity funds.</li>\\n</ul>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Identify the careers in the private equity industry.</li>\\n</ul>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n"]',
                'related_courses' => '[]',
                'category_id' => 34,
                'online' => 1,
                'created_at' => '2025-04-03 12:48:01',
                'updated_at' => '2025-04-03 12:48:01',
