                'id' => 1333,
                'lang_code' => 'en',
                'name' => 'LPC - Advanced Excel Training',
                'description' => '<p>Learn everything you need to master MS office &ndash; Excel, the world&#39;s most popular spreadsheet program. This course provides you with a comprehensive overview of Excel, including manipulating workbook and cell data, using functions, printing worksheets, and collaborating with others. In the last half of the course, the course covers more complex techniques, such as summarising data with charts, working with external data, adding images and shapes, and automating routine tasks.</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>Learn everything you need to master MS office &ndash; Excel, the world&#39;s most popular spreadsheet program. This course provides you with a comprehensive overview of Excel, including manipulating workbook and cell data, using functions, printing worksheets, and collaborating with others. In the last half of the course,</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>&nbsp;The course covers more complex techniques, such as summarising data with charts, working with external data, adding images and shapes, and automating routine tasks.</p>',
                'duration' => '5',
                'days_content' => '["<h6>Creating and modifying workbook templates</h6>\\n\\n<h6>&nbsp;</h6>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Working with worksheets, cells and cell data</li>\\n\\t<li>Sorting, filtering, and managing worksheets</li>\\n\\t<li>Summarising data using formulas and functions</li>\\n\\t<li>Working with advanced formulas and functions</li>\\n\\t<li>Using validation rules to restrict the data entered in cells</li>\\n\\t<li>Creating named ranges</li>\\n</ul>\\n","<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<h6>Analysing data and formulas</h6>\\n\\n<h6>&nbsp;</h6>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Formatting worksheet elements</li>\\n\\t<li>Introduction to arithmetic operators</li>\\n\\t<li>Using relative and absolute cell references</li>\\n\\t<li>Finding data using Vlookup and Hlookup</li>\\n\\t<li>Auditing formulas by identifying precedents and dependants</li>\\n\\t<li>Managing Excel formula error indicator</li>\\n</ul>\\n","<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<h6>Creating rule-based conditional formats</h6>\\n\\n<h6>&nbsp;</h6>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Defining data bar, colour scale and icon set conditional format</li>\\n\\t<li>Working with charts</li>\\n\\t<li>Creating bar, column, pie, line and XY charts</li>\\n\\t<li>Creating stock charts</li>\\n\\t<li>Adding trendline to a chart</li>\\n\\t<li>Creating sparkline charts</li>\\n</ul>\\n","<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<h6>Working with external data</h6>\\n\\n<h6>&nbsp;</h6>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Importing data from CSV and txt files</li>\\n\\t<li>Using hyperlinks</li>\\n\\t<li>Linking an excel chart to another MS Office programme</li>\\n\\t<li>Working with objects</li>\\n\\t<li>Creating and formatting shapes</li>\\n\\t<li>Managing objects using the Selection pane</li>\\n</ul>\\n","<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<h6>Introduction to Pivot tables</h6>\\n\\n<h6>&nbsp;</h6>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Pivoting a pivot table report</li>\\n\\t<li>Managing subtotals and grand totals</li>\\n\\t<li>Setting AutoCorrect and automatic replace options</li>\\n\\t<li>Protecting a workbook</li>\\n\\t<li>Automating workbooks using Macros</li>\\n\\t<li>Recording a macro</li>\\n</ul>\\n"]',
                'related_courses' => '[1329,599,1198]',
