w Roman\',serif; mso-ascii-theme-font: major-bidi; mso-hansi-theme-font: major-bidi; mso-bidi-theme-font: major-bidi; mso-font-kerning: 0pt; mso-ansi-language: EN-US;\\">The PR Transfer Process and the Six Point PR Plan</span></li>\\n<li class=\\"MsoNormal\\" style=\\"text-indent: 0in;\\"><span style=\\"font-family: \'Times New Roman\',serif; mso-ascii-theme-font: major-bidi; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-fareast-theme-font: major-bidi; mso-hansi-theme-font: major-bidi; mso-bidi-theme-font: major-bidi; mso-font-kerning: 0pt; mso-ansi-language: EN-US;\\"><span><span style=\\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\\">&nbsp;</span></span></span><span style=\\"font-family: \'Times New Roman\',serif; mso-ascii-theme-font: major-bidi; mso-hansi-theme-font: major-bidi; mso-bidi-theme-font: major-bidi; mso-font-kerning: 0pt; mso-ansi-language: EN-US;\\">The Role of Events in a Public Relations and Marketing Strategy</span></li>\\n</ul>","<ul>\\n<li class=\\"MsoNormal\\" style=\\"text-indent: 0in;\\">Working with VIPs</li>\\n<li>Hosting and Farewell</li>\\n<li>Follow-up</li>\\n<li>Post-event analysis</li>\\n<li>Lasting impression</li>\\n<li>WOW factor techniques</li>\\n<li>Checklists</li>\\n</ul>"]',
