            106 => 
            array (
                'id' => 1420,
                'lang_code' => 'en',
            'name' => 'Landscape Architect Registration Examination (LARE)',
                'description' => '<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>The Landscape Architect Registration Examination (LARE) is the national licensing examination that measures knowledge, skills, and abilities as they relate to the profession of landscape architecture; it is a product of the Council of Landscape Architectural Registration Boards (CLARB) and formally adopted by California as its licensure examination. It consists of four multiple-choice sections.</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>The Landscape Architect course shall provide the licensure with sufficient knowledge, skills and abilities to provide landscape architectural services without endangering the health, safety and welfare of the public. With all current standards for fairness and quality of licensure exams.</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>This course of Landscape architects registration examination will provide the combination of experience and education in landscape architecture thus using the principles of ecology, hydrology, horticulture, geology, and design technology to create a green space that allows for sustainable urban living.</p>',
                'duration' => '5',
            'days_content' => '["<h6><strong>Project and Construction Management</strong></h6>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Select Project Team &bull; Develop Contract &bull; Negotiate Contract &bull; Prepare RFPs or RFQs &bull; Determine Project Scope, Schedule, and Budget</li>\\n\\t<li>Execute Records Retention Policy &bull; Facilitate Client Review and Coordination &bull; Obtain Permits &bull; Prepare Cost Estimates &bull; Prepare Project Deliverables</li>\\n\\t<li>Develop Bidding Criteria &bull; Prepare and Issue Addenda &bull; Facilitate Meetings &bull; Evaluate Bids and Make Recommendations &bull; Identify Delivery Methods &bull; Evaluate Contractor Qualifications &bull; Assist with Construction Contract Execution and Administration</li>\\n\\t<li>Respond to RFIs &bull; Coordinate with Contractors &bull; Facilitate Pre-Construction Meeting &bull; Document Pre-Construction Existing Conditions Attend Final Completion Walkthrough &bull; Prepare As-Built (record) Drawings &bull; Conduct Warranty Review &bull; Conduct Project Close-out &bull; Collect and Analyze Performance Metrics</li>\\n\\t<li>Review Maintenance Services &bull; Prepare Management Plan</li>\\n</ul>\\n","<h6><strong>Inventory and Analysis</strong></h6>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Determine Applicable Codes, Regulations, and Permitting Requirements &bull; Collect Contextual Data &bull; Gather Stakeholder Input &bull; Identify Policy Objectives &bull; Conduct Project Related Research</li>\\n\\t<li>Determine Appropriate Types of Analyses &bull; Perform Circulation Analysis &bull; Interpret Utility Analysis &bull; Perform Visual Resource Analysis &bull; Perform Micro and Macro Climate Analysis &bull; Perform Hydrological Analysis &bull; Perform Vegetation Analysis &bull; Interpret Ecological Analysis &bull; Perform Topographical Analysis &bull; Interpret Soil and Geotechnical/Geological Analysis &bull; Interpret Environmental Studies</li>\\n\\t<li>Analyze Codes, Regulations, and Permitting Requirements for Design Impact &bull; Interpret Cultural, Historical, and Archeological Analysis &bull; Interpret Social Analysis &bull; Interpret Economic Analysis &bull; Analyze Contextual Data &bull; Analyze Stakeholder Feedback</li>\\n</ul>\\n","<h6><strong>Design</strong></h6>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Design and Execute Public Participation Process &bull; Prioritize Stakeholder Goals &bull; Initiate Communication Strategy &nbsp;</li>\\n\\t<li>Perform Site Analysis and Determine Opportunities and Constraints &bull; Develop Vision or Framework Plan &bull; Develop and Conduct Urban Plan &bull; Develop Land Use Plan &bull; Develop Strategic Implementation Plan &bull; Develop Site Master Plan &bull; Develop Historic/Cultural Restoration and Preservation Plan</li>\\n\\t<li>Synthesize and Apply the Site Analysis &bull; Develop and Refine the Program &bull; Create the Basis for the Design &bull; Create Conceptual Design Alternatives and Scenarios &bull; Evaluate Design Alternatives &bull; Refine and Synthesize Concept Alternative &bull; Develop Schematic Design</li>\\n</ul>\\n","<h6><strong>Grading and Drainage&nbsp; </strong></h6>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Develop Demolition Plan &bull; Develop Existing Conditions Plan &bull; Prepare Soil Boring Location Plan &bull; Develop Stormwater Pollution Prevention Plan &bull; Develop Site Protection Plan &bull; Develop Mitigation Plan</li>\\n\\t<li>Develop Layout Plan &bull; Develop General Notes &bull; Develop Grading and Drainage Plan &bull; Develop Planting Practices, Plans, Notes and Schedules &bull; Develop Materials Plan</li>\\n\\t<li>Develop Phasing Plan &bull; Develop Irrigation Plan &bull; Prepare Lighting Plan &bull; Develop Site Furnishings Plan</li>\\n</ul>\\n","<h6><strong>Construction Documentation</strong></h6>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Develop Signage and Wayfinding Plan &bull; Develop Traffic Control Plan &bull; Develop Emergency Access Plan &bull; Prepare Stormwater Management Plan</li>\\n\\t<li>Develop Technical Specifications &bull; Prepare Bid Form/Schedule &bull; Develop Project Manual/Front End Specifications</li>\\n\\t<li>CASE STUDIES | STRUCTURAL RESOURCES</li>\\n</ul>\\n"]',
                'related_courses' => '[]',
                'category_id' => 16,
                'online' => 0,
                'created_at' => '2025-04-03 12:49:04',
                'updated_at' => '2025-04-03 12:49:04',
            ),
