            'description' => '<p>The Landscape Architect Registration Examination (LARE) is the national licensing examination that measures knowledge, skills, and abilities as they relate to the profession of landscape architecture; it is a product of the Council of Landscape Architectural Registration Boards (CLARB) and formally adopted by California as its licensure examination. It consists of four multiple-choice sections.</p>

