<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>Professional collection specialist course will help you do just that identifying accounts with overdue payments and keeping records of the amount owed and the length of the delinquency, locating debtors and contacting them via phone or mail to address their overdue payments and determine the reason for the outstanding debt and lastly will teach you how to communicate with the sales department to maintain accurate and updated information on client accounts and payments</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>After completing this course on Professional collection specialist (PCS) , the participant shall be able to learn to contacting customers to inform on delinquency, encourage on-time payments and set up payment plans that can facilitate good credit, processing customer payments, account adjustments and customer refunds where appropriate and reviewing records for accuracy and handling disputes to make sure that account information is entered and maintained appropriately</p>',
                'duration' => '5',
            'days_content' => '["<h6><strong>FDCPA Essentials for the ARM Industry</strong></h6>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>FDCPA Essentials</li>\\n\\t<li>Understanding the consumer&rsquo;s rights</li>\\n\\t<li>Responsibilities under the FDCPA as a professional debt collector</li>\\n</ul>\\n","<h6><strong>FDCPA Essentials for the ARM Industry-2</strong></h6>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>The Fair Debt Collection Practices Act</li>\\n\\t<li>Identify restrictions on the method and timing of collection communications.</li>\\n\\t<li>Explain the purpose of the FDCPA and its implementing Regulation F.</li>\\n\\t<li>Identify the conditions and restrictions on the timing and method of collection communications with consumers.</li>\\n</ul>\\n","<h6><strong>Right Party Contact (&ldquo;RPC&rdquo;)</strong></h6>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Determine a Right Party Contact (&ldquo;RPC&rdquo;) with whom you may discuss the debt</li>\\n\\t<li>Limited Content Message (&ldquo;LCM&rdquo;)</li>\\n\\t<li>Mini-Miranda Disclosure</li>\\n\\t<li>Recognize and respond to consumer communication preferences, disputes, and attorney involvement</li>\\n\\t<li>Name the two federal agencies that enforce the FDCPA and explain the consequences of violations</li>\\n</ul>\\n","<h6><strong>Essential Collection Skills and Techniques</strong></h6>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Human Communication is our Business</li>\\n\\t<li>Build Rapport; Conquer Interference</li>\\n\\t<li>Ready, Set, Goal! Steps to Success</li>\\n</ul>\\n","<h6><strong>Essential Collection Skills and Techniques-2</strong></h6>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Verify the Consumer</li>\\n\\t<li>Identify Yourself</li>\\n\\t<li>Request Payment in Full</li>\\n\\t<li>Pause</li>\\n\\t<li>Ask About and Listen for Challenges</li>\\n\\t<li>Negotiate Solutions</li>\\n\\t<li>Confirm Arrangements</li>\\n\\t<li>Close the Call</li>\\n\\t<li>Previous Exam Questions | CASE STUDIES</li>\\n</ul>\\n"]',
                'related_courses' => '[]',
                'category_id' => 8,
                'online' => 1,
                'created_at' => '2025-04-03 12:49:08',
                'updated_at' => '2025-04-03 12:49:08',
            ),
            122 => 
            array (
                'id' => 1436,
                'lang_code' => 'en',
            'name' => 'Certified Special Events Professional (CSEP) (Preparation Course)',
            'description' => '<p>The Certified Special Events Professional (CSEP) designation was established in 1993 to recognize event professionals who have successfully demonstrated the knowledge, skills and ability essential to perform all components of a special event</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Obtaining the Certified Special Events Professional (CSEP) means clients will have more trust in your business and skills. The Certified Special Events Professional (CSEP) course shall provide you with a stamp of approval for marketing or soliciting new business and conveying instant credibility to clients.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>With CSEP course, one shall gain advance, market-relevant events industry expertise that demonstrates a career-long commitment to personal and professional development. Being able to put the letters CSEP after your name is verification of knowledge, expertise and excellence. Thus contributing to the industry’s overall knowledge base, removing performance uncertainty from your clients’ minds and qualifying for higher level opportunities.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>In this course the participants shall have an understanding to increase the proficiency of event professionals, to elevate industry standards and practices, to establish the level of knowledge and performance necessary for certification, to promote the advancement of the special events industry, to advance the careers of practitioners, to acknowledge the high calibre work of CSEPs and the value of the products and services they provide</p><p><br></p><p>This course is a preparation course, and designed to equip you with the necessary skills and knowledge to prepare for the certification, should you choose to pursue it in the future</p>',
                'duration' => '5',
            'days_content' => '["<h6><strong>Development of the The Project</strong></h6><p>&nbsp;</p><ul><li>Define goals and objectives.</li><li>Establish a budget.</li><li>Build your team.</li><li>Pick your venue and date.</li><li>Develop event branding.</li><li>Plan your program.</li><li>Confirm sponsors, exhibitors, and speakers.</li><li>Identify and select tech tools.</li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: black;\\">Management of Risk, Finance and Human Resources </strong></p><p><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">&nbsp;</span></p><ul><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Exploring risk identification and assessment techniques and tools </span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Discussing strategies for effective management of contracts </span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Strategies to manage event funding and financial resources </span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Understanding the process of developing a budget for a meeting/ event</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Discovering the way of establishing and managing monetary transaction procedures </span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Exploring techniques for assessing staffing needs and determining selection criteria&nbsp;</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: black;\\">Meeting or Event Design</strong></p><p>&nbsp;</p><ul><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Discovering the steps of developing a program: From theme development to outcome measurement </span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Understanding how to select and engage speakers and performers </span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Discussing guidance and strategies for selecting and coordinating food and beverage </span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Identifying criteria for selecting design requirements and decorations </span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Recognizing the importance of managing and oversing audiovisual and technical requirements </span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Discussing how to plan for managing attendees’ movements and controlling protocols&nbsp;</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: black;\\">Site Management </strong></p><p><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">&nbsp;</span></p><ul><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Discussing criteria for selecting meeting/ event site </span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Tools and techniques for developing site maps and floorplans </span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Steps of creating a logistics plan to manage meeting/ event site </span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Determining the importance of implementing the logistics plan during site set-up, operation, and takedown </span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Best practices for managing on-site communication </span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Discussing how to set communication procedures and protocols for each audience&nbsp;</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: black;\\">Marketing</strong></p><p>&nbsp;</p><ul><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Understanding the process of developing a marking plan </span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Exploring strategies for creating and managing marketing materials, including content and designs </span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Identifying the importance of aligning product design and specification with the marketing plan </span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Discovering different types of promotional activities to expand market reach </span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Discussing the role of public relations activities in promoting and succeeding meetings/ events </span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Best practices for managing meeting-related sales activities </span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Do and don’t for CMP exam&nbsp;</span></li></ul>"]',
                'related_courses' => '[703,1342,1458]',
                'category_id' => 49,
                'online' => 0,
                'created_at' => '2025-04-03 12:49:08',
                'updated_at' => '2025-04-03 12:49:08',
