            298 => 
            array (
                'id' => 1635,
                'lang_code' => 'en',
                'name' => 'Site Supervision and Management',
                'description' => '<p>The construction industry is constantly evolving, and effective site management and supervision are critical components of a successful construction project. As a site supervisor or construction manager, your role is pivotal in ensuring that projects are delivered on time, within budget, and to the required quality standards.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>This course has been designed to equip you with the knowledge and practical skills necessary to effectively manage and supervise construction projects on site. Over five days, we will cover a range of topics from site planning and preparation to health and safety management, project quality, and productivity management, and site handover and closeout.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>You will learn about the key responsibilities of a site supervisor, the common challenges faced, and the relevant laws and regulations that apply. Through interactive case studies and practical exercises, you will have the opportunity to apply what you have learned to real-world situations. Guest speakers with extensive experience in site management and supervision will also share their expertise and provide valuable insights.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>By the end of the course, you will have a solid understanding of the essential components of site management and be equipped with the tools and knowledge to manage construction projects on-site with confidence.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>',
                'duration' => '5',
            'days_content' => '["<p><strong>Introduction to Site Supervision and Management</strong></p>\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Understanding the role of a site supervisor</li>\\n<li>Key responsibilities of a site supervisor</li>\\n<li>Common challenges faced by site supervisors</li>\\n<li>Introduction to site management and its components</li>\\n<li>Overview of relevant laws and regulations</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Site Planning and Preparation</strong></p>\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Developing a site plan</li>\\n<li>Risk assessment and management</li>\\n<li>Preparing a project schedule</li>\\n<li>Procurement management for the site</li>\\n<li>Site logistics and resource planning</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Health and Safety Management</strong></p>\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Occupational Health and Safety (OH&amp;S) in construction</li>\\n<li>Identifying potential hazards and risks on site</li>\\n<li>Developing a health and safety plan</li>\\n<li>Managing site incidents and emergencies</li>\\n<li>Ensuring compliance with OH&amp;S regulations</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Project Quality and Productivity Management</strong></p>\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Understanding the importance of quality management on site</li>\\n<li>Implementing quality control and assurance</li>\\n<li>Measuring productivity and identifying areas for improvement</li>\\n<li>Managing subcontractors and suppliers to ensure quality and productivity</li>\\n<li>Communication and reporting to project stakeholders</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Site Handover and Closeout</strong></p>\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Planning for site handover and closeout</li>\\n<li>Documentation and record-keeping</li>\\n<li>Conducting a site walkthrough and final inspection</li>\\n<li>Managing punch lists and ensuring the completion of outstanding work</li>\\n<li>Finalising contracts and resolving any disputes</li>\\n</ul>"]',
