                'description' => '<p>The "Basics and Tools in MS Excel and MS Project for Project Managers" training is designed to provide project managers with the knowledge and skills to use Microsoft Excel and Microsoft Project effectively in managing their projects. The half-day training will cover the basics of these tools and their most commonly used features.<br /><br />Participants will learn how to use these tools to organise, analyse, and visualise project data and create project plans and schedules.</p>',
                'duration' => '5',
            'days_content' => '["<p><strong>Introduction to MS Excel and MS Project for Project Managers</strong></p>\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Introduction to MS Excel and MS Project</li>\\n<li>Understanding the role of these tools in project management</li>\\n<li>Understanding Excel interface and key features</li>\\n<li>Basic formulas and functions for project data analysis</li>\\n<li>Organising and visualising project data using Excel</li>\\n</ul>\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>","<p><strong>Advanced MS Excel for Project Managers&nbsp;</strong></p>\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Advanced formulas and functions for project data analysis</li>\\n<li>Creating and formatting charts for project data visualisation</li>\\n<li>Introduction to data validation and conditional formatting</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>MS Project Basics for Project Managers&nbsp;</strong></p>\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Understanding MS Project interface and key features</li>\\n<li>Creating project plans and schedules in MS Project</li>\\n<li>Tracking and monitoring project progress using MS Project</li>\\n</ul>\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>","<p><strong>Advanced MS Project for Project Managers&nbsp;</strong></p>\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Creating custom fields and views in MS Project</li>\\n<li>Creating multiple project plans and linking them together</li>\\n<li>Introduction to earned value management (EVM) in MS Project</li>\\n</ul>\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>","<p><strong>Integration of MS Excel and MS Project for Project Managers&nbsp;<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Importing project data from Excel to MS Project</li>\\n<li>Exporting project data from MS Project to Excel</li>\\n<li>Using MS Excel to enhance project data visualisation and analysis</li>\\n</ul>\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>"]',
                'related_courses' => '[]',
                'category_id' => 44,
                'online' => 0,
                'created_at' => '2025-04-03 12:50:24',
                'updated_at' => '2025-04-03 12:50:24',
            ),
            327 => 
            array (
                'id' => 1664,
                'lang_code' => 'en',
                'name' => 'Safety and Security in Facility Management',
                'description' => '<p>Safety and Security are critical aspects of Facility Management, and managing them effectively is crucial to ensuring business continuity and protecting people, processes, and property. The Safety and Security in Facility Management training course is designed to equip Facility Managers with the essential skills and knowledge required to manage safety and security in their organizations.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>The course covers the principles of safety and security, risk management, emergency response planning, security staffing, electronic surveillance, asset management, and compliance with quality standards and legal requirements. By the end of the course, participants will have a comprehensive understanding of safety and security in facility management and be equipped with the necessary skills and knowledge to perform their roles effectively.</p>',
                'duration' => '5',
                'days_content' => '["<p><strong>Introduction to Safety and Security in Facility Management</strong></p>\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Understanding the Principles of Security and Safety of People and Assets</li>\\n<li>Identifying Risks and Threats in Facilities</li>\\n<li>Developing a Risk Management Plan</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Emergency Response Planning</strong></p>\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Executing Emergency Responses in Various Scenarios</li>\\n<li>Communication and Coordination during Emergencies</li>\\n<li>Business Continuity Planning</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Security Staffing Deployments</strong></p>\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Roles and Responsibilities of Security Personnel</li>\\n<li>Managing Security Contracts</li>\\n<li>Legal Compliance in Security Operations</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Electronic Surveillance and IT-enabled Security</strong></p>\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Electronic Surveillance as a Force Multiplier</li>\\n<li>Planning and Deployment of Electronic Surveillance</li>\\n<li>IT Enabled Security and Asset Tracking Services</li>\\n<li>Adopting Green and Clean Technology in Security Operations</li>\\n</ul>\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>","<p><strong>Budget Planning and Asset Management</strong></p>\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Implementing ISO 27001 and ISO 17799 Quality Standards</li>\\n<li>Innovating and Adopting New Practices in Facility Management</li>\\n<li>Team Building and Communication</li>\\n</ul>"]',
                'related_courses' => '[]',
                'category_id' => 11,
                'online' => 1,
                'created_at' => '2025-04-03 12:50:24',
                'updated_at' => '2025-04-03 12:50:24',
            ),
