            'days_content' => '["<p><strong>Introduction to Social Phenomena and Research Methods<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Overview of social phenomena and their importance in society</li>\\n<li>Introduction to the research process and formulating research questions</li>\\n<li>Overview of qualitative and quantitative research methods</li>\\n<li>Ethical considerations in social research</li>\\n</ul>\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>","<p><strong>Qualitative Research Methods<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>In-depth interviews and focus groups</li>\\n<li>Participant observation and ethnography</li>\\n<li>Content analysis and discourse analysis</li>\\n<li>Case studies and comparative research</li>\\n<li>Coding and analyzing qualitative data</li>\\n</ul>\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>","<p><strong>Quantitative Research Methods<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Survey design and sampling techniques</li>\\n<li>Descriptive and inferential statistics</li>\\n<li>Regression analysis and correlation</li>\\n<li>Analyzing and interpreting quantitative data</li>\\n<li>Introduction to data visualization</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Social Network Analysis<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Overview of social network analysis</li>\\n<li>Key concepts and measures in network analysis</li>\\n<li>Data collection and preparation for network analysis</li>\\n<li>Visualization and interpretation of social networks</li>\\n<li>Application of network analysis in various social phenomena</li>\\n</ul>\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>","<p><strong>Presenting and Communicating Research Findings<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Strategies for effectively presenting research findings</li>\\n<li>Writing research reports and academic papers</li>\\n<li>Communicating research findings to different audiences (e.g., policymakers, media, and public)</li>\\n<li>Peer review and feedback on research projects</li>\\n<li>Course summary and next steps for further study and practice</li>\\n</ul>"]',
