            404 => 
            array (
                'id' => 1744,
                'lang_code' => 'en',
                'name' => 'Mastering Data Visualisation',
                'description' => '<p>Data is an essential part of decision-making in today\'s business world. However, the sheer amount of data available can be overwhelming, making it difficult to extract meaningful insights. Data visualization is a powerful tool that allows us to communicate complex information in a more accessible way. It enables us to tell compelling stories with data, make better decisions, and drive business outcomes.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>This 5-day course is designed to help UK professionals enhance their data visualization skills, whether they are analysts, data scientists, business intelligence professionals, marketers, or anyone who works with data. Through interactive lectures, hands-on practice sessions, and group projects, participants will learn the principles of effective data visualization and how to apply them to their work.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>This course covers the basics of data visualization, including data collection and preparation, choosing the right type of chart or graph, and designing effective visualizations. It also covers advanced techniques such as creating interactive visualizations, incorporating geospatial data and statistical analysis, and best practices for data-driven decision-making.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>By the end of this course, participants will be able to create compelling data visualizations that communicate insights effectively to a non-technical audience. They will also gain practical skills that they can apply to their work immediately, leading to better decision-making and business outcomes.</p>',
                'duration' => '5',
                'days_content' => '["<p><strong>Introduction to Data Visualization</strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Overview of data visualization and its importance</li>\\n<li>Principles of effective data visualization</li>\\n<li>Common types of charts and graphs</li>\\n<li>Understanding data types and variables</li>\\n</ul>\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>","<p><strong>Data Collection and Preparation for Visualization<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Collecting and preparing data for visualization</li>\\n<li>Cleaning and transforming data for better insights</li>\\n<li>Choosing the right data format for visualization</li>\\n<li>Introduction to data visualization software</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Designing Effective Visualizations<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Choosing the right type of chart or graph for your data</li>\\n<li>Design principles for creating effective visualizations</li>\\n<li>Color theory and best practices for color selection</li>\\n<li>Using typography and labels effectively</li>\\n</ul>\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>","<p><strong>Advanced Data Visualization Techniques<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Creating interactive visualizations for greater user engagement</li>\\n<li>Incorporating maps and geospatial data</li>\\n<li>Best practices for dashboard design</li>\\n<li>Incorporating statistical analysis in visualizations</li>\\n</ul>\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>","<p><strong>Presenting and Communicating Data Effectively<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Tips for presenting data to a non-technical audience</li>\\n<li>Using storytelling techniques in data visualization</li>\\n<li>Designing presentations with visualizations</li>\\n<li>Best practices for data-driven decision-making</li>\\n</ul>"]',
                'related_courses' => '[472,600,1039]',
                'category_id' => 51,
                'online' => 1,
                'created_at' => '2025-04-03 12:51:09',
                'updated_at' => '2025-04-03 12:51:09',
            ),
