            22 => 
            array (
                'id' => 1865,
                'lang_code' => 'en',
                'name' => 'Streamlining Hydrocarbon Operations: Oil and Gas Movement, Production Allocation, and Lifting Procedures under Separate Marketing Stream',
                'description' => '<p>This comprehensive 5-day course is designed to provide participants with a deep understanding of streamlining hydrocarbon operations, focusing on oil and gas movement, production allocation, and lifting procedures within the context of separate marketing streams. The course will cover essential concepts, industry best practices, regulatory frameworks, and advanced techniques to optimize operations and maximize efficiency in the oil and gas sector.</p>
<p>This training has been meticulously designed to furnish you with the essential knowledge of the hydrocarbon industry and learn from industry experts and real-world case studies, You will acquire specialized knowledge that goes beyond basic industry understanding. This expertise can make you a valuable asset to your organization and increase your career opportunities.</p>
<p>LPC provides this course to offer you a unique opportunity to gain specialized knowledge, practical skills, and industry insights that can accelerate your career and contribute to the success of your organization in the dynamic oil and gas sector.</p>',
                'duration' => '5',
            'days_content' => '["<p><strong>Fundamentals of Hydrocarbon Operations and Separate Marketing Streams<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Introduction to hydrocarbon operations: Exploration, drilling, production, and processing.</li>\\n<li>Overview of separate marketing streams: Understanding distinct marketing channels for oil and gas products.</li>\\n<li>Regulatory and legal considerations in separate marketing streams.</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Oil and Gas Movement Strategies<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Crude oil and natural gas transportation methods: Pipelines, tankers, LNG carriers, and more.</li>\\n<li>Storage facilities and their role in hydrocarbon movement.</li>\\n<li>Risk management and safety protocols during transportation.</li>\\n<li>Case studies: Real-world examples of successful hydrocarbon movement strategies.</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Production Allocation Techniques<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Importance of production allocation: Accurate measurement and allocation of produced hydrocarbons.</li>\\n<li>Allocation methodologies: Reservoir engineering, production logging, and tracer technologies.</li>\\n<li>Data management systems for production allocation.</li>\\n<li>Practical exercises: Allocating production in various reservoir scenarios.</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Lifting Procedures and Optimizing Production<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Lifting procedures and their significance in production optimization.</li>\\n<li>Types of lifting systems: Gas lift, ESP (Electric Submersible Pump), and more.</li>\\n<li>Monitoring and control of lifting operations.</li>\\n<li>Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning applications in lifting optimization.</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Enhancing Efficiency in Separate Marketing Streams<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Integrated operations management: Coordinating exploration, production, transportation, and marketing.</li>\\n<li>Role of technology in streamlining operations: IoT, automation, and data analytics.</li>\\n<li>Sustainability and environmental considerations in hydrocarbon operations.</li>\\n<li>Case studies: Successful examples of streamlining operations and marketing.</li>\\n</ul>"]',
                'related_courses' => '[]',
                'category_id' => 17,
                'online' => 1,
                'created_at' => '2025-04-03 12:51:57',
                'updated_at' => '2025-04-03 12:51:57',
            ),
