            ),
            32 => 
            array (
                'id' => 1875,
                'lang_code' => 'en',
                'name' => 'Getting Things Done “GTD “Training',
            'description' => '<p>In today\'s fast-paced world, we are constantly bombarded with tasks, commitments, and information, often leaving us feeling overwhelmed and stressed. In the midst of this chaos, it becomes increasingly challenging to focus on what truly matters and to make the most strategic decisions about where to invest our time and energy. The "Getting Things Done" (GTD) course, where LPC embark on a journey to regain control of our tasks, enhance productivity, and alleviate the burdens of stress and burnout. GTD is not just another time management system; it\'s a transformative approach to managing the relentless flow of requests, tasks, and interruptions that we encounter daily, both at work and in our personal lives.<br /><br /></p>
<p>By mastering GTD principles, you\'ll gain the tools and techniques needed to declutter your mind, prioritize effectively, and systematically conquer your to-do list.<br /><br /></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>Over the next five days, you will delve deep into the GTD methodology, equipping yourself with the skills to not only survive but thrive in the modern world of work. Whether you\'re a seasoned professional, a student seeking academic excellence, an overwhelmed caregiver, or anyone looking to enhance their personal and professional productivity, this course is tailored to meet your needs.</p>',
                'duration' => '5',
                'days_content' => '["<p><strong>Introduction to GTD<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Introduction to the concept of GTD and its benefits.</li>\\n<li>Understanding the challenges of modern work and information overload.</li>\\n<li>The GTD Workflow: Capture, Clarify, Organize, Reflect, Engage.</li>\\n<li>The Five Stages of GTD:</li>\\n</ul>\\n<ol style=\\"list-style-type: upper-roman;\\">\\n<li>Capture: Collecting all your tasks and commitments.</li>\\n<li>Clarify: Making decisions about what to do with each item.</li>\\n<li>Organize: Putting tasks into a system.</li>\\n<li>Reflect: Regularly reviewing your system.</li>\\n<li>Engage: Choosing what to work on.</li>\\n</ol>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Practical exercises for capturing tasks and commitments.</li>\\n</ul>\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>","<p><strong>Capturing and Collecting<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>The Art of Capturing: Tools and techniques for capturing tasks and ideas.</li>\\n<li>Inbox Zero: Managing your email and digital inputs.</li>\\n<li>&nbsp;<!--[endif]-->Effective note-taking and using digital tools.</li>\\n<li>Practical exercises for capturing and collecting tasks.</li>\\n<li>Setting up a physical and digital inbox.</li>\\n<li>Dealing with interruptions and distractions.</li>\\n</ul>\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>","<p><strong>Clarifying and Organizing<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>The importance of clarifying tasks.</li>\\n<li>The Two-Minute Rule: When to do it now and when to defer.</li>\\n<li>Contexts and Next Actions: How to determine what to work on next.</li>\\n<li>Organizing tasks in a trusted system.</li>\\n<li>Creating lists and project plans.</li>\\n<li>Practical exercises for clarifying and organizing tasks.</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Reviewing and Reflecting<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>The Weekly Review: A crucial GTD practice.</li>\\n<li>How to conduct a productive weekly review.</li>\\n<li>Goal setting and long-term planning with GTD.</li>\\n<li>Practical exercises for reviewing and reflecting.</li>\\n<li>Tips for maintaining a GTD system.</li>\\n<li>Handling priorities and deadlines effectively.</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Mastering GTD and Advanced Techniques<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Mastering GTD: Becoming a productivity pro.</li>\\n<li>Advanced GTD techniques and tips.</li>\\n<li>Handling complex projects and responsibilities.</li>\\n<li>Mindfulness and stress reduction with GTD.</li>\\n<li>Building a sustainable GTD habit.</li>\\n<li>Q&amp;A and course wrap-up.</li>\\n</ul>"]',
                'related_courses' => '[]',
                'category_id' => 41,
                'online' => 1,
                'created_at' => '2025-04-03 12:51:59',
                'updated_at' => '2025-04-03 12:51:59',
            ),
