w to minimise its effect.</li>\\n<li>Conduct simple inexpensive tests on different potting mixes and report accordingly.</li>\\n<li>Describe suitable soil mixes for container growing of different types of plants.</li>\\n<li>List a range of both natural and artificial fertilizers.</li>\\n<li>Describe fertilizer programs to be used in different situations with ornamental plants.</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Introductory Propagation Techniques<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Demonstrate propagation different plants by cuttings and seed.</li>\\n<li>Construct a simple inexpensive cold frame.</li>\\n<li>Mix and use a propagation media suited to propagating both seed and cuttings.</li>\\n<li>Describe the method and time of year used to propagate different plant varieties.</li>\\n<li>Describe and demonstrate the steps in preparing and executing a variety of grafts and one budding technique.</li>\\n<li>Explain the reasons why budding or grafting are sometimes preferred propagation methods.</li>\\n</ul>\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>","<p><strong>Identification and Use of Plants and pests, diseases<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Select plants appropriate for growing in different climates.</li>\\n<li>Select plants appropriate to use for shade, windbreaks, as a feature, and for various aesthetic effects.</li>\\n<li>Categorise priorities which effect selection of plants for an ornamental garden.</li>\\n<li>Explain the differences in the way plants perform in different microclimates within the same area.</li>\\n<li>List and analyze the situations where plants are used.</li>\\n<li>Describe the major ways in which diseases (fungal, viral, bacterial and nematode) affect turf, the life cycle features that cause them to become a</li>\\n<li>serious problem to turf culture and the methods available for their control.</li>\\n</ul>"]',
                'related_courses' => '[]',
                'category_id' => 45,
                'online' => 0,
                'created_at' => '2025-04-03 12:52:04',
                'updated_at' => '2025-04-03 12:52:04',
            ),
            50 => 
            array (
                'id' => 1893,
                'lang_code' => 'en',
                'name' => 'Mastering Facility Management: FMP Certification, Project Management Fundamentals, and Maintenance & Reliability Best Practices',
                'description' => '<p>Elevate your professional capabilities with our comprehensive suite of courses, each designed to empower you with essential skills and knowledge that are highly sought after in today\'s competitive business landscape.</p>
<p><strong>Project Management Fundamentals</strong>: In our Project Management course, you\'ll develop highly valued project management skills that are essential for meeting deadlines, controlling costs, and ensuring flawless deliverables. Dive into the full project life cycle, from defining projects to meticulous planning, and finally, seamless implementation.</p>
<p><strong>Facility Management Professional (FMP)</strong>: The Facility Management Professional (FMP) certification is the key to mastering the art of orchestrating facilities. This course equips you with advanced knowledge and competencies in facility management, making you a sought-after leader in shaping and managing facilities. Gain insights into critical facility management concepts and demonstrate your ongoing commitment to the profession.</p>
<p><strong>Maintenance &amp; Reliability Best Practices</strong>: Unlock the secrets to success with Maintenance &amp; Reliability Best Practices. This course offers practical insights, tools, and techniques to excel in maintenance planning and cost management. Engage in interactive discussions, case studies, and hands-on exercises to ensure you can apply these concepts effectively in your organization.</p>
<p>Whether you\'re looking to enhance your project management skills, become a Facility Management Professional, or excel in maintenance and reliability, our courses are tailored to empower your career journey. Join us and stay ahead in today\'s dynamic business world.</p>',
                'duration' => '10',
            'days_content' => '["<p><strong><span style=\\"font-size: 14pt;\\">Understanding the Fundamentals of Project Management</span><u><span style=\\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: Abadi, sans-serif; background: white;\\"><br /></span></u></strong><strong><br /><br />Introduction to Project Management<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Defining what a project is &ndash; and is not</li>\\n<li>Understanding Projects, Programs, Portfolios, and their relationship to Organizational Strategy</li>\\n<li>The significance of project management in achieving strategic objectives<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<p><strong>Project Management Basics<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Defining project management and the project lifecycle</li>\\n<li>Overview of different organizational structures: Functional, Projectized, Weak, Balanced &amp; Strong matrix</li>\\n<li>Identifying, analyzing, and engaging project stakeholders</li>\\n</ul>","<p><span style=\\"font-size: 14pt;\\"><strong>Planning and Executing Projects</strong></span></p>\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n<p><strong>Project Integration Management<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Writing the project charter&mdash;Purpose and contents</li>\\n<li>Developing the Project Management Plan</li>\\n<li>The process of project execution</li>\\n<li>The process of monitoring and controlling</li>\\n<li>Using Integrated change control</li>\\n<li>Handling change requests and corrective/preventive actions<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<p><strong>Planning the Project and Budgeting<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Collecting Project requirements</li>\\n<li>Planning and defining the total project scope</li>\\n<li>Creating the Work Breakdown Structure (WBS) and WBS dictionary</li>\\n<li>Identifying project activities</li>\\n<li>Estimating activity durations and resources using various methods</li>\\n<li>Developing the project schedule, including Network Diagrams and dependencies</li>\\n<li>Estimating project costs, budgeting, and cash flow analysis</li>\\n</ul>\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>","<p><span style=\\"font-size: 14pt;\\"><strong>Project Control and Strategic Project Management</strong></span></p>\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n<p><strong>Monitoring and Controlling the Project<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Understanding Scope creep and Gold plating</li>\\n<li>Controlling the project schedule with techniques like Crashing and Fast tracking</li>\\n<li>Controlling project costs using Earned Value analysis</li>\\n<li>Effective communication of project performance<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<p><strong>Project Strategy<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Differentiating between strategic and operational project management</li>\\n<li>Identifying projects that align with organizational strategy through SWOT analysis</li>\\n<li>Strategic project management and project selection financial models, including Net Present Value (NPV) and Decision trees</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong><span style=\\"font-size: 14pt;\\">Project Risk Management, Risk, and Closure</span><br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<p><strong>Project Risk Management<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Project risk identification and assessment</li>\\n<li>Qualitative and quantitative risk analysis</li>\\n<li>Developing project risk response plans to mitigate or exploit risks<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<p><strong>Closing Out The Project<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Administrative closure procedures</li>\\n<li>Updating Organizational processes assets</li>\\n<li>Documenting Lessons Learned for future improvement</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Facility Management Professional (FMP) - Finance and Business<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Essential Finance and Business Practices in Facility Management</li>\\n<li>Engaging with Finance Departments</li>\\n<li>Legal Aspects in Facility Management</li>\\n<li>Procurement Strategies and Practices</li>\\n<li>Risk Management in Facility Management</li>\\n<li>Maximizing Decision-Making for Your Organization</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Operations and Maintenance<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Assessing and Inspecting Facility Needs</li>\\n<li>Managing, Overseeing, and Monitoring O&amp;M of Buildings</li>\\n<li>O&amp;M of Systems and Equipment</li>\\n<li>Developing Occupant Service Specifications</li>\\n<li>Case Studies on O&amp;M Challenges</li>\\n</ul>\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>","<p><strong>Leadership and Strategy, Project Management, Strategic Planning &amp; Management<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Effective Strategies to Integrate People, Place, and Process</li>\\n<li>Aligning Facility Portfolio Functionality with Organizational Missions</li>\\n<li>Project Management in Facility Management</li>\\n<li>Strategic Planning and Management for Competitive Advantage</li>\\n<li>Business Continuity and Success in Facility Management</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Maintenance and Reliability Best Practices - Asset Cost Management and Laying the Groundwork</strong></p>\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Introduction to Asset Cost Management</li>\\n<li>Definitions of Reliability, Maintenance, and Asset Management</li>\\n<li>Total Cost of Maintenance</li>\\n<li>Best Practice Reliability and Maintenance Processes</li>\\n<li>Elements of Asset Management Best Practice</li>\\n<li>Auditing Performance</li>\\n<li>Overview of TPM, RCM, BCM, QCM, and Other Asset Management Concepts</li>\\n</ul>\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>","<p><strong>Applying the Value-based Process<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Teamwork in Maintenance, Operations, and Stores</li>\\n<li>Importance of Standards such as PAS 55 and JA1011</li>\\n<li>Corporate Asset Management Expectations</li>\\n<li>Asset Performance Expectations</li>\\n<li>Forms of Asset Failure and Degradation</li>\\n<li>Causes and Nature of Asset Failure and Degradation</li>\\n<li>Effects, Costs, and Risks of Asset Degradation</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Ensuring Continuity and Supporting Cost Reduction<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Breaking the Cycle of Failure and Degradation</li>\\n<li>Selecting PM Tactics Based on Costs and Risks</li>\\n<li>Determining PM Intervals</li>\\n<li>Condition-Based Maintenance Types and the PF-Curve</li>\\n<li>The Four Important Reliability Functions</li>\\n<li>Implementing Best Practice Maintenance Programs</li>\\n<li>Optimizing Spares to Support Maintenance</li>\\n<li>Maintenance Program Cost and Risk-Based Justification</li>\\n<li>Completing the PLAN, DO, REVIEW Improvement Cycle with FRACAS</li>\\n<li>Failure Reporting, Analysis, and Corrective Action System Requirements</li>\\n<li>Data Collection to Support Reliability Analysis</li>\\n<li>Reliability Analysis Case Study</li>\\n<li>Discussion of Supporting Software and Templates</li>\\n<li>Planning and Scheduling Best Practices</li>\\n<li>Cost-Effective Manpower and Skills Deployment</li>\\n<li>Performance Indicators for Continuous Improvement</li>\\n<li>Overall Review of Concepts Learned</li>\\n</ul>"]',
