            52 => 
            array (
                'id' => 1895,
                'lang_code' => 'en',
                'name' => 'Automated Power System Protection Testing',
                'description' => '<p>Welcome to the "Advanced Automated Power System Protection Testing" course! In today\'s rapidly evolving power industry, ensuring the reliable operation of protection relays is paramount. This intensive 5-day program has been meticulously designed to equip electrical professionals with the knowledge and hands-on skills necessary to excel in power system protection testing.</p>
<p>Throughout the course, you will delve into the intricacies of OMICRON Test Universe software and the CMC test set, mastering their application for testing overcurrent, distance, and transformer differential relays. We will cover fundamental protection principles, emphasize safety protocols, and empower you to create reusable test plans, boosting testing efficiency.</p>
<p>By the end of this program, you\'ll be proficient in testing a variety of protection relays and equipped to navigate OMICRON\'s support ecosystem. Whether you\'re an experienced engineer or a newcomer to protection testing, this course will elevate your expertise and contribute to the reliability and safety of power systems. Join us on this educational journey to become a proficient power system protection tester.</p>',
                'duration' => '5',
            'days_content' => '["<p><strong>Introduction to Protection Testing Basics<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul type=\\"disc\\">\\n<li>Power system protection principles and typical substation topologies</li>\\n<li>Overview of protection testing basics</li>\\n<li>Importance of safety aspects for test preparation and execution</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>OMICRON Test Universe and CMC Test Set<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul type=\\"disc\\">\\n<li>Introduction to the OMICRON Control Center (OCC) and relevant test modules</li>\\n<li>Modelling of relay characteristics in the Test Object for subsequent testing</li>\\n<li>Test setup and configuration options for the CMC test set</li>\\n<li>Quick current and voltage output for easy wiring tests</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Non-Directional Overcurrent Protection<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul type=\\"disc\\">\\n<li>Fundamentals of non-directional overcurrent protection functions</li>\\n<li>Creating a reusable test plan (OCC file) for testing non-directional overcurrent relays</li>\\n<li>Hands-on testing of non-directional overcurrent protection relays</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Distance and Transformer Differential Protection<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul type=\\"disc\\">\\n<li>Fundamentals of distance, ground fault, and transformer differential protection functions</li>\\n<li>Creating reusable test plans for testing distance relays</li>\\n<li>Creating reusable test plans for testing transformer differential relays</li>\\n<li>Testing ground fault protection with RelaySimTest using realistic network simulation</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Practical Testing and OMICRON Support<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul type=\\"disc\\">\\n<li>Hands-on testing of distance and transformer differential relays, as well as ground fault protection function</li>\\n<li>Exploring OMICRON support options, including technical support, knowledge library, and the worldwide community</li>\\n<li>Overview of the full range of OMICRON solutions for protection testing</li>\\n</ul>"]',
                'related_courses' => '[]',
                'category_id' => 19,
                'online' => 1,
                'created_at' => '2025-04-03 12:52:05',
                'updated_at' => '2025-04-03 12:52:05',
            ),
