            86 => 
            array (
                'id' => 1929,
                'lang_code' => 'en',
                'name' => 'Mastering Quality Management: ISO 9001:2015 Comprehensive Training',
            'description' => '<p>Having an internationally recognized Quality Management System (QMS) allows you to enhance organizational performance and increase customer satisfaction.&nbsp;&nbsp;ISO 9001:2015 would help your organisation deliver and drive continual improvement in your services.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>This course is an introduction for individuals with little or no previous knowledge of ISO 9001 or a Quality Management System (QMS). Essentials of ISO 9001:2015 provides a general understanding of the necessary concepts of the ISO 9000 series of standards and the impact of the requirements on the day-to-day operations of organizations in any industry.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>The course explains the clauses of ISO 9001:2015, providing a foundation for understanding quality management principles. It would help you identify the structure and requirements of an effective QMS. You will gain the required skills to conduct a baseline review of your organization&rsquo;s current position and implement the key principles of ISO 9001:2015.</p>',
                'duration' => '10',
                'days_content' => '["<p><strong>Introduction to Quality Management and ISO 9001:2015<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Overview of ISO 9001:2015 and its relevance</li>\\n<li>Quality Management Principles</li>\\n<li>Introduction to the structure of ISO 9001:2015</li>\\n<li>Understanding the Annex SL framework</li>\\n<li>Identifying key interested parties and risk-based thinking</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Context of the Organization<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>In-depth analysis of organizational context</li>\\n<li>Needs and expectations of interested parties</li>\\n<li>Determining the scope of the QMS</li>\\n<li>Understanding and managing external and internal issues</li>\\n<li>Interactive workshop on aligning QMS with organizational context</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Leadership and Commitment<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Role of top management in QMS</li>\\n<li>Establishing a quality policy</li>\\n<li>Roles, responsibilities, and authorities in QMS</li>\\n<li>Leadership\'s role in promoting a quality culture</li>\\n<li>Case studies of effective leadership in quality management</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Planning for the QMS<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Addressing risks and opportunities</li>\\n<li>Setting quality objectives and planning to achieve them</li>\\n<li>Change management strategies</li>\\n<li>Developing a comprehensive risk management framework</li>\\n<li>Group exercises on creating actionable quality plans</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Support and Resources<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Identifying and managing resources for QMS</li>\\n<li>Importance of competence, training, and awareness</li>\\n<li>Creating and maintaining documented information</li>\\n<li>Strategies for effective communication and awareness in QMS</li>\\n<li>Workshop on resource allocation and management</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Operation &ndash; Part 1<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Operational planning and control</li>\\n<li>Requirements for products and services</li>\\n<li>Control of externally provided processes, products, and services</li>\\n<li>Interactive session on design and development of services</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Operation &ndash; Part 2<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Control of production and service provision</li>\\n<li>Release of products and services</li>\\n<li>Control of nonconforming outputs</li>\\n<li>Practical exercises on operational control and process improvement</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Performance Evaluation<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Monitoring, measurement, analysis, and evaluation</li>\\n<li>Internal audit methodology and practices</li>\\n<li>Management review mechanisms</li>\\n<li>Implementing KPIs and performance metrics</li>\\n<li>Workshop on developing an internal audit program</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Improvement &ndash; Part 1<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>General concepts of improvement in QMS</li>\\n<li>Identifying and selecting opportunities for improvement</li>\\n<li>Corrective actions and problem-solving techniques</li>\\n<li>Case studies on successful QMS improvements</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Improvement &ndash; Part 2 and Course Wrap-Up<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Continual improvement strategies</li>\\n<li>Implementing and managing a culture of continuous improvement</li>\\n<li>Review of ISO 9001:2015 requirements and best practices</li>\\n<li>Final assessment and certification</li>\\n<li>Feedback session and course conclusion</li>\\n</ul>"]',
