</li>\\n<li>Requirements for products and services</li>\\n<li>Control of externally provided processes, products, and services</li>\\n<li>Interactive session on design and development of services</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Operation &ndash; Part 2<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Control of production and service provision</li>\\n<li>Release of products and services</li>\\n<li>Control of nonconforming outputs</li>\\n<li>Practical exercises on operational control and process improvement</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Performance Evaluation<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Monitoring, measurement, analysis, and evaluation</li>\\n<li>Internal audit methodology and practices</li>\\n<li>Management review mechanisms</li>\\n<li>Implementing KPIs and performance metrics</li>\\n<li>Workshop on developing an internal audit program</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Improvement &ndash; Part 1<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>General concepts of improvement in QMS</li>\\n<li>Identifying and selecting opportunities for improvement</li>\\n<li>Corrective actions and problem-solving techniques</li>\\n<li>Case studies on successful QMS improvements</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Improvement &ndash; Part 2 and Course Wrap-Up<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Continual improvement strategies</li>\\n<li>Implementing and managing a culture of continuous improvement</li>\\n<li>Review of ISO 9001:2015 requirements and best practices</li>\\n<li>Final assessment and certification</li>\\n<li>Feedback session and course conclusion</li>\\n</ul>"]',
