            175 => 
            array (
                'id' => 2019,
                'lang_code' => 'en',
                'name' => 'Tank Cleaning Hazards',
                'description' => '<p>Welcome to the "Tank Cleaning Hazards" course! Throughout this 5-day journey, designed with care by LPC, you&rsquo;ll gain a comprehensive knowledge and skills for safe and efficient tank cleaning and maintenance.<br /><br /></p>
<p>Over the span of 5 days with LPC, you&rsquo;ll learn about different tank cleaning hazards and how to ensure and implement safety precautions while cleaning tanks. The first step in this journey includes building the foundation of tank cleaning including the importance of tanks and regular tank cleaning, along with typical procedures and essential tools to achieve a spotless tank. Then, you&rsquo;ll learn how to conquer tank cleaning hazards by understanding the causes of these hazards and techniques to avoid them. Moving forward, we&rsquo;ll go deeper into safety precautions and risk minimization through focusing on personal protective equipment (PPE), pre-initiating procedures, and trainings. Next, you&rsquo;ll be ready to develop your tank cleaning safety plan. Finally, you&rsquo;ll explore international and global standards and regulations of tank cleaning to ensure the compliance with them.<br /><br /></p>
<p>By the conclusion of this course, you&rsquo;ll be armed with the expertise to navigate tank cleaning with confidence, ensuring a safe and efficient operation every time.<br /><br /></p>
<p>Are you ready to take control of tank cleaning safety? Join LPC and start your journey to excel tank cleaning safety.</p>',
                'duration' => '5',
            'days_content' => '["<p><strong>Introduction to Tank Cleaning</strong> <br /><br /></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Understanding why tanks are used</li>\\n<li>Discussing the importance of maintaining regular tank cleaning:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: square;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Internal moisture build-up</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Sludge</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Microbial contamination<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Understanding when tanks cleaning should be done</li>\\n<li>Discussing the typical procedures for cleaning tanks</li>\\n<li>Exploring tools to be used in tank cleaning</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Tank Cleaning Hazards<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Understanding why tank cleaning is dangerous</li>\\n<li>Defining fire, explosion, and flammable vapors hazards and understanding ways to avoid them</li>\\n<li>Exploring sources of ignition and how to deal with them to avoid hazard:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: square;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Electrical equipments</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Lighting</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Static electricity</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Hot surfaces</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Pyrophoric scale<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Techniques to avoid chemical, radiation and microbiological hazards</li>\\n<li>Understanding types of physical hazards can by caused by tank cleaning</li>\\n<li>Discussing hazards associated with oxygen deficiency</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Hazards Minimizing<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Discussing the recommended personal protection equipment&rsquo;s according to OSHA standards:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: square;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Hardhat</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Eye protection</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Gloves</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Boots</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Respiratory protection<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Discussing safety procedures before cleaning, including the situation of tank components</li>\\n<li>Understanding when and why to use harness and retrieval lines</li>\\n<li>Understanding when to use full body suites and its disposals procedures</li>\\n<li>Determining the importance of only allowing trained professional to perform tank cleaning and what kinds of skills and knowledge they should have</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Tank Cleaning Safety Plan</strong> <br /><br /></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Understanding the importance of having a plan before starting the cleaning of tanks</li>\\n<li>Determining the importance of communicating the plan with involved personnel</li>\\n<li>Exploring the components of safety plan:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: square;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Tank cleaning procedures</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Regulations for workers and managers</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Potential risks assessment</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Emergency preparedness training</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Permits required<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Discussing the importance of providing emergency rescue team to be prepared for the worst scenarios</li>\\n<li>Discussing techniques to analyze hazards and risks to conduct elimination and control plan</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Tank Cleaning Standards&nbsp;</strong> <br /><br /></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Overview of Quality, Health, Safety, and Environment (QHSE) framework</li>\\n<li>Discussing QHSE protocols for tank cleaning</li>\\n<li>Exploring OSHA regulations associated with tank cleaning</li>\\n<li>Discussing tank cleaning standards and codes developed by the American Petroleum Institute (API) and National Fire Protection Association (NFPA)</li>\\n<li>Discussion: analyzing real-work examples of successful and frailer stories about tank cleaning</li>\\n</ul>"]',
                'related_courses' => '[]',
                'category_id' => 15,
                'online' => 1,
                'created_at' => '2025-04-03 12:52:50',
                'updated_at' => '2025-04-03 12:52:50',
            ),
