            177 => 
            array (
                'id' => 2021,
                'lang_code' => 'en',
                'name' => 'Scaffolding Hazards & Safety Precautions',
                'description' => '<p>Welcome to the "Scaffolding Hazards &amp; Safety Precautions" course! We\'re thrilled to welcome you aboard for this transformative 5-day program meticulously designed by LPC. Throughout this course, you&rsquo;ll will gain the knowledge and skills to use scaffolds safely by understanding safety precautions and regulations.<br /><br /></p>
<p>In this journey with LPC, you&rsquo;ll explore different types of scaffolding and their components and applications, as well as the importance of ensuring scaffolding safety whether by following safety regulations or using manufacturer instructions. Then, you&rsquo;ll discover various types of potential hazards associate with scaffolding and how to assess these risks to implement effective risk mitigation plans and precautions. Moving on, you&rsquo;ll understand the OSHA&rsquo;s safety regulations for building safe and secured scaffolds, and maintaining safe and healthy work platforms. Additionally, you&rsquo;ll master techniques and ways for providing fall protection, electrocution prevention, and securing scaffoldings. Finally, you&rsquo;ll understand the importance of emphasizing regular inspections and maintenance and keeping records for scaffolding safety.<br /><br /></p>
<p>Join LPC on this enriching journey to gain the confidence to work on scaffolds with a focus on safety and efficiency. Let&rsquo;s build a strong secure foundation for your success!</p>',
                'duration' => '5',
            'days_content' => '["<p><strong>Introduction to Scaffolding</strong></p>\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: square;\\">\\n<li>What is scaffolding?</li>\\n<li>Understanding the function and common components of scaffold</li>\\n<li>Discussing the types of scaffolding and their applications:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: square;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Suspended scaffolds</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Supported scaffolds<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Exploring the role and responsibilities of scaffolds workers groups:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: square;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Erectors/ Dismantlers</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Users</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Designers<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Understanding the importance of ensuring scaffolding safety</li>\\n<li>Discussing how to use manufacturer instructions to ensure safety during all work levels</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Scaffolding Hazards &amp; Risk Assessment</strong></p>\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Discussing the common hazards associated with all scaffolds:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: square;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Falls from elevation</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Collapse of the scaffold</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Being struck by falling tools, work materials, or debris</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Electrocution</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Unsafe work practices</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Weather-related hazards<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Differentiating between competent and qualified person</li>\\n<li>Understanding the importance of assessing risks and hazards</li>\\n<li>Determining risk severity by probability of risk materializing and the impact of risk</li>\\n<li>Discussing the levels of probability of risk and impact of risk</li>\\n<li>Exploring main measurements for risk assessment of any hazard:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: square;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Potential hazard with consideration of equipment, environment</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<!--[endif]-->Who/ What could be harmed by the hazard?</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;The way of establishing risk level</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;The elimination and control precautions</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Scaffolding Requirements &amp; Regulations</strong> <br /><br /></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Overview of OSHA&rsquo;s Scaffolding Safety Standard</li>\\n<li>Exploring the regulations for scaffold load capacity?</li>\\n<li>Discussing the requirements for constructing scaffold platform and scaffold planking</li>\\n<li>Discussing supported and suspended scaffolds considerations</li>\\n<li>Discussing the importance of access requirements to scaffold platforms and types of access</li>\\n<li>Discovering what types of scaffolds are prohibited and when working on scaffolds is prohibited</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Scaffolding Safety Best Practices&nbsp;</strong></p>\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Techniques and tools for fall protection:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: square;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Guardrails</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Personal fall protection systems</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Safe access points (e.g. Ladders, stair towers, etc.)</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Toe-boards and screens</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Debris nets, catch platforms, or canopies<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>What is the personal protective equipment (PPE)? Why and how to use them?<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: square;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Helmets</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Harnesses</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Safety Glasses</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Hearing protection</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Gloves</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Footwear</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Protection clothing<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Discussing ways to ensure electrocution protection<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: square;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Enough distance between a scaffold and insulated powerlines</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Utilizing PPE</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Considering weather conditions<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Exploring how to secure scaffolding:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: square;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Resting the scaffold&rsquo;s base plates/ adjustable legs on a solid and level surface</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Utilizing scaffold ties and bracing</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Planning the scaffold to create safe and stable working platform<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Discovering common signages used for scaffold safety</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Inspection &amp; Maintenance<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Discussing the importance of adopting regular inspection and maintenance for scaffolds</li>\\n<li>Exploring when and for what inspection and maintenance should be done</li>\\n<li>Determining the importance of keeping records of inspection and repairs process&nbsp;&nbsp;</li>\\n<li>Practical inspection of different types of scaffolds</li>\\n<li>Course recap and Q&amp;A</li>\\n</ul>"]',
                'related_courses' => '[]',
                'category_id' => 15,
                'online' => 1,
                'created_at' => '2025-04-03 12:52:51',
                'updated_at' => '2025-04-03 12:52:51',
            ),
