            190 => 
            array (
                'id' => 2034,
                'lang_code' => 'en',
            'name' => 'Certified Management Accountant - Part 1 (Preparation Course)',
                'description' => '<p>Welcome to the " Certified Management Accountant - Part 1" course! This course is designed with care by LPC to equip you with the skills and knowledge needed to excel in financial planning, performance, and analytics.&nbsp;</p>
<p>Throughout this LPC course, you\'ll gain a deep understanding of various financial statements and reporting techniques. You&rsquo;ll master planning, budgeting, and forecasting strategies and tools. As we progress, we&rsquo;ll dive deep into cost management strategies and understand the significance of internal controls, technology systems, and data analytics in modern financial practices.&nbsp;</p>
<p>By the end of this program LPC program, you\'ll be well-equipped with tools and insights to enhance your financial and accounting acumen and support the strategic objectives of your organization. Join us and unlock the full potential of financial management and reporting with LPC!</p>',
                'duration' => '5',
                'days_content' => '["<p><strong>External Financial Reporting Decisions</strong></p>\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n<ul>\\n<li><strong>Identifying types of financial statements and their purpose, application and components:</strong></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>Balance sheet</li>\\n<li>Income statement&nbsp;</li>\\n<li>Statement of changes in equity&nbsp;</li>\\n<li>Statement of cash flows</li>\\n<li>Consolidated statements&nbsp;</li>\\n<li>Integrated reporting&nbsp;&nbsp;<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Discussing the application and limitation of each financial statement&nbsp;</li>\\n<li>Understanding the purpose and structure of integrated report&nbsp;</li>\\n<li>Methods for valuating assets and liabilities&nbsp;</li>\\n<li>Understanding the impact of equity transactions on capital, stock and revenues&nbsp;</li>\\n<li>The principles of revenue recognition&nbsp;</li>\\n<li>Strategies to measure income and define gains and losses&nbsp;</li>\\n<li>Differentiating between U.S, GAAP and IFRS accounting standards</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Planning, Budgeting, &amp; Forecasting</strong></p>\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>The process and techniques for strategic planning&nbsp;</li>\\n<li>Characteristics of successful strategic planning process&nbsp;</li>\\n<li>Defining budgeting and its key related terms</li>\\n<li>Characteristics of successful budgeting process&nbsp;<br /><br /></li>\\n<li>Understanding various forecasting techniques:</li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>Regression analysis&nbsp;</li>\\n<li>Learning curve analysis&nbsp;</li>\\n<li>Expected value&nbsp;<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Understanding different budgeting methods:&nbsp;</li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>Annual business plan&nbsp;</li>\\n<li>Project budgeting&nbsp;</li>\\n<li>Activity-based budgeting&nbsp;</li>\\n<li>Zero-based budgeting&nbsp;</li>\\n<li>Continuous budgets&nbsp;</li>\\n<li>Flexible budgeting&nbsp;<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Understanding how to plan for annual profit&nbsp;</li>\\n<li>Annual profit plan and supporting schedules&nbsp;</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Performance Management&nbsp;<br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Techniques for measuring cost and variation:&nbsp;</li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>Actual vs. planned results&nbsp;</li>\\n<li>Flexible budgets for performance analysis&nbsp;</li>\\n<li>Expectation management&nbsp;</li>\\n<li>Standards cost systems</li>\\n<li>Standard cost expectations for variation analysis&nbsp;<br /><br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Recognizing types of responsibility centers&nbsp;</li>\\n<li>Techniques for identifying organizational segments for reporting&nbsp;<br /><br /></li>\\n<li>Methods to measure performance:</li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>Product profitability analysis</li>\\n<li>Business unit profitability&nbsp;</li>\\n<li>Customer profitability analysis&nbsp;</li>\\n<li>ROI&nbsp;</li>\\n<li>Residual base issues</li>\\n<li>KPIs</li>\\n<li>Balanced scorecard&nbsp;</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Cost Management<br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Understanding the types of cost and cost behavior&nbsp;<br /><br /></li>\\n<li>Understanding different costing systems:</li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>Job order costing</li>\\n<li>Activity-based costing&nbsp;</li>\\n<li>Life-cycle costing&nbsp;<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Understanding the components of overhead costs and how to determine them&nbsp;&nbsp;</li>\\n<li>Exploring techniques to manage supply chain and resources</li>\\n<li>Exploring how to improve business process continuously&nbsp;</li>\\n<li>Discussing best practice analysis for business process improvement</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Internal Controls, Technology &amp; Analytics</strong></p>\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Understanding internal control risk and methods for testing&nbsp;</li>\\n<li>Standards and regulations for internal control&nbsp;<br /><br /></li>\\n<li>Exploring different system controls and security measures:</li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>General accounting system controls</li>\\n<li>Application and transaction controls</li>\\n<li>Technology controls&nbsp;</li>\\n<li>Backup controls&nbsp;<br /><br /></li>\\n<li>Exploring different information systems:</li>\\n<li>Accounting information systems</li>\\n<li>Enterprise resource planning systems</li>\\n<li>Enterprise performance management systems&nbsp;<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Understanding data policies and procedures and techniques to manage data&nbsp;</li>\\n<li>Discussing how to transform to technology-enabled finance and automation&nbsp;</li>\\n<li>Understanding data analytics types and tools</li>\\n<li>Course recap &amp; Evaluation</li>\\n</ul>\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>"]',
