            191 => 
            array (
                'id' => 2035,
                'lang_code' => 'en',
                'name' => 'Social Security & Risk Management',
                'description' => '<p>Welcome to the " Social Security &amp; Risk Management" course! We\'re thrilled to welcome you aboard for this intensive 5-day program meticulously designed by LPC. Throughout this course, you&rsquo;ll be equipped with the necessary knowledge and skills to manage risk associated with social security.&nbsp;</p>
<p>Over a span of 5 days, you&rsquo;ll enroll in a journey to gain a comprehensive understanding of social security systems and the critical role of risk management within these systems. Through engaging and interactive sessions, you\'ll explore the fundamentals of social security including social security benefits, funding methods and benefits calculation techniques. Moreover, you\'ll explore risk management strategies and tools. LPC will guide you through the entire process of risk management, including identifying, analyzing, measuring, controlling, monitoring and controlling risk. By the end of this course, you&rsquo;ll gain expertise in using risk management tools to manage uncertainty and reduce risks in social security systems.&nbsp;</p>
<p>Join LPC today on this enriching journey to gain valuable insight and practical skills to effectively manage social security systems and mitigate associated risks.</p>',
                'duration' => '5',
            'days_content' => '["<p><strong>Introduction to Social Security&nbsp;</strong></p>\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Introduction to the concept of social security and its significance&nbsp;</li>\\n<li>Discussing the evolution of social security&nbsp;<br /><br /></li>\\n<li>Exploring types of social security benefits and how each works:</li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>Retirement benefits</li>\\n<li>Disability benefits&nbsp;</li>\\n<li>Spousal benefits&nbsp;</li>\\n<li>Survivor benefits</li>\\n<li>Medical benefits<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Eligibility requirements for social security benefits&nbsp;</li>\\n<li>Case study: Analyzing examples of social security systems and highlighting its main features and challenges</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Social Security Fundamentals</strong></p>\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Understanding how social security system is funded:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>Taxation</li>\\n<li>Trust funds</li>\\n<li>Trust fund investments</li>\\n<li>Pay-as-you-go financing&nbsp;</li>\\n<li>Daily funding operations&nbsp;<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Formulas for calculating social security:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>Primary insurance amount (PIA)</li>\\n<li>Inflation-adjusted earnings base</li>\\n<li>Average indexed monthly earnings (AIME)</li>\\n<li>Bend point percentages<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Utilizing SSA tools to calculate social security benefits&nbsp;</li>\\n<li>Understanding the payment of social security benefits&nbsp;</li>\\n<li>Discussing social security regulations and standards&nbsp;</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Risk Management in Social Security:<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Risk categories in social security systems:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>Financial risks</li>\\n<li>Insurance and demographic risks</li>\\n<li>Strategic risk</li>\\n<li>Operational risks<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Understanding the enterprise risk management (ERM) approach and its role in managing social security systems risk<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>Exploring the process of risk management:</li>\\n<li>Strategic planning&nbsp;</li>\\n<li>Risk identification and analysis</li>\\n<li>Risk measurement&nbsp;</li>\\n<li>Risk control &amp; treatment&nbsp;</li>\\n<li>Risk monitoring &amp; reporting&nbsp;<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Understanding how to strategically plan for risk management</li>\\n<li>Discussing how to identify risk in social security systems</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>&nbsp;Risk Analysis, Assessment &amp; Control&nbsp;</strong></p>\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Exploring the process of analyzing risks:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>Describing and categorize risks</li>\\n<li>Analyzing likelihood and severity&nbsp;</li>\\n<li>Documenting risk</li>\\n<li>Mapping and prioritizing risk<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Understanding the importance of developing risk registers and risk maps&nbsp;</li>\\n<li>Developing key risk indicators (KRIs) to measure risk&nbsp;</li>\\n<li>Discussing when to tolerance, element, transfer, or transform risk&nbsp;</li>\\n<li>Exercise: Develop risk registers, risk map, KRIs and action plan&nbsp;</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Risk Monitoring &amp; Reporting&nbsp;</strong></p>\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Discussing the need for ongoing monitoring and surveillance process&nbsp;</li>\\n<li>Tools and techniques for risk monitoring&nbsp;</li>\\n<li>Best practices for reporting and communicating risk&nbsp;</li>\\n<li>Techniques to build a comprehensive risk management system&nbsp;</li>\\n<li>Exploring future trends and global practices in social security risk management&nbsp;</li>\\n<li>Final presentation of risk management plan&nbsp;</li>\\n<li>Course recap and Q&amp;A</li>\\n</ul>"]',
                'related_courses' => '[844,854,1530]',
                'category_id' => 15,
                'online' => 1,
                'created_at' => '2025-04-03 12:52:55',
                'updated_at' => '2025-04-03 12:52:55',
            ),
