            213 => 
            array (
                'id' => 2057,
                'lang_code' => 'en',
            'name' => 'Certified Associate in Project Management (CAPM) (Preparation Course)',
            'description' => '<p>LPC welcomes you to the &ldquo;Preparation Course for Certified Associate in Project Management (CAPM)&rdquo;. This 5-days intensive program is meticulously designed by LPC to provide a comprehensive knowledge of project management. Over five days, participants will embark on a learning journey, exploring the fundamentals, terminology and practice of effective project management as outlined in the PMI Guide to Associate in Project Management.<br /><br /></p>
<p>In these 5 days, the course unfolds the essential skills and knowledge required to excel as an associate project manager. We&rsquo;ll start by building strong fundamentals, we lay a strong foundation, gradually progressing to more complex concepts and practical applications. With LPC you learn about project predictive and adaptive approaches in project management, as well as business analysis frameworks, all that through interactive sessions, case studies, and group activities.<br /><br /></p>
<p>Join LPC for this transformative experience and elevate your professional capabilities in project management. This course will only prepare you to study for the PMI-CAPM.</p>',
                'duration' => '5',
            'days_content' => '["<p><strong>Introduction to Project Management</strong> <br /><br /></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>PMI Certified Associate in Project Management (CAPM)&reg; examination content outline</li>\\n<li>Defining project management and key related terms</li>\\n<li>Roles and responsibilities of a project managers</li>\\n<li>Understanding how to create value through project management</li>\\n<li>Fundamental principles of project management</li>\\n<li>Exploring challenges of project management</li>\\n<li>Interactive Q&amp;A and Discussion</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Project Performance &amp; Project Life Cycle</strong> <br /><br /></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Identifying and analyzing stakeholders</li>\\n<li>Exploring the structure of project organization</li>\\n<li>Discussing techniques to build effective project team</li>\\n<li>Understanding project life cycle and its component</li>\\n<li>Understanding the development approach and life cycle performance domain</li>\\n<li>Discussing techniques for selecting the best development approach</li>\\n<li>Identifying project activity, deliverables and milestones</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Predictive Approach<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Understanding the predictive methodology in project management</li>\\n<li>Discussing the process groups of predictive approach</li>\\n<li>Exploring how to develop project charter and project team</li>\\n<li>Steps to build project management plan</li>\\n<li>Understanding how to manage, monitor and control project work</li>\\n<li>Understanding the earned value analysis</li>\\n<li>Strategies to manage project communications</li>\\n<li>Strategies to manage risk, performance, and quality</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Adaptive Approach</strong> <br /><br /></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Understanding the adaptive approach in project management</li>\\n<li>Exploring the environment of adaptive approach and team structure</li>\\n<li>Identifying the stages of adaptive projects</li>\\n<li>Understanding the agile life cycle</li>\\n<li>Exploring different adaptive frameworks:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: square;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Lean</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Scrum</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Kanban</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Extreme programming</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;FDD, DSDM, and Crystal<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Discussing techniques to measure performance</li>\\n<li>Defining uncertainty in project management</li>\\n<li>Understanding how to tracking and managing risk in adaptive approaches</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Business Analysis</strong> <br /><br /></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Determining the significance of business analysis</li>\\n<li>Roles and responsibilities of business analyst</li>\\n<li>Understanding how to gather requirements for business analysis</li>\\n<li>The importance of engaging stockholders in business analysis</li>\\n<li>Determining the impact of project approach on business analysis</li>\\n<li>Exploring the business analysis domains:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: square;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Needs assessment</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Business analysis planning</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Requirements elicitation and analysis</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Traceability and monitoring</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Solution evaluation</li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Discussing the tailoring process of projects &nbsp;</li>\\n<li>Lessons Learned and Best Practices</li>\\n<li>Final Q&amp;A and Course Wrap-Up</li>\\n</ul>"]',
                'related_courses' => '[]',
                'category_id' => 44,
                'online' => 1,
                'created_at' => '2025-04-03 12:53:14',
                'updated_at' => '2025-04-03 12:53:14',
