            215 => 
            array (
                'id' => 2059,
                'lang_code' => 'en',
            'name' => 'Disciplined Agile Coach (DAC) Certification',
            'description' => '<p>Greetings and a warm welcome to the "Preparation Course Disciplined Agile Coach (DAC) Certification" course! Enhance your DA coaching skills with LPC through a transformative 5-day learning journey meticulously designed to equip you with tools and knowledge to achieve true agility by coaching teams across the enterprise. This course prepares you to successfully take the DASSM certification exam.<br /><br /></p>
<p>Over the next 5 days with LPC, we\'ll dive into the fundamental of DA coaching, providing a comprehensive understanding of its principles and processes. We\'ll discuss how to effectively implement and facilitate agile transformation process within an organization. Moving forward, we&rsquo;ll understand the importance of stakeholder engagement and continuous communication for agile transformation. By the end of this course, you\'ll be equipped to mentor, lead, guide transitions and coach individuals, teams, and groups of teams. You&rsquo;ll also gain skills to consult and counsel on agile practices.<br /><br /></p>
<p>Join us in this immersive learning experience, tailored by LPC, as we elevate coaching practices to new heights! Let&rsquo;s get started! This course will only prepare you to study for the DAC.</p>',
                'duration' => '5',
            'days_content' => '["<p><strong>Introduction to Disciplined Agile Coach (DAC)<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Disciplined Agile Coach (DAC) Certification content outline</li>\\n<li>Understanding the meaning and benefits of DA coach</li>\\n<li>Discussing the roles and responsibilities of DA coach</li>\\n<li>Exploring different DA toolkit that supports coaching</li>\\n<li>Understanding the different process goals</li>\\n<li>Understanding how to facilitate the DA way</li>\\n<li>Discussing how to plan and facilitate training, events and ceremonies</li>\\n<li>Techniques for developing ground-rules and facilitate collaboration</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Stakeholder Engagement &amp; Communication</strong></p>\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Discussing when and how to engage all stakeholders</li>\\n<li>Understanding steps required for effective transition to DA<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: square;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Analyzing the purpose and context of the transition</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Identify training needs and DA gaps</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Define metrics and approaches</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Develop roadmap and identify sponsors</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Brainstorming sessions<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Discussing the importance of communicating new vision, core concepts and change management to stakeholders</li>\\n<li>Discovering how to identify and sequence the initial initiatives</li>\\n<li>Understanding the importance of communication in demonstrating support for the organization</li>\\n<li>Discussing the key components of a successful community of practice</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Mentorship, Leadership &amp; Guided Transition</strong> <br /><br /></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Techniques for developing mentorships at individual levels</li>\\n<li>Methods for figuring out DA solutions</li>\\n<li>Discovering team building skills and knowledge:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: square;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Emotional intelligence skills and principles</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Communication skills</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Psychological safety</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Negotiation, problem solving and decision-making skills</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Active listening<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Determining the importance of encouraging collaboration within the organization</li>\\n<li>Discussing how to implement guided transition in the organization</li>\\n<li>Utilizing systems thinking to develop and review actions and experiments to the organization</li>\\n<li>Discussing how to facilitate organizational re-design and develop formal paths for change</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Coaching, Consulting, Counseling &amp; Lean Leadership<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Understanding the significance of identifying issues and their causes with working groups</li>\\n<li>Discussing how to understand personal emotional regulation and presence</li>\\n<li>Methods for flexibility and continuous adapt to situations</li>\\n<li>Understanding how to develop, integrate and tailor frameworks and toolkits</li>\\n<li>The benefits of explaining areas of improvements and benefits of solutions for clients</li>\\n<li>Discovering how to nurture the motivation techniques</li>\\n<li>Methods for a middle-up-down management approach</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Training &amp; Development<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Methods for creating an environment for continuous learning</li>\\n<li>Discussing how to develop formal learning outcomes and deliver content</li>\\n<li>The importance of identifying and socializing sources of information</li>\\n<li>Discussing how DA toolkit relates to other practices</li>\\n<li>Exploring DA challenges and how to overcome their challenges for improvement</li>\\n<li>Lessons Learned and Best Practices</li>\\n<li>Final Q&amp;A and Course Wrap-Up</li>\\n</ul>"]',
                'related_courses' => '[]',
                'category_id' => 44,
                'online' => 1,
                'created_at' => '2025-04-03 12:53:15',
                'updated_at' => '2025-04-03 12:53:15',
            ),
