            217 => 
            array (
                'id' => 2061,
                'lang_code' => 'en',
            'name' => 'Program Management Professional (PgMP)',
            'description' => '<p>A warm welcome to &ldquo;Program Management Professional (PgMP)&rdquo;! This exciting 5-day program is meticulously designed by LPC to well prepare you for PgMP exam and arm you with skills and knowledge of program management.<br /><br /></p>
<p>Over a 5-day period, you will embark on a learning journey, delving into the basics, terminology, and practical aspects of effective program management as described in the PMI Guide to Program Professional Management. With LPC, you&rsquo;ll a gain strong foundation in program management by learning program management principles and business value. You&rsquo;ll master program management performance domains: strategic alignment, benefits management, stakeholder engagement, governance framework, and collaboration. Additionally, you&rsquo;ll understand the program life cycle phases and activities associated with each phase.<br /><br /></p>
<p>Are you ready to enhance your program management skills? Join LPC for this transformative experience and elevate your professional capabilities in program management. This course will only prepare you to study for the PMI-PgMP.</p>',
                'duration' => '5',
            'days_content' => '["<p><strong>Introduction to Program Management</strong></p>\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>PMI Program Management Professional (PgMP)&reg; examination content outline</li>\\n<li>Introduction to PMI and PgMP certification</li>\\n<li>Defining program management and key related terms</li>\\n<li>Exploring the roles and responsibilities of a program manager</li>\\n<li>Understanding the relationship among organizational strategy, program management, portfolio management and operations management</li>\\n<li>Identifying the importance and techniques to create organizational business value</li>\\n<li>Discussing the principles of program management</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Domains of Program Management Performance</strong></p>\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Define program management performance domain</li>\\n<li>Understanding how to maintain strategic alignment in program management</li>\\n<li>Developing program charter</li>\\n<li>Program management plan and risk management strategy</li>\\n<li>Discussing the process of managing benefits in program management</li>\\n<li>Understanding how collaboration leads to program success</li>\\n<li>Discuss how program components and activists collaborate</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Domains of Program Management Performance<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Exploring how to maintain stockholder engagement</li>\\n<li>Techniques to identify and analyze stakeholders</li>\\n<li>Discussing techniques for effective communication with stakeholders</li>\\n<li>Understanding program governance framework and its significance</li>\\n<li>Techniques to design and implement management governance</li>\\n<li>Overview of program life cycle phases:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: square;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Program definition phase</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Program delivery phase</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Program closure phase</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Program Definition and Delivery Phases&rsquo; Activities<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Program integration management and infrastructure development</li>\\n<li>Program formulation phases and activities</li>\\n<li>Program change management</li>\\n<li>Program communication management</li>\\n<li>Program financial management</li>\\n<li>Program information management</li>\\n<li>Program procurement management</li>\\n<li>Program quality management</li>\\n<li>Program resources management</li>\\n<li>Program scope management</li>\\n<li>Program schedule management</li>\\n<li>Program risk management</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Program Closure Phase&rsquo;s Activities<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Program financial closer</li>\\n<li>Program information archiving and transition</li>\\n<li>Program procurement closure</li>\\n<li>Program resource transition</li>\\n<li>Program risk management transition</li>\\n<li>Lessons learned and best practices</li>\\n<li>Final Q&amp;A and course wrap-up</li>\\n<li>Simulated exam</li>\\n</ul>"]',
