            219 => 
            array (
                'id' => 2063,
                'lang_code' => 'en',
            'name' => 'PMI Agile Certified Practitioner (PMI-ACP)',
            'description' => '<p>Welcomes to the “PMI Agile Certified Practitioner (PMI-ACP)”. This 5-days intensive program is expertly designed by LPC to equip you with essential skills and knowledge to excel in Agile project environment and successfully pass the PMI-ACP exam.</p><p><br></p><p>Agile frameworks have transformed the landscape of project management, emphasizing flexibility, collaboration and focus on delivering value to customers. By obtaining the PMI-ACP certificate, you’ll be able to proof your proficiency in Agile principles and practices.</p><p><br></p><p>Over a span of 5 days with LPC, you’ll embark on a learning journey, exploring Agile concepts, techniques and practices. You’ll master Agile principles and frameworks such as Scrum, Kaban, Lean and others. You’ll learn strategies and techniques for managing and maintaining value driven delivery, stakeholder engagement, and high-performance team. Besides, you’ll explore how to develop adaptive planning strategies, manage risks and resolve issue, as well as adapting continuous improvement.</p><p><br></p><p>With LPC, you’ll attend interactive lectures, participate in group activities and discussions, and analyze various case studies in order to reinforce key concepts and prepare you for the PMI-ACP exam. Join LPC for this transformative experience and elevate your Agile skills. This course will only prepare you to study for the PMI-CAPM.</p>',
                'duration' => '5',
            'days_content' => '["<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\\">An Introduction to Agile&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">PMI Agile Certified Practitioner (PMI-ACP) ® examination content outline</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Distinguishing between definable work and high-uncertainty work</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Understanding the Agile manifesto and mindset</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Understanding the benefits of Agile project management&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Exploring different Agile frameworks and methodologies:</span></li></ul><p><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">﻿</span></p><ul><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Kanban</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Lean&nbsp;</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Defining project uncertainty and risk and their impact on project lifecycle</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\\">Life Cycle Selection&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Describing the characteristics of project life cycles:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ul><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Predictive life cycle&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Iterative life cycle&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Incremental life cycle&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Agile life cycle&nbsp;</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Exploring different types of hybrid and combined project life cycles and their characteristics&nbsp;</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ul><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Combined Agile and predictive approaches&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Predominantly predictive approach with some Agile components&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">A largely Agile approach with a predictive component&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Hybrid life cycles at fit-for-purpose</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Hybrid life cycles as a transition strategy&nbsp;</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Discussing the selection of an appropriate project life cycle&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Discovering methods for mixing Agile approaches&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Analyzing project factors impacting the tailoring of project attributes</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\\">Implementing Agile: Creating an Agile Environment&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Introduction to the process of creating an Agile environment&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Recognizing the role of the Agile mindset in building an Agile environment&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Identifying the benefits of servant leadership in Empowering Agile team&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Exploring the Responsibility and role of servant Leaders and project managers in an Agile environment&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Describing team composition and structure&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Determining the characteristics of Agile teams</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\\">Implementing Agile: Delivering in an Agile Environment&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Understanding the process of charting the project and the team&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Discovering common Agile practices:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ul><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Retrospectives&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Backlog preparation&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Backlog refinement&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Daily standups&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Demonstration/ Reviews&nbsp;</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Understanding the planning process for iteration-based Agile&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Exploring execution practices helps teams deliver value&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Identifying the role of interaction and increments in delivering work product&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Discussing troubleshooting strategies for Agile project challenges</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Exploring measurement techniques in Agile projects</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\\">Organizational Considerations for Project Agility&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Discussing change management drivers and methods for managing changes&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Strategies for assessing and building organizational culture&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Best practices for managing procurement and contracts&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Discussing business practices for organizational agility&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Understanding multiteam coordination and dependencies in projects&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Discussing the interaction between Agile and the project management office (PMO)&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Identifying the characteristics of organizational structure&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Lessons Learned and Best Practices</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Final Q&amp;A and Course Wrap-Up</span></li></ul>"]',
