            233 => 
            array (
                'id' => 2079,
                'lang_code' => 'en',
                'name' => 'Advance Warehousing Management',
                'description' => '<p>Welcome to LPC\'s comprehensive course on &ldquo;Advance Warehousing Management Program&rdquo;! This engaging 5-day journey, brought to you by LPC, is designed to equip you with cutting-edge strategies and technologies essential for optimizing warehouse operations.</p>
<p>Your journey will LPC begin with diving deep into the fundamentals of advanced warehouse management, including functions, characteristics, and benefits of advanced warehouse management, components of warehouse management, and supply chain integration. Then, we&rsquo;ll focus on warehouse layout and design, where you&rsquo;ll gain expertise to select warehouse locations, utilize advanced design technology, and optimize the layout. Besides, you&rsquo;ll gain a comprehensive understanding of advanced inventory management strategies, as well as how to process orders effectively to gain customer satisfaction. You&rsquo;ll master risk management and assessment techniques in warehouses, and develop risk mitigation strategies while ensuring compliance with international and national warehouse regulations and standards. Lastly, we&rsquo;ll discuss KPIs for measuring warehouse efficiency and labor productivity, strategies to manage and motivate the warehouse team, as well as how to apply warehouse lean principles to foster a culture of continuous improvement within the organization.</p>
<p>By the conclusion of this course, you will emerge equipped with a deep understanding of the latest warehouse management practices and well-prepared to drive operational excellence and customer satisfaction. So, let\'s embark on this journey together toward mastering Advanced Warehouse Management tools and techniques with LPC!</p>',
                'duration' => '5',
            'days_content' => '["<p><strong>Fundamentals of Warehousing Management</strong><br /><br /></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Function of warehouse of warehouse management</li>\\n<li>Key components of warehouse management:</li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>Inventory management</li>\\n<li>Order processing</li>\\n<li>&nbsp;Warehouse layout and design</li>\\n<li>Labor management</li>\\n<li>Technology integration</li>\\n</ul>\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Introduction to advanced warehouse technologies and techniques</li>\\n<li>&nbsp;Characteristics of advanced warehouse management</li>\\n<li>Benefits of adopting advanced warehouse management system</li>\\n<li>Discussing the integration of supply chain forecasting with warehouse functions</li>\\n<li>Techniques for managing export and import logistics</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Warehouse Layout &amp; Design</strong><br /><br /></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Methods for selecting warehouse location</li>\\n<li>Principles of warehouse layout</li>\\n<li>Technologies for designing warehouse:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>Warehouse management systems (WMS)</li>\\n<li>Slotting optimization</li>\\n<li>3D warehouse design software<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Factors affect warehouse design and layout</li>\\n<li>Discussing warehouse design and layout consideration aspects</li>\\n<li>Techniques for optimizing warehouse layout</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Advanced Inventory Management<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Classifying inventories based on multiple dimensions</li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>Methods for inventory management:</li>\\n<li>ABC analysis</li>\\n<li>Just-in-Time (JIT)</li>\\n<li>&nbsp;Safety stock</li>\\n<li>Cycle counting</li>\\n</ul>\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Advanced technologies to track and control inventory:</li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>Barcode inventory system</li>\\n<li>Radio-frequency identification (RFID)</li>\\n<li>Bin location systems</li>\\n<li>Perpetual inventory system</li>\\n<li>Periodical inventory system</li>\\n</ul>\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Understanding how to manage work-in-process (WIP) inventory</li>\\n<li>Understanding the role of effective order process in customer satisfaction<br /><br /></li>\\n<li>Discussing picking strategies for efficient order processing:</li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>Single order picking</li>\\n<li>Batch picking</li>\\n<li>&nbsp;Zone picking</li>\\n<li>&nbsp;Wave picking</li>\\n</ul>\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Discussing how order processing can be automated</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Importance of conducting warehouse risk assessment</strong><br /><br /></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Warehouse risk management techniques and tools</li>\\n<li>Understanding how to preserve equipment and inventory in warehouses</li>\\n<li>Common risks areas in warehouse management:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>Physical security of premises</li>\\n<li>&nbsp;Staff security systems</li>\\n<li>&nbsp;External contractors management</li>\\n<li>Financial and process risks</li>\\n<li>Health and safety risks<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Steps for creating risk mitigation strategy and urgency respond</li>\\n<li>Discussing the role of regular inventory management auditing in identifying and resolving discrepancies between recorded and actual stock levels</li>\\n<li>Exploring warehouse health and safety protocols and regulations</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Key KPIs to measure warehouse activities performance</strong><br /><br /></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Exploring metrics to measure labor productivity</li>\\n<li>Discussing inventory KPIs in warehouse</li>\\n<li>Principles of lean warehouse:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>Kaizen</li>\\n<li>5S methodology</li>\\n<li>Just-in-Time (JIT)<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Understanding 80/20 rule and &ldquo;your next customer&rdquo; concept</li>\\n<li>Techniques for motiving warehouse team member</li>\\n<li>The importance of providing workforce training for warehouse success</li>\\n<li>Exploring techniques to manage performance when things go wrong</li>\\n</ul>"]',
