            237 => 
            array (
                'id' => 2083,
                'lang_code' => 'en',
                'name' => 'Product Analytics & Metrics',
                'description' => '<p>Welcome to " Product Analytics &amp; Metrics" course! This immersive journey was designed with care by LPC to help you boost your product expansion with data-driven decisions by mastering the essentials of product analytics and metrics.<br /><br /></p>
<p>During 5 days, LPC instructors will guide you step-by step to fully understand the fundamentals of product analytics and implement its strategies and techniques to effectively analyze your data during all the stages of product development. You&rsquo;ll learn about the process of product analytics, data types and metrics. You&rsquo;ll master the advanced techniques of product analytics including customer segmentation, cohort analysis, retention analysis and funnel analysis. Not only that, we&rsquo;ll also discuss product experimentation and how to use A/B testing for your product.<br /><br /></p>
<p>By the end of this comprehensive course, you&rsquo;ll be well-equipped to make informed decisions and drive product success. Join us and unlock the full potential of Product Analytics with LPC!</p>',
                'duration' => '5',
            'days_content' => '["<p><strong>Introduction to Product Analytics<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Defining product analytics and its significance in product management</li>\\n<li>Understanding the process of product analytics and what should be completed at each stage:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Creating questions based on product goal</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Mapping user journeys</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Identifying key user events and related data</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Creating a data governance framework</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Selecting KPIs and metrics</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Reporting the analytics results<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Differentiating between predictive analytics and prescriptive analytics</li>\\n<li>Discovering the common analytics frameworks for structuring the analysis:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Pirate Metrics Framework (AARRR)</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Retention-First Framework (RARRA)<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Determining the importance of developing measurable products</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Data &amp; Metrics<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Identifying the types of product data:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Source-aligned data products</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Consumer-aligned data products</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Aggregated data products<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Distinguishing between transactional data and behavioral data</li>\\n<li>Exploring different data collection methods and best practices</li>\\n<li>Defining product metrics and its types:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Lagging indicator</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Leading indicator<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Overview of metrics categories based on user lifecycle:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Acquisition metrics</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Activation metrics</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <!--[endif]-->Engagement metrics</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Retention metrics</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Monetization metrics</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; North Star metrics</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Product Analytics Techniques<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Defining customer segmentation analysis and cohort analysis</li>\\n<li>Understanding customer lifetime value (CLV) metrics to identify high-value customer segments</li>\\n<li>Describing the Customer Segmentation RFM Analysis</li>\\n<li>Exploring the types of cohort analysis:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>Acquisition cohorts</li>\\n<li>Behavioral cohorts<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Describing how cohort analysis is used to increase retention and decrease churn</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Product Analytics Techniques<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Defining retention analysis and funnel analysis</li>\\n<li>Exploring Retention metrics:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Retention Rate</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Repeat Purchase Rate</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Churn Rate</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Aha Moment<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Understanding the Funnel analysis including:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Conversion and drop-off rates</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Segmentation and analytical techniques</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Funnel optimization<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Understanding the North Star metric and how it works for guiding the team</li>\\n<li>Utilizing KPI trees to visualize the relationship between KPI and business goals</li>\\n</ul>","<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n<p><strong>Product Experimentation &amp; Analytics Best Practices<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Understanding the meaning of product experimentation and scientific method</li>\\n<li>Exploring the techniques to design effective A/B testing</li>\\n<li>Discussing factors to consider when interpreting A/B testing results<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Sample size</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Test duration</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Conversion rate</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Internal and external factors</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Significance level<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Discussing the essential aspects of a data governance process for product analytics</li>\\n<li>Exploring the best practices to implement the data-driven culture within the product team &nbsp;&nbsp;</li>\\n</ul>\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>"]',
                'related_courses' => '[]',
                'category_id' => 52,
                'online' => 1,
                'created_at' => '2025-04-03 12:53:22',
                'updated_at' => '2025-04-03 12:53:22',
            ),
            238 => 
            array (
                'id' => 2084,
                'lang_code' => 'en',
                'name' => 'Product Analytics & Metrics',
                'description' => '<p>Welcome to " Product Analytics &amp; Metrics" course! This immersive journey was designed with care by LPC to help you boost your product expansion with data-driven decisions by mastering the essentials of product analytics and metrics.<br /><br /></p>
<p>During 5 days, LPC instructors will guide you step-by step to fully understand the fundamentals of product analytics and implement its strategies and techniques to effectively analyze your data during all the stages of product development. You&rsquo;ll learn about the process of product analytics, data types and metrics. You&rsquo;ll master the advanced techniques of product analytics including customer segmentation, cohort analysis, retention analysis and funnel analysis. Not only that, we&rsquo;ll also discuss product experimentation and how to use A/B testing for your product.<br /><br /></p>
<p>By the end of this comprehensive course, you&rsquo;ll be well-equipped to make informed decisions and drive product success. Join us and unlock the full potential of Product Analytics with LPC!</p>',
                'duration' => '5',
            'days_content' => '["<p><strong>Introduction to Product Analytics<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Defining product analytics and its significance in product management</li>\\n<li>Understanding the process of product analytics and what should be completed at each stage:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Creating questions based on product goal</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Mapping user journeys</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Identifying key user events and related data</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Creating a data governance framework</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Selecting KPIs and metrics</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Reporting the analytics results<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Differentiating between predictive analytics and prescriptive analytics</li>\\n<li>Discovering the common analytics frameworks for structuring the analysis:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Pirate Metrics Framework (AARRR)</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Retention-First Framework (RARRA)<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Determining the importance of developing measurable products</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Data &amp; Metrics<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Identifying the types of product data:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Source-aligned data products</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Consumer-aligned data products</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Aggregated data products<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Distinguishing between transactional data and behavioral data</li>\\n<li>Exploring different data collection methods and best practices</li>\\n<li>Defining product metrics and its types:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Lagging indicator</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Leading indicator<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Overview of metrics categories based on user lifecycle:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Acquisition metrics</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Activation metrics</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <!--[endif]-->Engagement metrics</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Retention metrics</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Monetization metrics</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; North Star metrics</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Product Analytics Techniques<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Defining customer segmentation analysis and cohort analysis</li>\\n<li>Understanding customer lifetime value (CLV) metrics to identify high-value customer segments</li>\\n<li>Describing the Customer Segmentation RFM Analysis</li>\\n<li>Exploring the types of cohort analysis:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>Acquisition cohorts</li>\\n<li>Behavioral cohorts<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Describing how cohort analysis is used to increase retention and decrease churn</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Product Analytics Techniques<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Defining retention analysis and funnel analysis</li>\\n<li>Exploring Retention metrics:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Retention Rate</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Repeat Purchase Rate</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Churn Rate</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Aha Moment<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Understanding the Funnel analysis including:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Conversion and drop-off rates</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Segmentation and analytical techniques</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Funnel optimization<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Understanding the North Star metric and how it works for guiding the team</li>\\n<li>Utilizing KPI trees to visualize the relationship between KPI and business goals</li>\\n</ul>","<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n<p><strong>Product Experimentation &amp; Analytics Best Practices<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Understanding the meaning of product experimentation and scientific method</li>\\n<li>Exploring the techniques to design effective A/B testing</li>\\n<li>Discussing factors to consider when interpreting A/B testing results<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Sample size</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Test duration</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Conversion rate</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Internal and external factors</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Significance level<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Discussing the essential aspects of a data governance process for product analytics</li>\\n<li>Exploring the best practices to implement the data-driven culture within the product team &nbsp;&nbsp;</li>\\n</ul>\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>"]',
                'related_courses' => '[]',
                'category_id' => 52,
                'online' => 0,
                'created_at' => '2025-04-03 12:53:22',
                'updated_at' => '2025-04-03 12:53:22',
            ),
            239 => 
            array (
                'id' => 2085,
                'lang_code' => 'en',
                'name' => 'Understanding the Customer & Market',
                'description' => '<p>Welcome to " Understanding Customer &amp; Market&rdquo; course! This course is designed by LPC to guide participants through the essential steps of aligning your product with market needs.<br /><br /></p>
<p>Throughout this interesting journey, you&rsquo;ll explore the world of product-market fit with LPC instructors. You&rsquo;ll dive understand the core concepts of product-market fit and its significance in developing a product. Then, you&rsquo;ll gain a comprehensive insight about customer as you&rsquo;ll learn how to determine your target audience and their needs. As we progress, you&rsquo;ll master the skills and techniques of designing compelling value propositions and developing feature sets that attract your customers. Finally, you&rsquo;ll learn the importance of user testing for improving your product-market fit and decide on what steps should be taken further.<br /><br /></p>
<p>Once you complete the course, you&rsquo;ll be armed with skills and knowledge to test and refine your product to ensure it meets the demands of your customers and stands out in the competitive market.<br /><br /></p>
<p>Enroll now and join LPC in this transformative experience to elevate your products to new heights.</p>',
                'duration' => '5',
            'days_content' => '["<p><strong>Product-Market Fit<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Defining product-market fit</li>\\n<li>Determining the importance of achieving product-market fit</li>\\n<li>Understanding the product-market pyramid</li>\\n<li>Familiarizing with technology adoption life cycle</li>\\n<li>Exploring real-world examples of successful and failed products lunch</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Knowing Your Customers</strong> <br /><br /></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Defining customers, target customer, customers needs, and underserved customer needs</li>\\n<li>Techniques to understand customer needs:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Segmenting the market</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Creating customer persona<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Techniques for customer discovery:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Understanding customers&rsquo; pain points</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Interviewing</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Lo-fi testing</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Journey mapping<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>What is &ldquo;Jobs to be Done&rdquo; framework? And how does it work?</li>\\n<li>Implementing customer benefit ladder to identify key benefits of a product</li>\\n<li>Tools to gather customer requirements and turn it to a product:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; House of Quality</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Quality Function Development (QFD)</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Value Proposition &amp; Feature Set<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>What is value proposition?</li>\\n<li>How to build your value proposition</li>\\n<li>What is feature set and minimum viable product (MVP)?</li>\\n<li>Understanding the steps of deciding features<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Chunking</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Scoping</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Prioritizing</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Deciding on MVP<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Tips to design prototype and user testing to validate MVP</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>MVP Testing<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Differentiating between market testing and product testing</li>\\n<li>Identify the importance of testing MVP with customers</li>\\n<li>Types of user testing:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; In-person</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Virtual<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>How to structure the user test?</li>\\n<li>Tips to find users to test and writing good questions</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Iterative Improvement<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Differentiating between market testing and product testing</li>\\n<li>Designing metrics and KPIs to track product&rsquo;s success and measure product-market fit</li>\\n<li>When to preserve, pivot or quit?</li>\\n<li>Final project presentation</li>\\n<li>Course recap and Q&amp;A</li>\\n</ul>"]',
                'related_courses' => '[]',
                'category_id' => 52,
                'online' => 1,
                'created_at' => '2025-04-03 12:53:22',
                'updated_at' => '2025-04-03 12:53:22',
            ),
