<p>What you are waiting for? Enroll now in LPC&rsquo;s &ldquo;Product Leadership and Influence&rdquo; course and unlock your full potential as a product leader.</p>',
                'duration' => '5',
                'days_content' => '["<p><strong>Product Leadership &amp; Influence</strong> <br /><br /></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Defining product leadership, influence and the relationship between them</li>\\n<li>Analyzing common leadership styles:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Visionary leadership style</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Affiliative leadership style</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Democratic leadership style</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Coaching leadership style</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Pacesetting leadership style</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Coercive leadership style<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Discussing product leadership challenges</li>\\n<li>Tips to select and apply the right leadership approach</li>\\n<li>Understanding the behavioral change stairway model</li>\\n<li>Discussing factors that affect the ability to lead and influence others:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Capacity to empathize</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Expertise level</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Management support</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Product Team &amp; Stakeholders<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Tips to guide and build the product team:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Giving choice and time to learn</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Letting the team own the solution</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Interacting with the team<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Exploring ways to motive your team:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Develop mastery</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Encourage autonomy</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Enhance meaning and purpose<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Defining psychological safety and its role in influencing and motiving the team</li>\\n<li>Analyzing and selecting key stakeholders to build a stakeholder community</li>\\n<li>Techniques to engage and involve stakeholders in product discovery and delivery</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Goals Setting &amp; Decision Making<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Understanding the principles of product vision, strategy, and roadmap</li>\\n<li>Utilizing Roman&rsquo;s goal-setting framework to set goals that align with stakeholders and create product success</li>\\n<li>Determining the benefits of adopting collaborative decision-making</li>\\n<li>Exploring common decision rules and their advantages in making better decisions:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Decide after discussion</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Consensus</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Majority vote</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Delegate</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Decide W/O discussion<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Exploring the process of inclusive decision-making</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Conversations &amp; Feedback<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Defining Covey&rsquo;s listening levels</li>\\n<li>Determining the role of deep listening to understand people&rsquo;s needs and interests</li>\\n<li>Utilizing Roman&rsquo;s feedback framework for providing feedback</li>\\n<li>Determining the power of saying &ldquo;No&rdquo;</li>\\n<li>Discussing the role of storytelling in communication with stakeholders</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Negotiation &amp; Conflicts<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Defining conflicts within workplace</li>\\n<li>Understanding the Non-violent Communication framework for conflict resolving</li>\\n<li>Exploring different styles of negotiation:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Accommodating</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Avoiding</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Collaborating</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Competing</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Compromising<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Discussing the advantages and disadvantages of each negotiation style and determining when to use each</li>\\n<li>Utilizing both advocacy and enquiry to create shared solutions</li>\\n<li>Discovering common mistakes and wrong practices when dealing with conflicts</li>\\n</ul>"]',
