                'lang_code' => 'en',
            'name' => 'Certified Credit Risk Management (Preparation Course)',
                'description' => '<p>Greetings and welcom e to the " Certified Credit Risk Managem ent" course! We\' re excited to have you on board for this unique 5-day educational experience m eticulously designed by LPC. In recent decades, various financial crises have underscored the im portance of robust credit risk m anagem ent as a critical tool for ensuring the stability and profitability of financial institutions. This LPC course is designed to equip you with the knowledge and skills to effectively assess, m anage, m itigate, and control credit risk. For 5 im m ersive days, you&rsquo;ll dive deep into the credit risk m anagem ent process, exploring various tools, techniques, and strategies for effective m anagem ent through the entire lending process. With LPC, you&rsquo;ll learn advanced credit risk analysis and assessm ent techniques enabling you to evaluate the im pact of credit risk events on banks and financial institutions. You\' ll also explore strategies for credit risk m itigation and transfer, focusing on m ethods to elim inate or reduce exposure to credit risk. Besides, you&rsquo;ll gain expertise in m anaging portfolio credit risk through identifying com m on risks and understanding their im pacts. We&rsquo;ll guide you through the steps of stress testing to assess the resilience of credit risk in your portfolio. By the end of this course, you\' ll have a com prehensive understanding of best practices in credit risk m anagem ent and hands-on experience in developing and im plem enting effective credit risk m anagem ent strategies. Join LPC in this engaging learning experience as we, navigate the com plexities of credit risk m anagem ent together, and prepare you to tackle its challenges with confidence</p>',
                'duration' => '5',
            'days_content' => '["<p><strong>Fundamentals of Credit Risk Management<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Overview of the course&rsquo;s objective and outlines</li>\\n<li>Understanding the meaning and types of credit risk</li>\\n<li>Understanding the 6 C&rsquo;s of credit</li>\\n<li>Overview of credit risk management process</li>\\n<li>Discussing credit risk management regulatory frameworks</li>\\n<li>Discussing the impact of credit risk in project finance and working capital</li>\\n<li>Case study: historical credit risk events</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Credit Risk Analysis &amp; Assessment<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Understanding financial statements analysis:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Balance sheets</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Income statements</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Cash flow statements<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Exploring qualitative and quantitative credit risk assessment methods</li>\\n<li>Techniques for estimating credit losses:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Probability of default (PD)</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Exposure at default (EAD)</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Loss given default (LEG)<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Understanding the fundamentals of scoring and rating systems in credit risk assessment</li>\\n<li>Discussing rating methodologies</li>\\n<li>Calculating credit risk exposure and strategies to manage the exposure</li>\\n<li>Methods for calculating credit risk:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Value-at-Risk (VaR) analysis</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Scenario analysis<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Best practices for structuring loans and reviewing loan documentation</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Credit Risk Mitigation &amp; Transfer<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Discussing credit risk mitigation strategies:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Credit enhancement</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Guarantees</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Covenants<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Understanding the role of collateralization in credit risk mitigation</li>\\n<li>Exploring the meaning and role of credit derivatives in credit risk management</li>\\n<li>Understanding the impact of securitization on credit risk transfer</li>\\n<li>Exploring covenant formulas and using them for mitigating credit risk</li>\\n<li>Tools to mitigate credit risk:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Credit insurance</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Surety of credit</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Letters of credit<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Discussing regulatory frameworks of credit risk management</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Portfolio Management &amp; Stress Testing<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Exploring common portfolio credit risks and their impact on diversification</li>\\n<li>Strategies to mitigate portfolio credit risks:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Diversification</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Collateral</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Securities<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Discussing the role of stress testing in credit risk</li>\\n<li>Exploring stress testing methods:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Backtesting using historical data</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Stress testing using hypothetical returns</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Principle components analysis<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Understanding the Basel III accord and its implication for capital adequacy</li>\\n<li>Distinguishing between credit risk pricing in non-financial and financial institutions</li>\\n<li>Exploring credit risk management practices in banking&nbsp;</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Challenges &amp; Best Practices<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Discussing best practices for managing credit risk in a corporate environment</li>\\n<li>Exploring the challenges and obstacles to credit risk management</li>\\n<li>Identifying post-lending problems and discovering strategies to handle them:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Financial distress</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Bankruptcy<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Exploring credit risk management technologies</li>\\n<li>Discussing the impact of emerging trends on credit risk management:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Fintech</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Climate change<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Simulation exercise of a credit risk crisis scenario</li>\\n<li>Lesson learned and best practices</li>\\n<li>Recap and course evaluation</li>\\n</ul>"]',
                'related_courses' => '[]',
                'category_id' => 34,
                'online' => 1,
                'created_at' => '2025-04-03 12:53:28',
                'updated_at' => '2025-04-03 12:53:28',
            ),
            260 => 
            array (
                'id' => 2106,
                'lang_code' => 'en',
            'name' => 'Certified Credit Risk Management (Preparation Course)',
                'description' => '<p>Greetings and welcom e to the " Certified Credit Risk Managem ent" course! We\' re excited to have you on board for this unique 5-day educational experience m eticulously designed by LPC. In recent decades, various financial crises have underscored the im portance of robust credit risk m anagem ent as a critical tool for ensuring the stability and profitability of financial institutions. This LPC course is designed to equip you with the knowledge and skills to effectively assess, m anage, m itigate, and control credit risk. For 5 im m ersive days, you&rsquo;ll dive deep into the credit risk m anagem ent process, exploring various tools, techniques, and strategies for effective m anagem ent through the entire lending process. With LPC, you&rsquo;ll learn advanced credit risk analysis and assessm ent techniques enabling you to evaluate the im pact of credit risk events on banks and financial institutions. You\' ll also explore strategies for credit risk m itigation and transfer, focusing on m ethods to elim inate or reduce exposure to credit risk. Besides, you&rsquo;ll gain expertise in m anaging portfolio credit risk through identifying com m on risks and understanding their im pacts. We&rsquo;ll guide you through the steps of stress testing to assess the resilience of credit risk in your portfolio. By the end of this course, you\' ll have a com prehensive understanding of best practices in credit risk m anagem ent and hands-on experience in developing and im plem enting effective credit risk m anagem ent strategies. Join LPC in this engaging learning experience as we, navigate the com plexities of credit risk m anagem ent together, and prepare you to tackle its challenges with confidence</p>',
                'duration' => '5',
            'days_content' => '["<p><strong>Fundamentals of Credit Risk Management<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Overview of the course&rsquo;s objective and outlines</li>\\n<li>Understanding the meaning and types of credit risk</li>\\n<li>Understanding the 6 C&rsquo;s of credit</li>\\n<li>Overview of credit risk management process</li>\\n<li>Discussing credit risk management regulatory frameworks</li>\\n<li>Discussing the impact of credit risk in project finance and working capital</li>\\n<li>Case study: historical credit risk events</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Credit Risk Analysis &amp; Assessment<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Understanding financial statements analysis:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Balance sheets</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Income statements</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Cash flow statements<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Exploring qualitative and quantitative credit risk assessment methods</li>\\n<li>Techniques for estimating credit losses:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Probability of default (PD)</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Exposure at default (EAD)</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Loss given default (LEG)<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Understanding the fundamentals of scoring and rating systems in credit risk assessment</li>\\n<li>Discussing rating methodologies</li>\\n<li>Calculating credit risk exposure and strategies to manage the exposure</li>\\n<li>Methods for calculating credit risk:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Value-at-Risk (VaR) analysis</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Scenario analysis<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Best practices for structuring loans and reviewing loan documentation</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Credit Risk Mitigation &amp; Transfer<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Discussing credit risk mitigation strategies:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Credit enhancement</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Guarantees</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Covenants<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Understanding the role of collateralization in credit risk mitigation</li>\\n<li>Exploring the meaning and role of credit derivatives in credit risk management</li>\\n<li>Understanding the impact of securitization on credit risk transfer</li>\\n<li>Exploring covenant formulas and using them for mitigating credit risk</li>\\n<li>Tools to mitigate credit risk:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Credit insurance</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Surety of credit</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Letters of credit<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Discussing regulatory frameworks of credit risk management</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Portfolio Management &amp; Stress Testing<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Exploring common portfolio credit risks and their impact on diversification</li>\\n<li>Strategies to mitigate portfolio credit risks:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Diversification</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Collateral</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Securities<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Discussing the role of stress testing in credit risk</li>\\n<li>Exploring stress testing methods:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Backtesting using historical data</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Stress testing using hypothetical returns</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Principle components analysis<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Understanding the Basel III accord and its implication for capital adequacy</li>\\n<li>Distinguishing between credit risk pricing in non-financial and financial institutions</li>\\n<li>Exploring credit risk management practices in banking&nbsp;</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Challenges &amp; Best Practices<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Discussing best practices for managing credit risk in a corporate environment</li>\\n<li>Exploring the challenges and obstacles to credit risk management</li>\\n<li>Identifying post-lending problems and discovering strategies to handle them:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Financial distress</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Bankruptcy<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Exploring credit risk management technologies</li>\\n<li>Discussing the impact of emerging trends on credit risk management:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Fintech</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Climate change<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Simulation exercise of a credit risk crisis scenario</li>\\n<li>Lesson learned and best practices</li>\\n<li>Recap and course evaluation</li>\\n</ul>"]',
                'related_courses' => '[]',
