            264 => 
            array (
                'id' => 2110,
                'lang_code' => 'en',
            'name' => 'Oil Spills (IMO): Level 1- First Respond',
                'description' => '<p>Oil spills might pose significant threats to the environment, human health, and even natural resources. The impact of these spills varies depending on the oil\'s type and properties, as well as the surrounding environmental conditions. When oil spills occur, response organizations must work quickly and effectively to mitigate the damage, protect both the environment and public health, and avoid further hazards. The first response to oil spills requires thorough preparation and a strategic understanding of various challenges that might arise. Adhering to world-best practices and frameworks will ensure the success and efficiency of the response. This LPC training course serves as your guide to understanding the strategic first responses to oil spills. Participants will gain a deep understanding of all aspects of oil spill response, including properties and fate of oil, health and safety regulations, and environmental aspects. The course also covers the development of a continuity plan to respond to oil spills and prepare your team and organizations for such incidents. The curriculum of this course is designed to guide you through the entire phase of strategic planning including monitoring and evaluation, containment and recovery, shoreline cleanup, and post-incident practices. With both theoretical knowledge and practical application, you&rsquo;ll be well-prepared as a first responder to manage and respond to oil spills effectively whenever they occur.</p>',
                'duration' => '5',
                'days_content' => '["<p><strong>Introduction to Oil Spills<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Defining oil spills and key related terms</li>\\n<li>Identifying the sources of oil spills</li>\\n<li>Exploring the properties, behavior and fate of oil spills</li>\\n<li>Distinguishing between the properties of different oil types</li>\\n<li>Discussing the impact of oil spills</li>\\n<li>Discussing environmental concerns in spill response</li>\\n<li>Exploring health and safety regulations and standards related to oil spills</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Response Strategies to Oil Spills</strong><br /><br /></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Overview of the response strategies to oil spills<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Monitoring and evaluation</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Containment and recovery</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Shoreline cleanup<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Techniques for developing contingency plan for effective spill response</li>\\n<li>Understanding the structure of the incident response organization</li>\\n<li>Understand how to activate and mobilize the response teams and organization</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Monitoring &amp; Evaluating Oil Spills<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Techniques for assessing the risk of oil spills</li>\\n<li>Exploring oil spills equipment for surveillance and tracking</li>\\n<li>Strategies for predicting oil movement</li>\\n<li>Strategies for quantify spillage size and volume</li>\\n<li>Site Safety assessment and briefing techniques</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Oil Spills Containment &amp; Recovery<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Exploring types of containment booms and how they work</li>\\n<li>Discussing how to select the appropriate containment booms</li>\\n<li>Overview of oil spill recovery equipment</li>\\n<li>Exploring types of oil skimmers and how to utilize them</li>\\n<li>Understanding how dispersants are used for oil spills</li>\\n<li>Discussing the advantages and disadvantages of dispersants</li>\\n<li>Discovering absorbing materials used to absorb oil during spill response</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Oil Spills Shoreline &amp; Post-Incident Management<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Techniques for shoreline cleanup oil spills</li>\\n<li>Exploring cleaning, maintenance and storage equipment</li>\\n<li>Understanding the procedures for safety storing and transportation of recovered oil</li>\\n<li>Discussing strategies for storage and disposal of recovered oil and waste</li>\\n<li>Understanding the procedures for oil sampling and documentation</li>\\n<li>Discussing the techniques of cost recovery</li>\\n<li>Tips for managing media and public awareness</li>\\n<li>Course recap &amp; evaluation</li>\\n</ul>"]',
                'related_courses' => '[]',
                'category_id' => 17,
                'online' => 0,
                'created_at' => '2025-04-03 12:53:29',
                'updated_at' => '2025-04-03 12:53:29',
            ),
            265 => 
            array (
                'id' => 2111,
                'lang_code' => 'en',
                'name' => 'OKRs Goal Setting 101',
                'description' => '<p>Goals direct our actions and provide clear direction by identifying tasks to be done within a specific timeline for specific purposes. In a business context, setting goals serves as a powerful tool to motivate employees and keep them on track, ensuring accountability, productivity, and efficiency. However, setting appropriate goals is not always an easy task as they need to be aligned with the team. OKRs or &ldquo;Objectives and Key Results&rdquo; are a goal-setting tool used by the world&rsquo;s leading organizations to develop appropriate goals and define milestones to achieve them. OKRs are effective for monitoring progress, fostering alignment, and encouraging participation to achieve these goals. LPC has created this engaging course to equip you with skills and knowledge to set and implement OKRs within your organization. The curriculum covers the fundamentals of goal setting and OKRs, the OKR process, OKRs in leadership and management, and techniques for measuring and updating OKRs. By taking this course, participants will learn to set quality objectives and key results, utilize OKRs to lead and manage teams, measure OKRs and update them as needed.</p>',
                'duration' => '5',
                'days_content' => '["<p><strong>Introduction to Goal Setting<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Overview of course objectives and content</li>\\n<li>Understanding the importance of goal setting</li>\\n<li>Exploring types of goal setting approaches</li>\\n<li>Understanding common mistakes arise when defining goals</li>\\n<li>Introduction to OKRs</li>\\n<li>Discussing the different between OKRs and traditional goal-setting strategies</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Fundamentals of OKRs<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Defining OKRs and its key related terms</li>\\n<li>Exploring the history of OKRs</li>\\n<li>Understanding objectives and key results in OKRs</li>\\n<li>Understanding the benefits of implementing OKRs approach</li>\\n<li>Exploring types of OKRs:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Challenging/ Aspirational OKRs</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Committed OKRs<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Understanding the 70% challenge</li>\\n<li>Discussing the core elements of OKRs:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Definition</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Implementation</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Continuous measurement<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Examples of OKRs&nbsp;</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>OKRs Goals Setting Process<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>The process of setting goals based on OKRs</li>\\n<li>Exploring the golden rules of defining OKRs</li>\\n<li>Understanding how to connect objectives to purpose and profit</li>\\n<li>Understanding the inputs, outputs and outcomes of results</li>\\n<li>Tips for quality objectives and results</li>\\n<li>Exercise: write your objectives &amp; results</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>OKRs in Leadership &amp; Management<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Exploring OKRs alignment strategies</li>\\n<li>Discussing the benefits of using OKRs in leadership and management</li>\\n<li>Techniques for leading people using OKRs</li>\\n<li>Discussing how company OKRs are used and adopted by different departments</li>\\n<li>Discussing how to OKRs and SCRUM can be combined in job environment</li>\\n<li>Exploring the role of OKRs in managing performance</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>OKRs Tools &amp; Measurement<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Techniques for measuring OKRs</li>\\n<li>Understanding how and when to update OKRs</li>\\n<li>Exploring common mistakes in writing OKRs:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;OKRs is not BAU</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;OKRs vs. KPIs</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Sandbagging<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Exploring OKRs tools and software</li>\\n<li>Discussing the implementation of OKRs in daily tasks</li>\\n<li>Final project: develop final draft of OKRs</li>\\n<li>Presentation and feedback</li>\\n<li>Recap and course evaluation&nbsp;</li>\\n</ul>"]',
                'related_courses' => '[]',
                'category_id' => 17,
                'online' => 1,
                'created_at' => '2025-04-03 12:53:30',
                'updated_at' => '2025-04-03 12:53:30',
            ),
