            267 => 
            array (
                'id' => 2113,
                'lang_code' => 'en',
                'name' => 'Well Integrity, Well Services & Well Workover',
                'description' => '<p>In the oil and gas industry, it is crucial to maintain the safety, reliability, and efficiency of wells throughout their lifecycle. Well integrity involves controlling fluids within a well to prevent leaks or spills that could harm the environment. Well services and workover are activities conducted after drilling to optimize well performance, improve production, and mitigate risks. The loss of well integrity during well operations can have serious health, safety, and environmental consequences, as well as financial losses. Managing well integrity alongside well servicing and workover can enhance resource extraction efficiency while prioritizing safety, environmental, and health considerations. With LPC and during this comprehensive course, you&rsquo;ll dive delve into the fundaments of well integrity, services, and workover. This course is designed to provide you with skills and knowledge needed to maintain well operations within the safety parameters and follow industry best practices. Through lectures, engaging discussions, and real-world examples, you&rsquo;ll get the opportunity to learn about the tools, equipment, processes, and methods used for well integrity, serving, and workover.</p>',
                'duration' => '5',
            'days_content' => '["<p><strong>Introduction to Well Integrity<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Introduction to course content and objectives</li>\\n<li>Understanding the meaning of well integrity and its significance</li>\\n<li>Explore the historical evolution of well integrity practices</li>\\n<li>Overview of well lifecycle stages<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Design and construction</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Well operation and intervention</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Abandonment<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Discussing the consequences of well integrity failure and the importance of managing integrity throughout the well lifecycle</li>\\n<li>Discussing standards and regulations of well integrity</li>\\n<li>Real-world examples about well integrity failure&nbsp;</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Risk Awareness &amp; Barriers<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Discussing risks associated with completion and well intervention operations</li>\\n<li>Techniques for assessing the current status of the well</li>\\n<li>Understanding the philosophy and operation of barrier systems</li>\\n<li>Discussing the requirements of wall barriers</li>\\n<li>Identifying the importance of barriers for well completions and interventions</li>\\n<li>Discovering levels of barriers:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Primary barriers</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Secondary barriers<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Understanding types of barriers:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Mechanical barriers</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Fluid barriers<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Techniques for managing barriers:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Testing mechanical barriers</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Validating fluid barriers</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Detecting a failed barrier<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Understanding the fundamentals of pressure</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Well Services<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Defining well servicing and understand its significance in maintaining well integrity</li>\\n<li>Discovering types work done under well servicing:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Well interventions</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Well workover</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Inspections<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Understanding the operations of well servicing:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Wireline operations</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Subbing operations</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Coiled tubing operations</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Workover operations<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Discussing the role of well control in ensuring safe, reliable well servicing</li>\\n<li>Exploring equipment used in well servicing</li>\\n<li>Case study of successful well servicing</li>\\n<li>Simulation of well servicing techniques</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Well Workover<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Discussing the importance of well workover</li>\\n<li>Discussing reasons for work over</li>\\n<li>Understanding the operations and process of workover</li>\\n<li>Exploring workover operation techniques:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Wireline</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Pumping operations</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Coil tube and snubbing<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Exploring well workover tools and equipment</li>\\n<li>Understanding the purpose of workover fluids</li>\\n<li>Discussing types and properties of fluid:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Brines</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Gases</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Well Integrity Monitoring &amp; Testing<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Discussing the interrelationship between well integrity, well services and well workover</li>\\n<li>Exploring methods and tools for monitoring well integrity</li>\\n<li>Understanding well testing and acceptance criteria</li>\\n<li>Understanding management of change for well integrity</li>\\n<li>Discussing health, safety, and environmental (HSE) regulations</li>\\n<li>The importance of developing an emergency response plan</li>\\n<li>Best practices for well integrity, well services and well workover</li>\\n<li>Course evaluation and recap</li>\\n</ul>"]',
                'related_courses' => '[]',
                'category_id' => 17,
                'online' => 1,
                'created_at' => '2025-04-03 12:53:31',
                'updated_at' => '2025-04-03 12:53:31',
            ),
