            271 => 
            array (
                'id' => 2117,
                'lang_code' => 'en',
                'name' => 'Strategic Growth & Change',
                'description' => '<p>The main goal of every business strategy is to achieve a sustainable competitive advantage. This includes actively pursuing fresh prospects, initiating new projects, and guiding change and transformation efforts. High levels of uncertainty are associated with strategic growth and change, especially because of the fast-paced changes caused by global digital transformation. Dealing with this lack of certainty and achieving success can be accomplished by strategically planning and efficiently executing change in a company.<br /><br /></p>
<p>Abandon the traditional decision-making methods and adopt modern techniques to drive growth throughout this enriching journey designed by LPC. This course will equip you with the skills and knowledge to navigate and deal with uncertainty, grasp new opportunities, and lead changes.<br /><br /></p>
<p>Over the course of 5 days, you will learn to develop your new strategy playbook, create an opportunity portfolio for evaluating investments, align your strategy with customer expectations, conduct discovery-driven planning, adopt a positive politics approach, build mutually beneficial relationships, and develop a digital strategy.</p>',
                'duration' => '5',
                'days_content' => '["<p><strong>Introduction to Strategic Growth &amp; Change<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Introduction to course content and objectives</li>\\n<li>Defining strategic growth and change</li>\\n<li>Discussing the importance of strategic growth and change</li>\\n<li>Understanding the importance of innovation and transformation for competitive advantages</li>\\n<li>Understanding the ultimate goal of a strategy in business landscape</li>\\n<li>Exploring the evolving nature of competitive advantage</li>\\n<li>Discussing the role of transformation and innovation for sustainable competitive advantage</li>\\n<li>Discussing the fundamentals of new strategy playbook:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Agility &ndash; continuous reconfiguration</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Health disengagement</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Deft resource allocation</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; An innovation proficiency</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Discovery driven leadership</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Entrepreneurial careers</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Planning for Growth<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Understanding the significance of real options in strategic investment</li>\\n<li>Discussing how to manage uncertainty and create value through strategic resource allocation</li>\\n<li>Evaluating investment opportunities using opportunity portfolio:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Core business</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; New platforms positioning/ scouting</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Options positioning/ scouting</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Stepping stones<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Understanding the design thinking approach for creative solutions</li>\\n<li>Defining discovery driven planning and identifying its significance in tackling uncertainty and mitigate risk</li>\\n<li>The process of discovery driven planning:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Reversing success metrics in an income statement</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Evaluating the feasibility of the plan with the market</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Developing optional requirements</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Documenting and recording key assumptions and updating based on new insights</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Utilizing iterative checkpoints to progressively enhance knowledge<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Practical Exercise: Create an opportunity portfolio for growth</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Customer Insight<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Understanding the importance and objective of creating customer insight</li>\\n<li>Techniques for creating customer insight:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Behavior-based segmentation&nbsp;</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Customer journey mapping&nbsp;</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Customer offer tradeoffs analyzation&nbsp;<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Defining elements of choice&nbsp;</li>\\n<li>Discussing the impact of cognitive and emotional biases in decision-making&nbsp;</li>\\n<li>Exploring the elements of choice:<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Defaults</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Promising paths</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; The order and number of choices</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Other elements<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Case Studies about decision architectures&nbsp;</li>\\n<li>Practical Exercise: Developing customer insight&nbsp;</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Organizational Change<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Discussing the elements and characteristics of large-scale organizational transformation<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul style=\\"list-style-type: circle;\\">\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Assumptions</li>\\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Management in uncertain and volatile conditions<br /><br /></li>\\n</ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Analyzing the opportunities and challenges of organizational transformation</li>\\n<li>Understanding the meaning of positive politics and its significance in growth and change programs</li>\\n<li>Discussing how to assess political prospects</li>\\n<li>Exploring real world examples of organizational transformation</li>\\n</ul>","<p><strong>Network &amp; Strategy<br /><br /></strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Understanding how modern strategy operates within network ecosystems</li>\\n<li>Understanding complementary relationships and its significance in creating values</li>\\n<li>Discussing the effects of network and its limitation</li>\\n<li>Exploring the two sides of markets</li>\\n<li>Identifying the role of platform strategies in combining the two sides of a market</li>\\n<li>Differentiating between product business and platforms in term of interactions control</li>\\n<li>Discussing the impact of digital revolution on competition and value positioning</li>\\n<li>Discovering how to build a digital strategy for businesses</li>\\n<li>Lesson learnt and course review</li>\\n</ul>"]',
                'related_courses' => '[]',
                'category_id' => 41,
                'online' => 1,
                'created_at' => '2025-04-03 12:53:32',
                'updated_at' => '2025-04-03 12:53:32',
            ),
