hetic Principles </strong></p><p><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">&nbsp;</span></p><ul><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Understanding composition and framing </span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Composition techniques:</span></li></ul><p><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\"><span class=\\"ql-cursor\\">﻿</span></span></p><ol><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Leading lines</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Rule of thirds</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Symmetry</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Juxtaposition</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Exploring lighting techniques </span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Discussing how to ensure contrast in images</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">&nbsp;Understanding the Gestalt theory principles&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Understand the golden ration </span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Activity: practicing taking photos based on aesthetic principles&nbsp;</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: black;\\">Adobe Photoshop</strong></p><p><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">&nbsp;</span></p><ul><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Discussing the functions of Adobe Photoshop</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Navigating Adobe Photoshop interface </span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Utilizing Adobe Photoshop to edit and retouching photos</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Utilizing Adobe Photoshop to correct and enhance colors</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Exploring how to manipulate and composite images in Adobe Photoshop</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Discovering filters and effects in Adobe Photoshop</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Understanding how to use selection and masks functions </span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Activity: editing photos using Adobe Photoshop</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: black;\\">Photography Best Practices&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Discussing common mistakes in photography</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Exploring the characteristics of a sound photo </span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Discussing how to use photography for storytelling </span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Techniques for photo session planning </span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Exploring how to select the best camera and lenses </span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Final Project on telling stories through photography </span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Lesson learned and recap</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Course evaluation</span></li></ul>"]',
