            312 => 
            array (
                'id' => 2158,
                'lang_code' => 'en',
                'name' => 'Public Policy Challenges of the 21st Century',
                'description' => '<p>Public Policy is concerned with identifying and addressing collective problems. When societies change, it brings new challenges that need to be resolved. Sticking to old policies and refusing to reform them might cause further challenges and negative consequences.</p><p>The 21st century presents unique challenges that affect national and international public policies. Inequality, poverty, climate change, environmental sustainability, health care, migration, refugees, technological advancements, education, employment, terrorism, and many other challenges will be covered in the “Public Policy Challenges of the 21st Century” course.</p><p><br></p><p>This training course is designed to provide participants with a strong foundation in public policy by analyzing contemporary challenges and evaluating the impact of public policies on addressing them. Participants will understand the policy-making process at various levels and the role of advocacy in public relations. They\'ll also improve their skills in policy analysis and evaluation and develop their policy advocacy strategy throughout the course.</p>',
                'duration' => '5',
            'days_content' => '["<p><strong>Contemporary Public Policy Challenges</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li>Overview of contemporary public policy challenges</li><li>Economic inequality and poverty</li><li>Climate change and environmental sustainability</li><li>Health care and pandemics</li><li>Migration and refugee crises</li><li>Technological advancements and digital governance</li><li>Education and workforce development</li><li>Security and terrorism</li><li>Balancing national and global interests</li></ul>","<p><strong>Role of Public Policy in Addressing Global Issues</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li>Introduction to global public policy</li><li>Discussing the role of public policy in international cooperation</li><li>Discussing global health policies and international responses</li><li>Exploring climate policies and international agreements (e.g., Paris Agreement)</li><li>Exploring economic policies in a globalized world</li><li>Discovering social policies addressing global inequality</li><li>Discussing human rights and global governance</li><li>Case studies of successful global policy interventions</li></ul>","<p><strong>Policy Analysis and Evaluation</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li>Introduction to policy analysis</li><li>Frameworks and models for policy analysis</li><li>Methods for evaluating public policies</li><li>Understanding cost-benefit analysis and economic evaluation</li><li>Exploring qualitative and quantitative data in policy evaluation</li><li>Tools for policy analysis: SWOT, PESTEL</li><li>Techniques for developing evidence-based policy recommendations</li><li>Discussing challenges in policy analysis and evaluation</li></ul>","<p><strong>Policy Implementation and Stakeholders</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li>Understanding the policy-making process</li><li>Exploring levels of government and policy implementation:</li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Local</li><li>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;National</li><li>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;International</li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li>Understanding the role of bureaucracies and agencies.</li><li>Exploring the stakeholders in the policy process:</li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Government</li><li>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;NGOs</li><li>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Private sector</li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li>Case studies of public policy implementation</li><li>Discussing barriers to effective policy implementation</li><li>Identifying the role of advocacy and public opinion in policy-making</li><li>Understanding the relationship between collaborative governance and multi-stakeholder partnerships</li></ul>","<p><strong>Strategies for Effective Policy Advocacy</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li>Introduction to policy advocacy</li><li>Techniques for effective advocacy campaigns</li><li>Methods for building coalitions and networks</li><li>Discussing how to use media and public relations for advocacy</li><li>The role of policy makers and influencers in advocacy</li><li>Strategies for monitoring and evaluating advocacy efforts</li><li>Case studies of successful policy advocacy</li><li>Developing a personal or organizational advocacy plan</li></ul>"]',
                'related_courses' => '[]',
                'category_id' => 55,
                'online' => 0,
                'created_at' => '2025-04-03 12:53:55',
                'updated_at' => '2025-04-03 12:53:55',
            ),
            313 => 
            array (
                'id' => 2159,
                'lang_code' => 'en',
                'name' => 'Public Relations: Media Crisis Communications',
                'description' => '<p>Public Policy is concerned with identifying and addressing collective problems. When societies change, it brings new challenges that need to be resolved. Sticking to old policies and refusing to reform them might cause further challenges and negative consequences.</p><p><br></p><p>The 21st century presents unique challenges that affect national and international public policies. Inequality, poverty, climate change, environmental sustainability, health care, migration, refugees, technological advancements, education, employment, terrorism, and many other challenges will be covered in the “Public Policy Challenges of the 21st Century” course.</p><p><br></p><p>This training course is designed to provide participants with a strong foundation in public policy by analyzing contemporary challenges and evaluating the impact of public policies on addressing them. Participants will understand the policy-making process at various levels and the role of advocacy in public relations. They\'ll also improve their skills in policy analysis and evaluation and develop their policy advocacy strategy throughout the course.&nbsp;</p>',
                'duration' => '5',
            'days_content' => '["<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Principles of Media Relations &amp; Public Affairs</strong></p><p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">﻿</strong></p><ul><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\">Defining media relations and its key related concepts</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\">Discussing the importance of media relations</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\">Exploring the principles of public affairs</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\">Techniques for building and maintaining media relationships</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\">Understanding the role of the media in public perception</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\">Differentiating between proactive and reactive media relations</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\">Exploring key stakeholders in media relations</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\">Understanding the media landscape</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\">Discussing legal and regulatory considerations</span></li></ul>","<p><strong>Role of Public Policy in Addressing Global Issues</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li>Introduction to global public policy</li><li>Discussing the role of public policy in international cooperation</li><li>Discussing global health policies and international responses</li><li>Exploring climate policies and international agreements (e.g., Paris Agreement)</li><li>Exploring economic policies in a globalized world</li><li>Discovering social policies addressing global inequality</li><li>Discussing human rights and global governance</li><li>Case studies of successful global policy interventions</li></ul>","<p><strong>Policy Analysis and Evaluation</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li>Introduction to policy analysis</li><li>Frameworks and models for policy analysis</li><li>Methods for evaluating public policies</li><li>Understanding cost-benefit analysis and economic evaluation</li><li>Exploring qualitative and quantitative data in policy evaluation</li><li>Tools for policy analysis: SWOT, PESTEL</li><li>Techniques for developing evidence-based policy recommendations</li><li>Discussing challenges in policy analysis and evaluation</li></ul>","<p><strong>Policy Implementation and Stakeholders</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li>Understanding the policy-making process</li><li>Exploring levels of government and policy implementation:</li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Local</li><li>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;National</li><li>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;International</li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li>Understanding the role of bureaucracies and agencies.</li><li>Exploring the stakeholders in the policy process:</li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Government</li><li>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;NGOs</li><li>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Private sector</li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li>Case studies of public policy implementation</li><li>Discussing barriers to effective policy implementation</li><li>Identifying the role of advocacy and public opinion in policy-making</li><li>Understanding the relationship between collaborative governance and multi-stakeholder partnerships</li></ul>","<p><strong>Strategies for Effective Policy Advocacy</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li>Introduction to policy advocacy</li><li>Techniques for effective advocacy campaigns</li><li>Methods for building coalitions and networks</li><li>Discussing how to use media and public relations for advocacy</li><li>The role of policy makers and influencers in advocacy</li><li>Strategies for monitoring and evaluating advocacy efforts</li><li>Case studies of successful policy advocacy</li><li>Developing a personal or organizational advocacy plan</li></ul>"]',
                'related_courses' => '[]',
                'category_id' => 55,
                'online' => 1,
                'created_at' => '2025-04-03 12:53:56',
                'updated_at' => '2025-04-03 12:53:56',
            ),
            314 => 
            array (
                'id' => 2160,
                'lang_code' => 'en',
                'name' => 'Public Relations: Media Crisis Communications',
            'description' => '<p><span style="color: rgb(24, 3, 44);">What do companies do during a time of crisis? They react by communication and deliver messages to the media. Communication during a crisis not only protects a company\'s reputation but can even improve it. The sudden nature of crises means companies can\'t predict and plan for them, but effective communication is key.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style="color: rgb(24, 3, 44);">With our training courses, you can develop your crisis communication skills and create strategies to protect your company’s image during crisis time. The “Public Relations: Media Crisis Communication” course offers practical and theoretical knowledge on media relations, public affairs, crisis communication strategies, media interactions and interview management, and communication strategy evaluation. Participants will learn to develop their crisis communication plan and practice dealing with and communicating with different media during a crisis.</span></p><p><br></p>',
                'duration' => '5',
            'days_content' => '["<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Principles of Media Relations &amp; Public Affairs</strong></p><p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\"><span class=\\"ql-cursor\\">﻿</span></strong></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Defining media relations and its key related concepts</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Discussing the importance of media relations</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Exploring the principles of public affairs</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Techniques for building and maintaining media relationships</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Understanding the role of the media in public perception</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Differentiating between proactive and reactive media relations</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Exploring key stakeholders in media relations</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Understanding the media landscape</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Discussing legal and regulatory considerations</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Media Communication During a Crisis</strong></p><p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\\"><span class=\\"ql-cursor\\">﻿</span></strong><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\">&nbsp;</span></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Identifying types of crises and their characteristics</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Preparing for potential crises: risk assessment</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Key elements of an effective crisis communication strategy</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Techniques for crafting clear and consistent messages</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Discussing the timing and channel elements for crisis communication</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Strategies for engaging with stakeholders during a crisis</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Discussing the role of spokespersons</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Techniques for managing misinformation and rumors</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Case Studies of Media Crisis Communications</strong></p><p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\"><span class=\\"ql-cursor\\">﻿</span></strong></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Analysis of notable crisis communication cases</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Success stories and lessons learned</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Understanding failures and what went wrong</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Discussing the impact of crisis communication on organizational reputation</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Exploring crisis communication in different industries.</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Understanding the comparative analysis of crisis responses.</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Discussing the long-term effects of crisis communication.</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Adapting strategies based on case study insights.</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Techniques for Managing Media Interactions &amp; Interviews</strong></p><p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\"><span class=\\"ql-cursor\\">﻿</span></strong></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Defining globalization and its dimensions</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Techniques for media interaction preparation</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Techniques for handling tough questions</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Dos and don’ts of media interviews</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Role-playing and practice sessions</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Strategies for managing press conferences and briefings</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Discussing the effective use of press releases</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Understanding how to build a media kit</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Follow-up strategies post-interaction</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Social Media and Ethical Considerations in Crisis Communications</strong></p><p><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">&nbsp;</span></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Understanding the role of social media in crisis communication</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Strategies for effective social media use during crises</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Techniques for monitoring and responding to social media activity</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Steps for developing a social media crisis communication plan</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Discussing ethical considerations in media communications</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Understanding how to balance transparency and confidentiality</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Addressing ethical dilemmas in crises</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Evaluating and refining the crisis communication plan</span></li></ul>"]',
                'related_courses' => '[]',
