            321 => 
            array (
                'id' => 2167,
                'lang_code' => 'en',
                'name' => 'Sustainability & ESG: Design, Plan and Implement',
            'description' => '<p>In an era where sustainability is no longer just an option but a necessity, mastering environmental, social, and governance (ESG) principles is crucial for modern businesses. The "Sustainability &amp; ESG: Design, Plan, and Implement" course offers a deep dive into the essentials of ESG risk management and strategic implementation. This comprehensive five-day course is tailored to equip professionals with the necessary tools and knowledge to drive sustainability initiatives within their organizations.</p><p><br></p><p>Participants will gain insights into the evolution and significance of ESG practices, explore global standards and frameworks, and learn how to align ESG goals with corporate strategies. Through interactive sessions and real-world examples, attendees will understand the nuances of assessing and managing ESG risks, developing strategic plans, and integrating sustainable practices into business operations. The course also emphasizes the financial implications of ESG factors, providing techniques for incorporating ESG into investment decisions and corporate governance.</p><p><br></p><p>Furthermore, the course covers the importance of transparency in ESG reporting and communication, ensuring that participants can effectively convey their ESG efforts to stakeholders. By the end of this course, attendees will have a solid foundation in designing, planning, and implementing ESG strategies, empowering them to contribute to sustainable and responsible business operations.&nbsp;</p>',
                'duration' => '5',
                'days_content' => '["<p><strong>Introduction to Sustainability &amp; ESG</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li>Defining Sustainability, ESG and related key terms</li><li>Understanding the three pillars of ESF: Environment, Social and Governance</li><li>Tracing the development of ESG practices over time in business landscape</li><li>Benefits of integrating ESG into corporate strategies and operations</li><li>Exploring global ESG standards, frameworks and agreements</li><li>Discussing common challenges of implementing ESG</li></ul>","<p><strong>Designing ESG Strategy</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li>Utilizing materiality impact assessment to evaluate current ESG practices</li><li>Sitting ESG goals and vision, and aligning them with corporate strategy</li><li>Identifying stakeholders and their ESG expectations</li><li>The importance of assessing risks and opportunities for competitive advantage</li><li>Discovering methods and tools to identify and evaluate ESG risks and opportunities</li></ul>","<p><strong>Planning, Implementing ESG Initiatives</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li>Developing a plan for ESG initiatives includes milestones and responsibilities</li><li>Designing ESG roadmap step-by step for implementing and integrating ESG strategy</li><li>Establishing ESG targets and metrics to track performance</li><li>Understanding how to integrate ESG practices into business operations</li><li>Discussing how to promote sustainable practice in supply chain</li></ul>","<p><strong>ESG in Finance &amp; Decision Making</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li>Assessing the impact of ESG factors on financial performance metrics</li><li>Methods for integrating ESG into investment decisions and portfolio management</li><li>Techniques for integrating ESG factors into corporate governance structure and practices</li><li>Understanding how to integrate ESG into strategic planning and innovation within business model</li><li>Utilizing tools to balance ESG initiatives with financial goals in decision-making processes</li></ul>","<p><strong>&nbsp;ESG Reporting &amp; Communication</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li>Understanding the importance of transparency and disclosure in reporting ESG initiatives</li><li>Discussing the best practices for clear and honest reporting on ESG initiatives</li><li>Discussing regulatory requirements for ESG disclosure</li><li>Techniques for communicating ESG efforts and achievements with stakeholders</li><li>Case studies of successful and unsuccessful ESG integration</li><li>Presentation of ESG plans and feedback</li><li>Lesson learned and course evaluation</li></ul>"]',
                'related_courses' => '[]',
                'category_id' => 34,
                'online' => 1,
                'created_at' => '2025-04-03 12:53:58',
                'updated_at' => '2025-04-03 12:53:58',
            ),
            322 => 
            array (
                'id' => 2168,
                'lang_code' => 'en',
                'name' => 'Sustainability & ESG: Design, Plan and Implement',
            'description' => '<p>In an era where sustainability is no longer just an option but a necessity, mastering environmental, social, and governance (ESG) principles is crucial for modern businesses. The "Sustainability &amp; ESG: Design, Plan, and Implement" course offers a deep dive into the essentials of ESG risk management and strategic implementation. This comprehensive five-day course is tailored to equip professionals with the necessary tools and knowledge to drive sustainability initiatives within their organizations.</p><p><br></p><p>Participants will gain insights into the evolution and significance of ESG practices, explore global standards and frameworks, and learn how to align ESG goals with corporate strategies. Through interactive sessions and real-world examples, attendees will understand the nuances of assessing and managing ESG risks, developing strategic plans, and integrating sustainable practices into business operations. The course also emphasizes the financial implications of ESG factors, providing techniques for incorporating ESG into investment decisions and corporate governance.</p><p><br></p><p>Furthermore, the course covers the importance of transparency in ESG reporting and communication, ensuring that participants can effectively convey their ESG efforts to stakeholders. By the end of this course, attendees will have a solid foundation in designing, planning, and implementing ESG strategies, empowering them to contribute to sustainable and responsible business operations.&nbsp;</p>',
