            359 => 
            array (
                'id' => 2205,
                'lang_code' => 'en',
                'name' => 'ESG Reporting for Businesses',
            'description' => '<p><span style="color: rgb(24, 3, 44);">The growing emphasis on sustainability and ethical governance has made environmental, social, and governance (ESG) reporting an essential aspect of modern business operations. ESG reporting provides a framework for organizations to disclose their impact on environmental and social factors while demonstrating transparency and accountability to stakeholders. By effectively communicating their ESG initiatives, businesses can enhance their reputation, meet regulatory requirements, and identify opportunities for improvement.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style="color: rgb(24, 3, 44);">The ESG Reporting for Businesses training course offers a comprehensive guide to understanding and implementing ESG reporting practices. Over five days, participants will explore the fundamentals of ESG reporting, including key standards and frameworks such as the Global Reporting Initiative (GRI) and the Task Force on Climate-related Financial Disclosures (TCFD). The course covers the process of conducting materiality assessments, collecting and analyzing ESG data, and crafting compelling reports that engage stakeholders.&nbsp;</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style="color: rgb(24, 3, 44);">Through practical exercises and real-world examples, attendees will gain the skills needed to create accurate and impactful ESG reports that align with industry best practices and drive sustainable business outcomes.</span></p>',
                'duration' => '5',
            'days_content' => '["<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">ESG Reporting Fundamentals</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\">Overview of ESG factors and principles</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\">Defining ESG reporting and its related key terms</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\">Discussing the benefits of ESG reporting for businesses</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\">Exploring the principles of ESG reporting</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\">Distinguishing between mandatory and voluntary ESG reporting requirements</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\">Discussing ESG reporting requirements:</span></li></ul><p><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\">﻿</span></p><ol><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\"> Requirements imposed by the ESG framework</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\"> </span><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\">ESG data reporting requirements</span></li></ol>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">ESG Standards &amp; Frameworks</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Global reporting initiative (GRI)</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Corporate sustainability reporting directive (CSRD)</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Environmental, social, and governance reporting standards (ESRS)</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Taskforce on climate-related financial disclosures (TCFD)</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Sustainability Accounting Standards Board (SASB)</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">International Sustainability Standards Board IFRS S1 &amp; IFRS S2 (ISSB-IFRS)</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Communication on Progress (CoP)</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">UN global compact and SDGs reporting</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">ESG Reporting Process</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Identifying material ESG issues</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Establishing ESG strategy and goals</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Choosing ESG reporting framework</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Collecting data and information</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Analyze data to determine areas for improvement.</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Communicating analysis results with stakeholders</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Drafting and publishing ESG reports in an accessible format</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Materiality Assessment &amp; Data Collection</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Understanding the meaning and importance of materiality assessment</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Exploring the process of conducting a materiality assessment</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Defining double materiality and understanding its benefits</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Techniques for collecting and managing ESG data</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Understanding how to align data with ESG criteria</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Tips for ensuring accurate, reliable, and reflective ESG data&nbsp;</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Crafting a Compelling ESG Report</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Exploring the main components of ESG reports:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Environmental factors</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Social factors</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Governance factors</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Goals and performance</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">ESG reporting framework</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Stakeholder engagement</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Risk and opportunities</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">ESG strategy</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">External assurance</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Tools and software for ESG reporting</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">The importance of copywriting and storytelling skills for stakeholder engagement</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Discussing challenges for ESG reporting</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Exploring ESG reporting best practices</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Final Project: Create an ESG report based on specific scenarios.</span></li></ul>"]',
                'related_courses' => '[]',
                'category_id' => 34,
                'online' => 1,
                'created_at' => '2025-04-03 12:54:10',
                'updated_at' => '2025-04-03 12:54:10',
