            array (
                'id' => 2212,
                'lang_code' => 'en',
                'name' => 'Capstone Project in Product Management',
            'description' => '<p><span style="color: rgb(24, 3, 44);">Effective product management plays a pivotal role in translating innovative concepts into market successes. For instance, consider how a company’s successful market entry often relies on a well-coordinated approach across various stages—from concept development to market launch. This involves understanding market dynamics, defining clear product visions, and meticulously planning and executing product strategies. Without these elements, even the most promising product can falter.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style="color: rgb(24, 3, 44);">The Capstone Project in Product Management training course is designed to address these challenges comprehensively. This course provides an in-depth exploration of the product management lifecycle, equipping you with the advanced skills necessary to navigate complex product development processes. Through a series of detailed, hands-on activities, you will engage with real-world scenarios, allowing you to develop and refine product management strategies and frameworks.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style="color: rgb(24, 3, 44);">By completing this course, you will gain a robust understanding of how to effectively manage every phase of the product lifecycle—from initial conception and strategic planning to execution and market delivery. This knowledge is critical for ensuring that products not only meet market needs but also achieve long-term success in competitive environments.</span></p>',
                'duration' => '10',
            'days_content' => '["<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Fundamentals of Product Management&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Overview of the responsibilities of a product manager and required skills&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Selecting a scenario for your capstone project&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Overview of the process of activities required to complete your capstone project&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Defining Porter’s five forces model and discussing the strategies to deal with those forces&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Utilizing the Ansoff matrix to visualize strategy options based on market and product parameters </span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Product Conceiving Phase</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Defining the product conception phase and its stages:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Concept identification&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Concept investigation&nbsp;</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Identify the purpose of the product concept document.&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Discussing the external assessment considerations:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Market view</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Competitor view</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Technology view&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Partner view&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Environmental view&nbsp;</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Discussing the internal assessment considerations:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Competitiveness view</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Product view</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Competencies view&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Resources View&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Partner view&nbsp;</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Exercise: Conducting external and internal assessments to develop a product concept document </span></li></ul><p><br></p>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Product Conceiving Phase</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Exploring the elements of the product concept document:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Market problem or opportunity&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Market segments</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Key financials&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Competitive landscape&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Main features and functionality&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Key differentiators</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Go-to-market logistics&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Business success measurements&nbsp;</span></li></ol><p><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\"><span class=\\"ql-cursor\\">﻿</span></span></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Exercise 1: Develop your product concept document&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Defining product vision and its significance&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Understanding the format of elevator pitch to develop a product vision</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Exercise 2: Develop your product vision </span></li></ul><p><br></p>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Product Planning Phase: PRD &amp; User Stories&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Defining the product plan phase and its stages:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Product definition&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Product plan activities&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Marketing plan activities&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Business case&nbsp;</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Discussing the entries of the product requirements document (PRD):</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Product users</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Functional requirements&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Non-functional requirements&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Support requirements&nbsp;</span></li></ol><p><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\"><span class=\\"ql-cursor\\">﻿</span></span></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Exercise 1: Develop your product requirements document (PRD).</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Understanding how to create user stories and a product backlog to support product development&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Exercise 2: Develop your user stories and prioritized product backlog. </span></li></ul><p><br></p>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Product Planning Phase: Roadmap &amp; Business Case</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Understanding the role of the product roadmap in developing a product&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Discussing the components of the product roadmap:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Product name/identifier&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Defined release cycles&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Features planned for each release cycle&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Beta test and launch milestones&nbsp;</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Exercise 1: Develop your product roadmap&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Finalizing the business case by including and completing all its components:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Summary of marketing needs and opportunities</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Primary competition&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Product Capabilities&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Product vision summary&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Value proposition and positioning statement&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Strategic objectives&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Go-to-market plans&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Financial analysis summary</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Risk assessment summary&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Open issues&nbsp;</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Exercise 2: Develop your final business case </span></li></ul><p><br></p>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Product Development Phase: Beta Plan&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Defining the development phase and its stages:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Product development&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Market validation&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Lunch planning&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Program review</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Understanding the meaning and importance of beta plans&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Discussing the types of beta tests/market tests and their benefits:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Open beta testing&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Closed beta testing&nbsp;</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Understanding the categories of beta planning:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Testing purpose&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Internal Readiness&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Tester Recruitment&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Testing objectives&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Test management&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Communications&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Costs</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Schedules&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Non-disclosure authority (NDA)</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Key performance indicators (KPIs)</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Exercise 1: Develop your beta plan&nbsp;</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Product Development Phase: Usability Testing&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Defining usability testing and determining its significance&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Discussing usability testing criteria and its related considerations:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Learnable&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Efficient&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Memorable&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Free of errors&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Delightful&nbsp;</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Exploring the elements of usability testing:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Prototype</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Test plan&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Target users</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Location selection&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Test modifying&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Result documentation&nbsp;</span></li></ol><p><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\"><span class=\\"ql-cursor\\">﻿</span></span></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Discussing the ethical considerations in usability testing&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Exercise 2: Define your usability testing requirements </span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Product Qualify Phase&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Defining the qualifying phase and its stages:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Market validation&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Launch preparation&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Lunch readiness assessment&nbsp;</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Exploring methods for qualifying your product:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Beta testing</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Focus groups</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Internal feedback&nbsp;</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Analyzing testing results to achieve market validation&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Discussing techniques to assess launch readiness:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Beta planning&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Beta testing&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Roles and responsibilities&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Success metrics&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Launch plan&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Sales and channel</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Customer support&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Manufacturing and operations</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Product Documentation&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Business plan&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Launch decision&nbsp;</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Exercise: Conduct a launch readiness assessment for your product. </span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Product Lunch Phase&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Defining the launch phase and its stages:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Launch activities&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Post-launch activities&nbsp;</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">How to finalize positioning and marketing preparation:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Demand generation planning&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Functional readiness&nbsp;</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Exploring the elements of the demand generation plan:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Marketing objectives&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Market trends&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Marketing theme</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Target audience/customer segments&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Programs/tactics</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Key influencers&nbsp;</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Determining the support functions that must be ready to launch the product:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Sales and channel readiness&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Operational and support readiness&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Product support readiness&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Manufacturing&nbsp;</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Exercise 1: Creating Potential Marketing Collateral Options&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Exercise 2: Develop your demand generation plan. </span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Product Delivering &amp; Retraining Phase&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Defining the deliver phase and retain phase&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Discussing the ways of product retirement:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Harvest the product.&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Sell the product&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Discontinue the product&nbsp;</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Overview of the product lifecycle:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Introduction</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Growth&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Maturity&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Decline&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Discussing the end-of-life (EOL) plan and its components:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Product identification&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">The rationale for retiring the product&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Communications</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Impacts on internal and external stakeholders&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Cost-benefit analysis&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Critical success factor plan</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Exercise: Develop your EOL plan.&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Final presentation: present your capstone project in product management. </span></li></ul>"]',
