            369 => 
            array (
                'id' => 2215,
                'lang_code' => 'en',
                'name' => 'Asset Life Cycle and Maintenance Management',
            'description' => '<p><span style="color: rgb(24, 3, 44);">Asset Life Cycle Management (ALCM) is a comprehensive approach that involves overseeing an asset\'s journey through its key phases: planning, acquisition, operation, maintenance, and eventual decommissioning or disposal. Each phase requires strategic decisions that impact the asset\'s performance, lifespan, and cost-effectiveness.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style="color: rgb(24, 3, 44);">By implementing proactive asset management practices, organizations can significantly enhance asset reliability and reduce costs associated with unplanned downtime and inefficient maintenance. Studies show that structured maintenance strategies can lead to a reduction in maintenance costs by 5-10% and extend asset life by up to 50%.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style="color: rgb(24, 3, 44);">This course is designed to provide participants with a deep understanding of the asset life cycle and the critical role of maintenance management. Key topics include the development of maintenance plans and schedules, the selection of appropriate maintenance strategies, and the use of advanced technologies such as computerized maintenance management systems (CMMS) and the Internet of Things (IoT) in predictive maintenance.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style="color: rgb(24, 3, 44);">Participants will also learn how to develop key performance indicators (KPIs) to measure maintenance effectiveness and implement change management strategies to enhance asset performance. Through practical case studies and interactive discussions, this course equips professionals with the tools to optimize asset management processes and improve their organization\'s overall efficiency.</span></p>',
                'duration' => '5',
            'days_content' => '["<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Introduction to Asset Life Cycle Management</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\">Introduction to Course Content and Outlines</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\">Definition and significance of asset life cycle management</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\">Describing key phases of the asset life cycle:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\"> Planning</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\"> </span><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\">Acquisition</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\"> </span><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\">Operation</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\"> </span><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\">Maintenance</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\"> </span><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\">Decommission/Disposal</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\">Exploring types of assets and identifying their maintenance needs</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\">Identifying the role and benefits of maintenance throughout the asset life cycle</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\">Analyzing the impact of poor maintenance practices on asset performance and costs</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Maintenance Fundamentals: Planning and Scheduling</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Distinguishing between maintenance by plan and maintenance by default</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Identifying the role of planning and scheduling in asset life cycle management</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Steps and components of maintenance plan</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Exploring maintenance scheduling techniques:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Time-based technique</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Condition-based technique</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Tools and platforms for maintenance planning and scheduling</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Best practices for optimizing maintenance intervals for various assets</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Maintenance Strategies</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Detailed analysis of maintenance strategies:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Preventative strategy</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Corrective strategy</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Predictive strategy</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Reliability-center maintenance (RCM) strategy</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Criteria for selecting the best maintenance strategy</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Techniques for predicting asset failures</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Identifying the procedures of preventive maintenance</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Process of developing corrective maintenance responses</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Steps to implement the RCM strategy</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Maintenance Management Technologies</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Overview of maintenance management systems:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Computerized maintenance management systems (CMMS)</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Enterprise asset management systems (EAM)</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Identifying the benefits and key features of maintenance management systems</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Understanding how CMMS and EMA work</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Determining the role of AI and IoT in maintenance</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Case studies of technology applications in maintenance management</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Group Discussion: Limitations and Challenges of Maintenance Management Systems</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Performance Measurement and Change Management</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Determining the significance of measuring maintenance performance</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Steps for developing KPIs for measuring maintenance performance</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Best practices for conducting maintenance audits and assessments</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Case studies of maintenance KPIs</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Strategies for implementing and managing changes</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Identifying key challenges and issues with change management</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Recap and lesson learned</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Course evaluation and feedback</span></li></ul>"]',
                'related_courses' => '[]',
                'category_id' => 19,
                'online' => 1,
                'created_at' => '2025-04-03 12:54:13',
                'updated_at' => '2025-04-03 12:54:13',
            ),
