            'days_content' => '["<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Introduction to Asset Life Cycle Management</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Introduction to Course Content and Outlines</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Definition and significance of asset life cycle management</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Describing key phases of the asset life cycle:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">          Planning</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">          </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Acquisition</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">          </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Operation</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">          </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Maintenance</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">          </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Decommission/Disposal</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Exploring types of assets and identifying their maintenance needs</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Identifying the role and benefits of maintenance throughout the asset life cycle</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Analyzing the impact of poor maintenance practices on asset performance and costs</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Maintenance Fundamentals: Planning and Scheduling</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Distinguishing between maintenance by plan and maintenance by default</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Identifying the role of planning and scheduling in asset life cycle management</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Steps and components of maintenance plan</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Exploring maintenance scheduling techniques:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">           Time-based technique</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">           </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Condition-based technique</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Tools and platforms for maintenance planning and scheduling</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Best practices for optimizing maintenance intervals for various assets</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Maintenance Strategies</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Detailed analysis of maintenance strategies:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">         Preventative strategy</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">         </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Corrective strategy</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">         </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Predictive strategy</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">         </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Reliability-center maintenance (RCM) strategy</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Criteria for selecting the best maintenance strategy</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Techniques for predicting asset failures</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Identifying the procedures of preventive maintenance</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Process of developing corrective maintenance responses</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Steps to implement the RCM strategy</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Maintenance Management Technologies</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Overview of maintenance management systems:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">           Computerized maintenance management systems (CMMS)</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">           </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Enterprise asset management systems (EAM)</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Identifying the benefits and key features of maintenance management systems</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Understanding how CMMS and EMA work</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Determining the role of AI and IoT in maintenance</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Case studies of technology applications in maintenance management</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Group Discussion: Limitations and Challenges of Maintenance Management Systems</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Performance Measurement and Change Management</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Determining the significance of measuring maintenance performance</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Steps for developing KPIs for measuring maintenance performance</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Best practices for conducting maintenance audits and assessments</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Case studies of maintenance KPIs</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Strategies for implementing and managing changes</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Identifying key challenges and issues with change management</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Recap and lesson learned</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Course evaluation and feedback</span></li></ul>"]',
                'related_courses' => '[]',
                'category_id' => 19,
                'online' => 0,
                'created_at' => '2025-04-03 12:54:13',
                'updated_at' => '2025-04-03 12:54:13',
            ),
            371 => 
            array (
                'id' => 2217,
                'lang_code' => 'en',
                'name' => 'Design Thinking and User Experience',
            'description' => '<p><span style="color: rgb(24, 3, 44);">As technology continues to evolve and consumer expectations rise, the demand for user-centric product design becomes increasingly critical. Design thinking provides a structured approach to innovation by focusing on understanding users\' needs, generating creative solutions, and iteratively refining those solutions to improve user experiences.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style="color: rgb(24, 3, 44);">The Design Thinking and User Experience course is crafted to offer a deep dive into this methodology, exploring how it can be applied to create impactful, user-friendly products. Over the course, participants will learn to navigate the stages of design thinking—from empathizing with users and defining their problems to prototyping and testing solutions. This hands-on training will also cover essential aspects of user experience design, including user research, persona creation, and journey mapping, ensuring a comprehensive understanding of how to build products that resonate with users.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style="color: rgb(24, 3, 44);">By integrating these principles, professionals will be equipped to lead design projects that are not only innovative but also grounded in real user needs, ultimately enhancing product effectiveness and market success.</span></p>',
                'duration' => '5',
            'days_content' => '["<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Introduction to Design Thinking&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Identifying the meaning of design thinking&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Discussing the history of design thinking&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Discussing the application of design thinking in product management&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Understanding the stages of the design thinking process:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Empathize</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Define&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Ideate</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Prototype</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Test</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Familiarizing with design thinking frameworks:</span></li></ul><p><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">﻿</span></p><ol><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Stanford’s Five-Stage Model</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">IDEO’s three-phase model</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">IBM’s Enterprise Design&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Double Dimond Model by UK Design Council</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Design Sprint</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Balanced Breakthrough Model </span></li></ol>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Designing for User Experience</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Defining user experience design and discussing its principles&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Exploring the process of designing UX&nbsp;</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Understanding the user\'s pain points&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Creating user personas&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Map out the user journey.&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Create a website wireframe.</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Start prototyping&nbsp;</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Defining UX deliverables:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">User Research&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Competitor Assessment&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Interaction Design&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Information Architecture&nbsp;</span></li></ol><p><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">﻿</span></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Understanding the relationship between user experience (UX) and user interface (UI)</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Understanding the core principles of UI</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">User Research &amp; Persona&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Understanding empathy for the target customer and how to develop it&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Techniques to gather information from customers and understand their needs:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Interviews</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Surveys</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">What is a customer persona?&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Understanding the elements of persona:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Name, age, gender, and image of the persona</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">A tag line&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Persona experience and relevant skills</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">The context indicates how the persona would interact with the product.&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Goals, attitudes, concerns&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Quotes/brief scenario&nbsp;</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Understanding the types of user persona:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Lightweight/prototype persona</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Qualitative persona&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Statistical persona</span></li></ol>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Story Mapping vs. Journey Mapping&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Understand the meaning of story mapping and its purpose.&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Differentiating between story mapping and journey mapping&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Understanding the components of story mapping:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Goal</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Epic</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">User story&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Swimlane&nbsp;</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Defining the process of creating a story map:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Initial planning&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Organizing user stories&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Prioritizing and estimating&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Slicing the map for release&nbsp;</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Understanding the elements of the journey map:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Actors/ subjects</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Expectations</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Phases/paradigms&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Actions, mindsets, and emotions</span></li></ol>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Prototyping &amp; User Testing&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Understanding the meaning and function of the prototype</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Defining the types of prototypes:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Low-fidelity</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Mid-fidelity&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">High-fidelity&nbsp;</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Integrating user interaction into a prototype&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Defining the meaning of usability testing and its types:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Hallway usability testing&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Remote usability testing&nbsp;</span></li></ol><p><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">﻿</span></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Analyzing the test results and identifying areas for improvement in UX</span></li></ul>"]',
                'related_courses' => '[]',
                'category_id' => 52,
                'online' => 1,
                'created_at' => '2025-04-03 12:54:14',
                'updated_at' => '2025-04-03 12:54:14',
            ),
