            'days_content' => '["<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Introduction to Design Thinking&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Identifying the meaning of design thinking&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Discussing the history of design thinking&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Discussing the application of design thinking in product management&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Understanding the stages of the design thinking process:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Empathize</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Define&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Ideate</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Prototype</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Test</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Familiarizing with design thinking frameworks:</span></li></ul><p><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\"><span class=\\"ql-cursor\\">﻿</span></span></p><ol><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Stanford’s Five-Stage Model</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">IDEO’s three-phase model</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">IBM’s Enterprise Design&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Double Dimond Model by UK Design Council</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Design Sprint</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"backgroun