strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">User Research &amp; Persona&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Understanding empathy for the target customer and how to develop it&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Techniques to gather information from customers and understand their needs:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Interviews</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Surveys</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">What is a customer persona?&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Understanding the elements of persona:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Name, age, gender, and image of the persona</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">A tag line&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Persona experience and relevant skills</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">The context indicates how the persona would interact with the product.&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Goals, attitudes, concerns&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Quotes/brief scenario&nbsp;</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Understanding the types of user persona:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Lightweight/prototype persona</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Qualitative persona&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Statistical persona</span></li></ol>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Story Mapping vs. Journey Mapping&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Understand the meaning of story mapping and its purpose.&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Differentiating between story mapping and journey mapping&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Understanding the components of story mapping:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Goal</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Epic</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">User story&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Swimlane&nbsp;</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Defining the process of creating a story map:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Initial planning&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Organizing user stories&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Prioritizing and estimating&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Slicing the map for release&nbsp;</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Understanding the elements of the journey map:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Actors/ subjects</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Expectations</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Phases/paradigms&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Actions, mindsets, and emotions </span></li></ol>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Prototyping &amp; User Testing&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Understanding the meaning and function of the prototype</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Defining the types of prototypes:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Low-fidelity</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Mid-fidelity&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">High-fidelity&nbsp;</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Integrating user interaction into a prototype&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Defining the meaning of usability testing and its types:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Hallway usability testing&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Remote usability testing&nbsp;</span></li></ol><p><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\"><span class=\\"ql-cursor\\">﻿</span></span></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Analyzing the test results and identifying areas for improvement in UX</span></li></ul>"]',
                'related_courses' => '[]',
                'category_id' => 52,
                'online' => 0,
                'created_at' => '2025-04-03 12:54:14',
                'updated_at' => '2025-04-03 12:54:14',
            ),
            373 => 
            array (
                'id' => 2219,
                'lang_code' => 'en',
                'name' => 'Global Product Management',
            'description' => '<p><span style="color: rgb(24, 3, 44);">In a world where market boundaries are increasingly blurred, managing a product on a global scale presents both significant opportunities and complex challenges. Imagine a product designed for a specific market segment encountering varied consumer preferences, regulatory standards, and competitive landscapes as it enters new regions. The need for a nuanced approach to product management becomes evident when considering how a single product must be adapted to meet diverse local requirements while maintaining a cohesive global strategy.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style="color: rgb(24, 3, 44);">The Global Product Management training course delves into the strategic and operational considerations essential for navigating these global complexities. Participants will explore how globalization necessitates a shift from traditional product management practices to a more integrated global approach. The course covers the development and implementation of strategies for international market entry, the intricacies of global product development, and the best practices for managing products across diverse regions.&nbsp;</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style="color: rgb(24, 3, 44);">By understanding these dynamics, professionals will be better equipped to manage global product portfolios, ensuring alignment with both local market needs and overarching business objectives.</span></p>',
                'duration' => '5',
            'days_content' => '["<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Introduction to Global Product Management&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Understanding the meaning of global product management and its significance in today’s world&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Discussing the impact of globalization on the transformation to global product management&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Understanding the reasons behind the transformation to a global product&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Comparing the global product management approach with the conventional approach&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Discussing real-world examples of companies and countries adopting global products</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Introducing New Global Product Strategies&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Exploring strategies for introducing products to a new international market:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Straight product extension&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Product Adoption&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Product invention</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Advantages and disadvantages of product extension, adoption, and invention&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Discussing factors to consider when introducing new products:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Local knowledge</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Country-of-origin effect</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Distinguishing between outsourcing and offshoring in global product management&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Understanding the models of global product development operations based on ownership and resource location:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Centralized</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Local outsourcing&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Captive offshoring&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Global outsourcing</span></li></ol>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Product Adoption vs. Global Innovation</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Discovering the dimensions of value proposition adoption&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Discussing what influences value proposition adoption&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Understanding the advantages and opportunities of adopting a global innovation strategy&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Exploring the steps of global innovation strategy:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Prospecting&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Assessing new sources of innovation&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Mobilizing the footprint&nbsp;</span></li></ol><p><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">﻿</span></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Discussing the principles of innovation for the Bottom of the Pyramid (BOP)</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Global Product Development Deployment Strategy</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Overview of deploying global product development strategy</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Understanding the outsourcing process approach and its stages:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Outsourcing simple tasks&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Outsourcing complex and integrated tasks&nbsp;</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Understanding the component outsourcing approach and its stages:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Designing simple components&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Designing integrated components&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Developing complete product modules&nbsp;</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Understanding the captive design center approach and its stages:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Outsourcing simple tasks or components&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Outsourcing complex and integrated tasks and components&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Completing modules/subsystems&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Developing derivative products</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Developing new global products</span></li></ol><p><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">﻿</span></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Discussing the success factors for deploying global products</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Best Practices &amp; Future Trends</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Discovering the ground rules for global products:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Think global</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Understand and select the global market</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Select the competitive battleground&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Global product strategy&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Upfront planning&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Prescriptive approach</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Clear and common terminology&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Architectures and models&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Digital products and digital manufacturing</span></li></ol><p><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">﻿</span></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Understanding the opportunities and challenges associated with global products&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Discussing different techniques and approaches used to improve the performance of business with global products&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Discussing future trends of global product management and its influence&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Course recap and Q&amp;A&nbsp;</span></li></ul>"]',
                'related_courses' => '[]',
                'category_id' => 52,
                'online' => 1,
                'created_at' => '2025-04-03 12:54:14',
                'updated_at' => '2025-04-03 12:54:14',
            ),
