            393 => 
            array (
                'id' => 2239,
                'lang_code' => 'en',
                'name' => 'Project Management for NGO',
            'description' => '<p><span style="color: rgb(24, 3, 44);">Project management in the context of NGOs presents distinct challenges compared to corporate environments, demanding a tailored approach that takes into account the unique goals, stakeholders, and funding structures of non-profit organizations. The project management for NGOs training course is designed to provide professionals with a comprehensive understanding of the principles and practices essential for successful project execution in the NGO sector.&nbsp;</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style="color: rgb(24, 3, 44);">Participants will explore the project management lifecycle within NGOs, learn the key differences between non-profit and corporate project management, and gain insight into the legal and regulatory frameworks governing NGO operations.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style="color: rgb(24, 3, 44);">Throughout the course, participants will master techniques for defining project scope, designing impactful projects, and managing stakeholder relationships. In addition, they will develop the skills necessary to craft compelling proposals, secure funding, and manage donor relationships effectively. The course also covers crucial topics such as risk management, governance, partnerships, and monitoring and evaluation.&nbsp;</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style="color: rgb(24, 3, 44);">By the end of the program, participants will be equipped to design, implement, and monitor NGO projects with precision, ensuring that they align with organizational goals, meet community needs, and comply with donor expectations. This course is essential for anyone looking to enhance their expertise in managing NGO projects with efficiency and impact.</span></p>',
                'duration' => '5',
            'days_content' => '["<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Introduction to Project Management in NGOs&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\">Defining project management in the context of NGOs</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\">Comparing corporate and non-profit project management</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\">Determining the core purpose and role of NGOs</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\">Principles of project management in NGOs</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\">Overview of project management lifecycle in NGOs</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\">Understanding laws and regulations governing NGOs</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Planning and Designing Projects in NGOs</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Techniques for defining project scope and objectives</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">The methodology of identifying and analyzing project stakeholders</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Steps of developing project plans</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Understanding budgeting and financial planning in NGOs</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Describing the key components of project design metrics</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Techniques for recruiting and selecting project staff and volunteers</span></li></ul><p><br></p>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Proposal Development and Fund Management</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Fundamentals of grant and fund management</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">&nbsp;Exploring funding sources in NGOs:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ul><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Grants</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Donations</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Corporate sponsorships</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Earned income</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Describing fundraising and diversification strategies</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Discovering the donor cycle</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Process of proposal development</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Characteristics of a compiling grant proposal</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Best practices for managing donor funds and compliance</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Governance, Partnership and Collaboration in NGO Projects</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Discussing the impact of different governance structures on NGOs</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Importance of partnership and collaboration in NGO projects</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Strategies for cooperation with other NGOs and government agencies</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Techniques for empowering and engaging local communities in projects</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Best practices for managing project staff and volunteers</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Describing the significance of managing communication with partners and stakeholders</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Risk Management, Monitoring and Evolution for NGOs</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Techniques for identifying and assessing risks in NGO operations</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Best practices for managing risk and ensuring safety</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Strategies for crisis management and business continuity planning</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Steps of developing monitoring and evaluation plans for NGO projects</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Importance of data collection and analysis in improving projects</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Best practices for reporting results to donors and stakeholders</span></li></ul>"]',
