            397 => 
            array (
                'id' => 2243,
                'lang_code' => 'en',
                'name' => 'Piping System: Repair and Welding Techniques',
            'description' => '<p><span style="color: rgb(24, 3, 44);">In industries ranging from oil and gas to chemical processing, piping systems play a crucial role in ensuring the safe and efficient transport of fluids. Understanding the fundamentals of these systems is essential for anyone involved in their design, construction, maintenance, or repair. This course offers a comprehensive exploration of the key elements that make up a piping system, from the basic materials used to the detailed design principles that guide their construction.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style="color: rgb(24, 3, 44);">Participants will begin by examining the importance of piping systems across various industries and will gain insight into the materials commonly used and their specific applications. The course then delves into the critical components of a piping system, such as pipes, fittings, valves, and flanges, providing a foundational understanding that is essential for both new and experienced professionals.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style="color: rgb(24, 3, 44);">As the course progresses, participants will explore the complexities of piping design, the principles of fluid dynamics within these systems, and the standards and codes that govern their safe operation. The program also covers essential topics such as stress analysis, load considerations, and the various methods used in piping repair and maintenance. Finally, the course will introduce participants to the fundamentals of welding in piping systems, followed by a thorough review of weld testing techniques to ensure the integrity of these crucial systems.</span></p>',
                'duration' => '5',
            'days_content' => '["<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Fundamentals of Piping System</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\">Identifying the importance of piping systems in various industries</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\">Discovering common piping materials and their applications</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\">Main components of piping systems:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\"> Piping</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\"> </span><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\">Fittings</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\"> </span><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\">Valves</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\"> </span><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\">Flanges</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\">Discussing the principles of fluid flow in piping systems&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\">Understanding piping standards and codes which governing piping systems</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Piping Design and Construction</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\">Describing the main principles of piping design:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\"> Piping layout design</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\"> Isometric drawings</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\">Understanding the fundamentals of stress analysis and load considerations</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\">Key factors influencing piping engineering and design</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\">Methodology of determining pipe sizes and pressure rating</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\">Definition, importance and formulas of pipe schedules</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\">Identifying the significance of piping insulation and protection</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Piping Repair and Maintenance Process</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Recognizing regular maintenance practices and schedules for piping systems</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Discussing main causes of piping failures and their impact</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Exploring piping repair techniques:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">        Welding</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">        </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Sleeving</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">        </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Clamping</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Steps of piping repair and maintenance</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Strategies of prevention maintenance and their role in preventing piping failure</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Piping Welding Fundamentals</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Definition and importance of welding in piping systems</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Exploring common welding techniques:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">             Shielded Metal Arc Welding (SMAW)</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">             </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Gas Tungsten Arc Welding (GTAW)</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">             </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Gas Metal Arc Welding (GMAW)</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">             </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Flux Cored Arc Welding (FCAW)</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">             </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Submerged Arc Welding (SAW)</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Understanding welding symbols and welded joint configurations on construction drawings</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Discovering welding tools, equipment and safety protocols</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Describing essential welding standards and codes</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Weld Testing Techniques</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Definition and types of welding defects</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Discovering weld inspection methods:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">           Destructive methods</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">           Non-Destructive methods</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Discussing the importance of visual inspection and its methods</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Definition and importance of procedure qualification records (PQR)</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Identifying the purpose and application of welding procedure specification (WPS)</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Recognizing the importance of weld testing documentation and reporting </span></li></ul>"]',
