            409 => 
            array (
                'id' => 2256,
                'lang_code' => 'en',
                'name' => 'Modern Strategies and Methodologies in Contract Management and Conflict Prevention',
            'description' => '<p><span style="color: rgb(24, 3, 44);">In today\'s business environment, managing contracts effectively is essential for maintaining smooth operations and preventing costly disputes. Contracts are the foundation of all business relationships, governing everything from procurement and service agreements to supplier partnerships and project deliveries. To ensure these relationships run smoothly, professionals need a solid understanding of contract management principles, from drafting and negotiation to handling risks and resolving conflicts. The Modern Strategies and Methodologies in Contract Management and Conflict Prevention course offers participants the tools and knowledge to handle contracts with confidence.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style="color: rgb(24, 3, 44);">This course covers the full lifecycle of contracts, helping participants understand key elements such as contract types, sourcing strategies, risk allocation, and post-award activities. Participants will learn how to structure contracts to protect their organizations while developing skills to manage negotiations, avoid disputes, and resolve any issues that arise. The course also focuses on practical solutions to common challenges in contract management, including the legal and regulatory frameworks that guide contract creation and execution.&nbsp;</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style="color: rgb(24, 3, 44);">By the end of this course, participants will have a deeper understanding of how to manage contracts in a way that reduces risk, enhances clarity, and ensures that all parties involved are satisfied with the terms and execution of the agreement. This approach helps protect businesses while ensuring that projects and partnerships move forward without unnecessary complications.</span></p>',
                'duration' => '5',
            'days_content' => '["<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Introduction to Contracts</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\\">Understanding the meaning of contracts and their significance</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\\">Exploring the elements of contracts: Legal, technical and administrative elements</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\\">Types of contract: verbal vs. written contracts</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\\">Exploring contract lifecycle</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\\">Discussing laws and regulations in contract</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\\">Laws and regulation in contract</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\\">Understanding the meaning of risk allocation among contracting parties</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\\">Discussing the fundamentals of identifying contractor, service provider or supplier</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\\">Understanding the contractual obligations of the parties</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\\">Practical exercise: Analyzing standard contract sample</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Scope Development</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Understanding sourcing strategies</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Classifying contracts based on pricing methods:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">        Fixed price contract</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">       </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\"> Price adjustment contract</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">        </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Cost-plus contract</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">        </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Bills of quantity contract</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">        </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Schedule of rates contract</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Classifying contracts based on contracting methods:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">        </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Competitive contract</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">        </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Negotiated contract</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Discussing other types of contracts</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">        </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Turnkey contract</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">        </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Series contract</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">        </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Frame contracts</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Techniques for identifying contractual requirements, including legal, technical, commercial and financial requirements</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Discussing the pros and cons of standard form contracts</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Understanding Scope, pricing, and payment terms in contracts</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Contractual Clauses Interpretation Rules</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Understanding the manifestation of intent</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Discussing key rules of contract interpretation</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Defining parole evidence rule</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Discussing the role of doctrine of contra proferentem in managing contracts</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Understanding key contractual clauses in:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">           Construction contracts – FIDIC</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">           </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Supply contracts</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">           </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Consultancy terms of reference ToR</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">           </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Special condition of contract</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">           </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Insurance and guarantees</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Practical exercise: group activity on drafting terms of reference</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Contract Negotiations, Modification &amp; Termination</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Understanding the principles of contract negotiation</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Exploring contract negotiation strategies</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Understand BATA: Best alternative to negotiated agreement</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Defining win-win negotiations</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Discussing when contracts need modification</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Understanding contract termination process&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Role play: negotiations on contract terms</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Contract Disputes Resolution</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Understanding when disputes occur</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Discussing techniques for avoiding disputes</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Identifying the role of negotiation in resolving disputes</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Understanding contractual clauses related to disputes and disputes resolution</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Defining compensation claims and when it occurs</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Understanding arbitration clauses and procedures</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Practical exercise: drafting an arbitration clause</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Recap and course evaluation</span></li></ul>"]',
                'related_courses' => '[]',
                'category_id' => 18,
                'online' => 1,
                'created_at' => '2025-04-03 12:54:37',
                'updated_at' => '2025-04-03 12:54:37',
