            'days_content' => '["<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Introduction to Contracts</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Understanding the meaning of contracts and their significance</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Exploring the elements of contracts: Legal, technical and administrative elements</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Types of contract: verbal vs. written contracts</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Exploring contract lifecycle</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Discussing laws and regulations in contract</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Laws and regulation in contract</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Understanding the meaning of risk allocation among contracting parties</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Discussing the fundamentals of identifying contractor, service provider or supplier</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Understanding the contractual obligations of the parties</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Practical exercise: Analyzing standard contract sample</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Scope Development</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Understanding sourcing strategies</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Classifying contracts based on pricing methods:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">        Fixed price contract</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">       </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\"> Price adjustment contract</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">        </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Cost-plus contract</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">        </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Bills of quantity contract</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">        </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Schedule of rates contract</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Classifying contracts based on contracting methods:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">        </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Competitive contract</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">        </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Negotiated contract</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Discussing other types of contracts</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">        </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Turnkey contract</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">        </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Series contract</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">        </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Frame contracts</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Techniques for identifying contractual requirements, including legal, technical, commercial and financial requirements</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Discussing the pros and cons of standard form contracts</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Understanding Scope, pricing, and payment terms in contracts</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Contractual Clauses Interpretation Rules</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Understanding the manifestation of intent</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Discussing key rules of contract interpretation</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Defining parole evidence rule</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Discussing the role of doctrine of contra proferentem in managing contracts</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Understanding key contractual clauses in:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">           Construction contracts – FIDIC</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">           </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Supply contracts</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">           </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Consultancy terms of reference ToR</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">           </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Special condition of contract</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">           </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Insurance and guarantees</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Practical exercise: group activity on drafting terms of reference</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Contract Negotiations, Modification &amp; Termination</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Understanding the principles of contract negotiation</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Exploring contract negotiation strategies</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Understand BATA: Best alternative to negotiated agreement</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Defining win-win negotiations</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Discussing when contracts need modification</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Understanding contract termination process&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Role play: negotiations on contract terms</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Contract Disputes Resolution</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Understanding when disputes occur</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Discussing techniques for avoiding disputes</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Identifying the role of negotiation in resolving disputes</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Understanding contractual clauses related to disputes and disputes resolution</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Defining compensation claims and when it occurs</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Understanding arbitration clauses and procedures</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Practical exercise: drafting an arbitration clause</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Recap and course evaluation</span></li></ul>"]',
