            414 => 
            array (
                'id' => 2261,
                'lang_code' => 'en',
                'name' => 'Financial Modelling in Hospitality',
            'description' => '<p><span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(24, 3, 44);">In the hospitality industry, accurate financial management is crucial for making sound business decisions and maintaining profitability. Financial modeling helps hospitality professionals better understand their operations by providing a clear picture of revenue, expenses, and overall financial performance. These models allow for informed decision-making by offering insights into different scenarios, helping businesses plan for growth, manage costs, and improve long-term sustainability. The Financial Modelling in Hospitality course is designed to provide participants with the essential skills needed to develop and analyze financial models that directly address the unique challenges and needs of the hospitality sector.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(24, 3, 44);">Throughout the course, participants will gain practical experience with advanced Excel functions, learning how to structure data effectively for financial analysis and forecasting. The program will also cover important topics such as expense modelling, chart of accounts creation, and real-world financial analysis techniques. By mastering these areas, participants will be able to build financial models that enhance business decision-making and support ongoing financial health in their hospitality operations. This course is structured to ensure that attendees not only learn the theory behind financial modelling but also apply it in a way that is practical and relevant to their everyday professional challenges.</span></p>',
                'duration' => '5',
            'days_content' => '["<p><strong style=\\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Introduction to Financial Modelling in Hospitality&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Definition of modeling and financial models</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Discussing the importance and benefits of financial modeling in strategic decision-making</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Discovering common financial modeling types</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Exploring the applications of financial modeling in hospitality</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Reviewing and analyzing financial statements specific to hospitality:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">             Income statements</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">             </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Balance sheets</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">             </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Cash flow statements</span></li></ol>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Advanced Excel Techniques for Financial Modeling</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Advanced functions and formulas in Excel:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">       Array functions</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">       </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Index-match</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">       </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Conditional formulas</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Data analysis tools:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">       </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Pivot Tables</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">       </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Power Query</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Steps of structuring models in Excel for clarity and usability</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Understanding documentation and version control in financial models</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Discussing best practices and common challenges in building financial models</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Chart of Account Classification in Financial Modeling</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Definition chart of accounts classification and its role in organizing financial data</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Steps of designing charts and classifying accounts into major categories</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Ways of linking chart of accounts with revenue and expense models</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Using chart of accounts to improve financial performance forecasts and facilitate reporting</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Best practices for regular update and maintenance of charts</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Discussing the importance of documenting any changes in charts for effective financial management</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Detailed Expense Modeling</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Distinguishing between fixed and variable cost analysis</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Steps of categorizing costs specific to hospitality operations</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Labor cost modeling techniques:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">        Occupancy-based techniques&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">        </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Service level-based techniques</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Process of capital expenditure planning</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Strategies for identifying areas of cost saving in hospitality</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">&nbsp;Financial Analysis and Valuation</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Exploring various financial metrics</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Exploring types of financial analysis:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">        Break-even analysis</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">        </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Scenario analysis</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">        </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Sensitivity analysis</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Ways of conducting financial analysis</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Discussing the pros and cons of each financial analysis approaches</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Techniques for integrating sensitivity analysis and scenario analysis in financial models&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Lesson learned and best practices</span></li></ul>"]',
