            'days_content' => '["<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Introduction to Project Closing&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Reviewing key phases in construction projects lifecycle&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Understanding project closeout in construction: Terms, significance, and objectives&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Key stages of construction project closeout&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Identifying the roles and responsibilities during closeout&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Exploring construction project closeout categories:&nbsp;</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Client closeout&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Organizational closeout&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Subcontractor closeout</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Team closeout</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Reviewing regulatory requirements and standards related to project closeout&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Discussion on common challenges and issues during project closeout</span></li></ul><p><br></p>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Documentation and Punch List&nbsp;<span class=\\"ql-cursor\\">﻿</span></strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Exploring key documents required to close a construction project&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Steps and methods to prepare operation and maintenance (O&amp;M) manuals for clients&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Definition of as-built drawings and its role in reflecting the final status of the project&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Best practices for documenting and managing warranties and guarantees&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Techniques and strategies to create, manage, and resolve punch lists&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Methods and tools to track the progress of punch list items</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Activity: Creating an O&amp;M manual and punch list for a simulated construction project </span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Financial Closeout and Final Payments&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Understanding the financial aspects of project closeout&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Definition and importance of financial reconciliation&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Understanding the usage of retainage releases in construction projects&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Techniques for handling change orders and claims&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Definition and importance of lien waivers and best practices for securing lien releases&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Techniques and tools to prepare final financial reports&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Group activity: reconciling a budget for a simulated construction project </span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Substantial Completion and Inspection&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Definition and importance of substantial completion&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Understanding the final inspection process and its significance&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Exploring certifications required for final handover:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Third-party certifications&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Certificate of occupancy&nbsp;</span></li></ol><p><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\"><span class=\\"ql-cursor\\">﻿</span></span></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Discussing the importance of a final walkthrough to verify work completion&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Methods for transferring utilities and facilities&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Discussion on challenges and pitfalls in project inspection </span></li></ul><p><br></p>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Handover and Post-Closeout&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Discovering the phases of the final handover to the client&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Understanding system verification as a part of the final handover&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Exploring the main types of supports required after closeout&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Discussing the importance of providing end-user training&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Identifying the importance of documenting lessons learned from the project&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Case studies highlighting best practices in post-closeout support</span><strong style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(98, 98, 98);\\"> </strong></li></ul>"]',
