            'description' => '<p><span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(24, 3, 44);">Innovation has become a key driver of success in modern business environments. Organisations that can effectively manage and lead innovation are better equipped to create products that meet customer needs, improve market positioning, and sustain long-term growth. The Certified Innovation Leader course provides participants with the essential skills and knowledge to guide innovation initiatives within their organisations, focusing on building a culture of creativity and strategic alignment throughout the product lifecycle.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(24, 3, 44);">This course covers all aspects of the innovation process, from generating new ideas and developing business cases to planning projects, managing risks, and conducting product testing. Participants will also explore the practical tools and methods used to ensure successful transitions from the idea stage to product development, helping their teams work efficiently and deliver products that add real value to the market. By gaining a comprehensive understanding of how to manage and execute innovation initiatives, participants will leave the course prepared to contribute to their organisation’s growth and competitiveness.</span></p>',
                'duration' => '5',
            'days_content' => '["<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Innovation Strategic Alignment&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Understanding the meaning of innovation and its key related terms</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Discussing the roles and responsibilities of innovation leader</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Overview of managing front end process&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">The role of strategic alignment in fostering innovation&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Identifying key areas for aligning innovation with organizational goals and strategy&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Strategies to cultivate supportive innovation culture and promote creativity mindset</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Exploring various tools and methodologies to drive organizational change </span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Ideation &amp; Business Case Development</strong></p><p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Exploring different innovation framework and their application in innovation&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Utilizing ideation techniques to generate creative ideas&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Understanding voice of the customer (VOC) tools&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Establishing criteria for evaluating and selecting the right ideas for potential business case development&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Discussing how to assess the financial feasibility and financial aspects of proposed innovation projects&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Evaluate the market potential of the product concept&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Crafting a compelling business case for moving forward with new product development process </span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Knowledge Creation &amp; Project Planning&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Techniques for managing the transition from front end management into new product development process&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Creating customer-centric product through identifying customer’s pain points and collecting VOC data&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Discussing the elements that create customer value&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Tactics for organizing and planning for gate meetings and gate decision&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Exploring the elements of project plan and identify the significance of planning&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Identifying project’s objectives and deliverables</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Strategies for risk management planning</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Understanding how to plan for increased success </span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Innovation Development &amp; Lunch&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">The importance of integrating customer feedback and needs into the design process&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Understanding Alpha and Beta testing</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Techniques for developing portfolio management plans</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Discussing how to prepare for lunch&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Understanding the meaning and function of roll-out strategy&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Discussing activities should be done after lunch:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">        Selling</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\">        <span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Evaluation&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\">        <span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Take action cycle&nbsp;</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Discussing the importance of planning for next generation activities</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Prototyping, Testing &amp; Leadership&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Discussing the key components of successful prototyping&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Techniques for conducting concept testing to assess the suitability of product ideas</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Discussing how to create communication strategies to communicate innovation messages to internal stakeholders&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Exploring tools and methodologies for innovation&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Discussing the principles of effective coaching for innovation&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Methods for maintaining and sustaining innovation initiatives&nbsp;</span></li></ul>"]',
