            427 => 
            array (
                'id' => 2274,
                'lang_code' => 'en',
            'name' => 'Preparation Course for Project Management Professional (PMP)',
            'description' => '<p><span style="color: rgb(24, 3, 44);">The PMP® Preparation Course offers an in-depth exploration of the core concepts and methodologies in project management, designed to equip participants with the knowledge and skills required to pass the Project Management Professional (PMP)® certification exam. Grounded in the PMI’s PMP® examination content outline, the course covers all aspects of managing projects efficiently, from understanding the role and responsibilities of project managers to mastering advanced techniques in planning, execution, monitoring, and closing projects.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style="color: rgb(24, 3, 44);">Throughout this course, participants will engage with key project management domains such as stakeholder management, project lifecycle performance, workflow optimization, and risk mitigation. By delving into both theoretical concepts and practical applications, this course enables participants to develop a comprehensive understanding of how to apply project management principles in real-world scenarios. Case studies, exercises, and interactive discussions will also help attendees refine their leadership skills, enhance team dynamics, and successfully manage complex projects. In addition to preparing for the PMP® exam, participants will leave the course with actionable insights that can be applied immediately in their professional roles.</span></p>',
                'duration' => '10',
            'days_content' => '["<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Introduction to Project Management</strong></p><p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\">PMI Project Management Professional (PMP)® examination content outline</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\">Definition and purpose of project management, and the role of project managers</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\">Understanding the principles of value creation and delivery in project management</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\">Exploring core functions associated with projects</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\">Describing the environment in which the project operates: External vs. Internal environment</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\">Discussing the principles of project management and their impact on project execution</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Stakeholder and Team Performance Domains</strong><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Definition of project stakeholder and their impact on a project</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Describing the process of stakeholder engagement</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Understanding the dynamics of a project team and the aspects of team development</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Discussing key leadership skills required to lead and manage project team</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Exploring project team management and leadership strategies</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Recognizing the role of project managers in building project team culture and creating a high-performing project team</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Development Approach and Life Cycle Performance Domain&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Analyzing the relationship between development, cadence and life cycle</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Definition of delivery cadence and its types</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Distinguishing between development approaches: Predictive vs. Hybrid vs. Adaptive</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Criteria and key considerations for selecting a development approach</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Exploring phases in the project life cycle</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Understanding the alignment between delivery cadence, development approach and life cycle</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Planning Performance Domains</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Definition and purpose of planning in project management</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Exploring the variables of planning: Delivery, estimation, schedules and budget</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Methods to plan for project team composition and structure</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Identifying the importance of planning for communication and changes</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Steps and methods to plan for physical resources and procurement</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Understanding metrics and alignment planning</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Project Work Performance Domain</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Understanding project processes and ways of optimizing processes for the environment</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Discussing the importance of balancing competing constraints associated with project work</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Methods and best practices for maintaining project team focus</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Understanding the type of project communication and ways of ensuring engagement</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Techniques for managing physical resources</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Exploring types of contracting and procurement in projects and the way of working with them</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Best practices for monitoring new work and changes in projects and the importance of learning throughout the project</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Delivery Performance Domain</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Definition of project delivery and its importance</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Understanding delivery of value in projects</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Describing project deliverables:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">      Requirements</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">      </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Scope definition</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">      </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Moving targets of completion</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Discussing the ways of reflecting quality requirements in projects</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Definition of suboptimal outcomes and best practices for reducing negative outcomes</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Measurement Performance Domain</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Understanding the purpose and needs for project measures</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Steps of establishing effective measures</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Discussing what to measure in projects</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Methods for presenting measurement findings and information</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Challenges and pitfalls related to measurement</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Tools and techniques for troubleshooting performance</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Uncertainty Performance Domain</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Recognizing nuances to uncertainty in project management</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Methods to respond to uncertainty</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Definition of ambiguity and its categories</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Understanding complexity in project management and its types</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Methods for addressing volatility in the project environment</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Distinguishing between threats and opportunities as types of project risk</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Definition of contingency reserve and the importance of managing reserve</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Tailoring</strong></p><p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Definition of tailoring and its role in adopting project management processes&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Identifying types of project management elements that can be tailored for different projects</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Describing the tailoring process based on project needs</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Methods for tailoring project performance domains</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Exploring diagnostics techniques for various situations&nbsp; </span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Models, Methods and Artifacts&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Exploring commonly used models and their applications across the performance domain</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Exploring commonly used methods and their applications across the performance domain</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Exploring commonly used artefacts and their applications across the performance domain</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Exploring the interaction between performance domains for project success</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Lessons Learned and Best Practices</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Final Q&amp;A and Course Wrap-Up</span></li></ul>"]',
