            'name' => 'Preparation Course for Project Management Professional (PMP)',
            'description' => '<p><span style="color: rgb(24, 3, 44);">The PMP® Preparation Course offers an in-depth exploration of the core concepts and methodologies in project management, designed to equip participants with the knowledge and skills required to pass the Project Management Professional (PMP)® certification exam. Grounded in the PMI’s PMP® examination content outline, the course covers all aspects of managing projects efficiently, from understanding the role and responsibilities of project managers to mastering advanced techniques in planning, execution, monitoring, and closing projects.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style="color: rgb(24, 3, 44);">Throughout this course, participants will engage with key project management domains such as stakeholder management, project lifecycle performance, workflow optimization, and risk mitigation. By delving into both theoretical concepts and practical applications, this course enables participants to develop a comprehensive understanding of how to apply project management principles in real-world scenarios. Case studies, exercises, and interactive discussions will also help attendees refine their leadership skills, enhance team dynamics, and successfully manage complex projects. In addition to preparing for the PMP® exam, participants will leave the course with actionable insights that can be applied immediately in their professional roles.</span></p>',
                'duration' => '10',
