            'name' => 'Preparation Course for Project Management Professional (PMP)',
            'description' => '<p><span style="color: rgb(24, 3, 44);">This PMP® Preparation Course is designed to offer a thorough understanding of project management principles, focusing on the key domains that form the foundation of the Project Management Professional (PMP)® certification. The course provides an in-depth look at how project management practices are applied in real-world situations, covering topics such as stakeholder engagement, project team dynamics, lifecycle phases, and performance management. Each session is structured to help participants not only prepare for the PMP® exam but also to apply best practices in managing projects efficiently.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style="color: rgb(24, 3, 44);">Participants will gain insights into tailoring project management processes to suit the unique needs of different projects, as well as how to use models, methods, and artifacts that are critical to ensuring project success. Through hands-on activities, discussions, and case studies, attendees will explore how to adapt their approaches to meet the demands of both internal and external environments. The course wraps up with lessons learned and best practices that participants can apply in their day-to-day project management activities.</span></p>',
                'duration' => '5',
            'days_content' => '["<p><strong>Introduction to Project Management</strong></p><p><strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">PMI Project Management Professional (PMP)® examination content outline</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Definition and purpose of project management, and the role of project managers</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Understanding the principles of value creation and delivery in project management</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Exploring core functions associated with projects</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Describing the environment in which the project operates: External vs. Internal environment</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Discussing the principles of project management and their impact on project execution</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Project Performance Domain I</strong></p><p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\"><span class=\\"ql-cursor\\">﻿</span></strong></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Defining project performance domains and understanding the way they operate</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Exploring the interaction between performance domains for project success</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Activities and functions associated with stakeholders</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Activities and functions associated with the project team</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Activities and functions associated with the development approach and lifecycle phases of a project</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Project Performance Domain II&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Activities and functions associated with planning, initiating, and organizing projects</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Activities and functions associated with establishing and managing project work&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Activities and functions associated with delivering the project’s scope and quality</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Activities and functions associated with the measurement of project performance</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Activities and functions associated with risk and uncertainty</span></li></ul>","<p><strong>Tailoring</strong></p><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Definition of tailoring and its role in adopting project management processes&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Identifying types of project management elements that can be tailored for different projects</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Describing the tailoring process based on project needs</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Methods for tailoring project performance domains</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Exploring diagnostics techniques for various situations&nbsp;</span></li></ul>","<p><strong>Models, Methods and Artifacts&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Exploring commonly used models and their applications across the performance domain</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Exploring commonly used methods and their applications across the performance domain</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Exploring commonly used artefacts and their applications across the performance domain</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Exploring the interaction between performance domains for project success</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Lessons Learned and Best Practices</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Final Q&amp;A and Course Wrap-Up</span></li></ul>"]',
