                'lang_code' => 'en',
                'name' => 'IT in Hospitality Operations',
            'description' => '<p><span style="color: rgb(24, 3, 44);">The IT in Hospitality Operations course provides a comprehensive understanding of the role of information technology in the modern hospitality industry. As technology becomes more integral to enhancing guest experiences and streamlining operational efficiency, this course delves into the specific tools and systems that are reshaping hospitality management. From front-desk operations to back-office systems, participants will explore how technology such as property management systems (PMS), in-room automation, keyless entry, and customer relationship management (CRM) software can drive better guest satisfaction and operational control.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style="color: rgb(24, 3, 44);">The course also covers critical aspects of system selection, integration, and maintenance, ensuring that participants are well-equipped to implement and manage these technologies within their organizations. Additionally, emerging technologies such as AI, machine learning, and virtual reality will be discussed, highlighting their growing influence in the hospitality sector. By the end of this course, attendees will be able to navigate the complex intersection of IT and hospitality, using technology to address challenges, improve service, and support the operational needs of the industry.</span></p>',
