            461 => 
            array (
                'id' => 2311,
                'lang_code' => 'en',
                'name' => 'Hotel Investments Analysis and Financing',
            'description' => '<p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Hotel investment analysis involves a detailed assessment of the financial performance and viability of hotel properties, using key financial metrics such as Net Present Value (NPV), Internal Rate of Return (IRR), and performance ratios to guide decision-making. Understanding cost behaviour and applying costing methods like Activity-Based Costing (ABC) is essential for optimizing financial control and planning in hotel operations. Additionally, advanced techniques such as Cost-Volume-Profit (CVP) analysis and risk analysis tools enable investors and managers to forecast financial outcomes and address potential uncertainties in hotel investments.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">In the Hotel Investments Analysis and Financing course, participants will apply these financial principles and tools to real-world scenarios. They will learn how to evaluate hotel investments from multiple perspectives, including those of owners, managers, and lenders, and make informed decisions on capital investments and financing. The course will also cover strategies for optimizing capital structure using methods like Weighted Average Cost of Capital (WACC) and the Capital Asset Pricing Model (CAPM), while also exploring the implications of various financing options on the overall financial strategy.</span></p>',
                'duration' => '5',
            'days_content' => '["<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Financial Performance in Hospitality&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\">Identifying types of information and data required for financial statements</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\">Describing the nature of financial statements and their usage in hospitality</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\">Definition of financial analysis and its role in decision-making</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\">Steps of conducting ratio analysis and creating pyramids of ratios to evaluate business performance</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\">Discussing the importance of evaluating business performance from multiple perspectives:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\">&nbsp;&nbsp;Management’s point of view</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\">Owners’ point of view</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\">Lenders’ point of view</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\">Discussing the prediction of financial distress using metrics and indicators</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Investment Decision Analysis Techniques&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Overview of investment decision analysis techniques and the adaption of strategic perspective</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Understanding the way of evaluating investment opportunities using time-adjusted measures</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Formulas for calculating investment appraisal to evaluate hotel investments:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">   &nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Net Present Value (NPV)</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">   &nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Internal Rate of Return (IRR)</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">   &nbsp; &nbsp; Economic Value Added (EVA)</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Techniques for refining investment analysis:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">   &nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\\">Equivalent annual cost (EAC)</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">   &nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\\">Modified internal rate of return (MIRR)</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\\">Discussing the impact of risks and uncertainty in hotel investment and the way of addressing them</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\\">Exploring risk analysis techniques used in investment-decision making:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">   &nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\\">Sensitivity Analysis</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">   &nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\\">Scenario Analysis,</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">   &nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\\">Simulation</span></li></ol>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Financing Strategies for Hotel Investments&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\\">Distinguishing between long-term and short-term sources of finance available for hotel investments</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\\">Exploring types of equity capital and debt financing</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Criteria for selecting the optimal capital structure</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Steps of calculating of </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\\">Weighted Cost of Capital (WACC) and The Capital Asset Pricing Model (CAPM)</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\\">Determining the appropriate situation for using WACC and CAPM</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Discussing the implications of dividend decisions on financing strategy</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Cost Analysis Techniques for Hospitality Management</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Analyzation of cost behaviour and activities within hotel operations</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Describing the classification of cost:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">     &nbsp; &nbsp; Fixed vs. variable costs</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">     &nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Direct vs. indirect costs</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Distinguishing between product costs and period costs</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Exploring techniques for cost allocation and absorption of overheads</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Understanding costing methods:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">     &nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Absorption costing</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">     &nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Marginal costing</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Steps of performing Cost-Volume-Profit (CVP) analysis and what-if scenarios using Excel</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Exploring cost management techniques:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">     &nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\\">Activity Based Costing (ABC)</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">     &nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\\">Activity Based Management (ABM)</span></li></ol>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Budgeting and Performance Management&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Understanding the purpose and benefits of budgeting in the hospitality sector</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Exploring key phases of the budgeting preparation process</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Strategies for developing a master budget</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Methods for effective budgetary control:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">          Responsibility accounting</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">          </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Variance analysis</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Discussing the advantages and disadvantages of budgeting in the hotel context</span></li></ul>"]',
                'related_courses' => '[]',
