                'duration' => '5',
            'days_content' => '["<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Financial Performance in Hospitality&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Identifying types of information and data required for financial statements</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Describing the nature of financial statements and their usage in hospitality</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Definition of financial analysis and its role in decision-making</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Steps of conducting ratio analysis and creating pyramids of ratios to evaluate business performance</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Discussing the importance of evaluating business performance from multiple perspectives:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">     &nbsp; &nbsp; Management’s point of view</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">     &nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Owners’ point of view</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">     &nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Lenders’ point of view</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Discussing the prediction of financial distress using metrics and indicators</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Investment Decision Analysis Techniques&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Overview of investment decision analysis techniques and the adaption of strategic perspective</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Understanding the way of evaluating investment opportunities using time-adjusted measures</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Formulas for calculating investment appraisal to evaluate hotel investments:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">   &nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Net Present Value (NPV)</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">   &nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Internal Rate of Return (IRR)</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">   &nbsp; &nbsp; Economic Value Added (EVA)</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Techniques for refining investment analysis:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">   &nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\\">Equivalent annual cost (EAC)</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">   &nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\\">Modified internal rate of return (MIRR)</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\\">Discussing the impact of risks and uncertainty in hotel investment and the way of addressing them</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\\">Exploring risk analysis techniques used in investment-decision making:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">   &nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\\">Sensitivity Analysis</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">   &nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\\">Scenario Analysis,</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">   &nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\\">Simulation</span></li></ol>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Financing Strategies for Hotel Investments&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\\">Distinguishing between long-term and short-term sources of finance available for hotel investments</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\\">Exploring types of equity capital and debt financing</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Criteria for selecting the optimal capital structure</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Steps of calculating of </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\\">Weighted Cost of Capital (WACC) and The Capital Asset Pricing Model (CAPM)</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\\">Determining the appropriate situation for using WACC and CAPM</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Discussing the implications of dividend decisions on financing strategy</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Cost Analysis Techniques for Hospitality Management</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Analyzation of cost behaviour and activities within hotel operations</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Describing the classification of cost:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">     &nbsp; &nbsp; Fixed vs. variable costs</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">     &nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Direct vs. indirect costs</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Distinguishing between product costs and period costs</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Exploring techniques for cost allocation and absorption of overheads</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Understanding costing methods:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">     &nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Absorption costing</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">     &nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Marginal costing</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Steps of performing Cost-Volume-Profit (CVP) analysis and what-if scenarios using Excel</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Exploring cost management techniques:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">     &nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\\">Activity Based Costing (ABC)</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">     &nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\\">Activity Based Management (ABM)</span></li></ol>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Budgeting and Performance Management&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Understanding the purpose and benefits of budgeting in the hospitality sector</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Exploring key phases of the budgeting preparation process</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Strategies for developing a master budget</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Methods for effective budgetary control:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">          Responsibility accounting</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">          </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Variance analysis</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Discussing the advantages and disadvantages of budgeting in the hotel context</span></li></ul>"]',
