            463 => 
            array (
                'id' => 2313,
                'lang_code' => 'en',
                'name' => 'English Law System in International Disputes: Risks and Rewards',
            'description' => '<p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">The English legal system plays a central role in many international disputes, offering a framework widely recognised for its stability, precedent-based rulings, and detailed procedures. Understanding how English law operates in an international context is crucial for legal professionals and business practitioners alike. One key aspect of English law is its reliance on the common law system, which uses judicial decisions as primary sources of law, in contrast to many other jurisdictions that follow civil law systems. This approach precedes previous court decisions, creating a reliable structure for contractual obligations, dispute resolution, and risk management in legal agreements.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">In the English Law System in International Disputes: Risks and Rewards course, participants will gain an in-depth understanding of these aspects of English law and learn how to apply them effectively in international disputes. The course covers key areas such as contract drafting under English law, risk assessment and allocation, and various dispute resolution strategies like arbitration and mediation. By the end of the course, participants will be well-equipped to manage legal risks, draft contracts in compliance with English law, and navigate complex international legal disputes with greater confidence.</span></p>',
                'duration' => '5',
            'days_content' => '["<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Introduction to the English Law System&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\">Overview of the historical development of the English Law</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\">Identifying the characteristics of the English Law</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\">Distinguishing between the English Law and the Civil Law systems</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\">Describing the principle of Justice in English Law</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent;\\">Recognizing the role of English Law in international legal transactions</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Sources of English Law and Court Structure</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Distinguishing between the primary and secondary sources of English Law</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Exploring the main sources of English law:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">     &nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Decisions of the Courts</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">     &nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Statues</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">     &nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Case Law</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">     &nbsp; &nbsp; Customs and Conventions</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Understanding the Doctrine of Precedent and its applications</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Describing the principles of State Decisis in court decisions</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Understanding the structure of English courts</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Exploring common types of English courts</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">The English Contract Law</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Definition and purpose of the English contract law</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Exploring the process of forming a contract under the English Law:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">       Offer and Acceptance</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">       </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Consideration</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">       </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Intention to create legal relations</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Explaining the components of a contract:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">       </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Express terms</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">       </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Implied terms</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Methods for terminating contracts:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">       </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Expiry</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">       </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Termination</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">       </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Rescission</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">       </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Frustration</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Describing the way English contract law deals with breaches:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">       </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Conditions</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">       </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Warranties</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">       </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Remedies</span></li></ol>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Risk Allocation Strategies in Contractual Agreements&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Discussing types of risks in contractual agreements and the importance of risk allocation&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Exploring risk allocation strategies: Indemnity Clauses and Limitations</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Understanding the concepts of force majeure and frustration in English contract law</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Explaining the mechanism of contractual clauses in risk transfer</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Discussing factors affecting risk allocation in contractual agreements</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Exploring negotiation strategies for risk allocation</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Disputes Resolution Strategies</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Describing the English litigation process</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Exploring stages of litigation</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Discussing alternative dispute resolution strategies:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">        </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Arbitration</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">        </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Mediation</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">        Negotiation</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Criteria for selecting the appropriate dispute resolution method&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Discussing the enforcement of international judgments </span></li></ul>"]',
                'related_courses' => '[]',
                'category_id' => 18,
                'online' => 1,
                'created_at' => '2025-04-03 12:54:55',
                'updated_at' => '2025-04-03 12:54:55',
