ckground-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Understanding the Doctrine of Precedent and its applications</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Describing the principles of State Decisis in court decisions</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Understanding the structure of English courts</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Exploring common types of English courts</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">The English Contract Law</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Definition and purpose of the English contract law</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Exploring the process of forming a contract under the English Law:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">       Offer and Acceptance</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">       </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Consideration</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">       </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Intention to create legal relations</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Explaining the components of a contract:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">       </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Express terms</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">       </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Implied terms</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Methods for terminating contracts:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">       </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Expiry</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">       </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Termination</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">       </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Rescission</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">       </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Frustration</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Describing the way English contract law deals with breaches:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">       </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Conditions</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">       </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Warranties</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">       </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Remedies</span></li></ol>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Risk Allocation Strategies in Contractual Agreements&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Discussing types of risks in contractual agreements and the importance of risk allocation&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Exploring risk allocation strategies: Indemnity Clauses and Limitations</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Understanding the concepts of force majeure and frustration in English contract law</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Explaining the mechanism of contractual clauses in risk transfer</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Discussing factors affecting risk allocation in contractual agreements</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Exploring negotiation strategies for risk allocation</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Disputes Resolution Strategies</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Describing the English litigation process</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Exploring stages of litigation</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Discussing alternative dispute resolution strategies:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">        </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Arbitration</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">        </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Mediation</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">        Negotiation</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Criteria for selecting the appropriate dispute resolution method&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Discussing the enforcement of international judgments </span></li></ul>"]',
