 41);\\">Describing the criteria for identifying contract validity with customers</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Understanding contract combination and contract modifications</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Discussing the characteristics of a distinct good, service, and bundles of both</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Techniques for assessing the implied promises and administrative tasks</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Exploring treatment methods of warranties, licenses and options</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Transaction Price and Allocation&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Exploring types of considerations for determining transaction price:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">         Variable considerations and the constraints</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">         </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Significant financing components</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">         </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Non-cash considerations</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">         </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Consideration payable to a customer</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Discussing the accounting method for sales taxes and duties</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Analyzing the impact of customer credit risk on transaction price</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Describing the steps of allocating the transaction price:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">         </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Determine standalone selling prices</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">         </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Allocate the transaction price</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Understanding the treatment of contract modification and reallocation for price</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Revenue Recognition and Contract Costs&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Describing types of revenue recognition: over-time vs. point-in-time recognition</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Discussing situations when control of goods and services is transferred</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Exploring methods for measuring the progress towards complete satisfaction of a performance obligation</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Discussing the way to deal with repurchase, consignment, and bill-and-hold agreements</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Describing the accounting for contract costs:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">           Costs of obtaining a contract</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">           </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Costs of fulfilling a contract</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\\">Understanding the amortization of contract costs and impairment considerations </span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Presentation, Disclosures, and Application Issues</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Exploring presentation requirements of financial position, profit/loss and cash flows under IFRS 15</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Reviewing annual and interim disclosure requirements under IFRS 15</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Discussing the application of IFRS 15 standard to licences of intellectual property</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Analyzing application issues of IFRS 15</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Best practices and lessons learned </span></li></ul>"]',
