                'lang_code' => 'en',
                'name' => 'Comprehensive Energy and Procurement Management: Strategies, Contracts, and Future Trends',
            'description' => '<p><span style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);">Navigating the complexities of the energy sector requires a solid grasp of procurement strategies, contract management, and an awareness of industry trends. As global energy markets shift, professionals in the field must be equipped to handle evolving contracts, manage supplier relationships, and mitigate risks effectively. The Comprehensive Energy and Procurement Management: Strategies, Contracts, and Future Trends course provides an in-depth understanding of these areas, focusing on essential skills for managing upstream and downstream contracts in energy. This course also explores the fundamentals of risk assessment, supplier management, and strategic sourcing, ensuring that participants are prepared to address challenges unique to energy procurement.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);">Designed to offer practical insights, the seven-day program includes case studies and real-world scenarios that allow participants to refine their negotiation skills, develop sustainable procurement processes, and analyze emerging trends that impact the energy industry. By the end of the course, participants will be equipped to lead procurement initiatives with confidence and foresight, positioning their organizations for sustainable growth.</span></p>',
                'duration' => '7',
            'days_content' => '["<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Global Energy Market and Energy Contracts</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Overview of structure and key players in global energy markets</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Defining energy contracts and their purpose&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Exploring the main types and components of energy contracts&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Discovering the lifecycle of energy contracts</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Analyzing the impact of future trends and technological advancements in energy contracts </span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Energy Industry Risk Management&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Describing types of risks in the energy industry:&nbsp;</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ul><li>Market Risks&nbsp;</li><li>Credit Risks</li><li>Operational Risks</li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\">Regulatory Risk</li></ul><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Recognizing the process of risk assessment in energy contracts&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Exploring risk assessment techniques and tools</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Discussing risk mitigation strategies to minimize the impact of risks in the energy industry&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Case studies and real-world examples</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Energy Contract Analysis: Upstream and Downstream Contracts&nbsp;<span class=\\"ql-cursor\\">﻿</span></strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Distinguishing between upstream and downstream contracts&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Describing types of upstream energy contracts:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Exploration Contract</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Production Contract</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Drilling Contract</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Describing types of downstream energy contracts:&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Refining Contracts</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Distribution Contracts</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Retail Contracts&nbsp;</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Determining and analyzing key clauses and common issues in energy contracts&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Case studies and real-world examples</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Strategic Procurement</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Understanding strategic procurement: Definition, purpose and history&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Determining the role of strategic procurement in driving organizational growth&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Overview of strategic procurement process and its cycle stages&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Describing the main components of procurement planning:&nbsp;</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Needs identification&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Market research&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Budgeting&nbsp;</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Definition of sustainable procurement and the impact of digitalization on strategic procurement </span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Supplier Management and Vendor Relationship Building</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Exploring the methodology and criteria for identifying and selecting suppliers&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Techniques for developing and maintaining supplier relationships:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Communication&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Performance monitoring&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Dispute resolution&nbsp;</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Discussing the way of improving supplier performance through development and governance&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Exploring tools and techniques to identify and manage supplier risk&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Case studies and real-world examples</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Strategic Sourcing and Category Management</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Defining strategic sourcing and its benefits&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Describing the process of strategic sourcing&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Understanding category management strategy in procurement&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Discussing the role of cross-functional teams in strategic sourcing and category management&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Determining the role of market intelligence in strategic sourcing and category management </span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Negotiation and Contract Management&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Introduction to the principles of contract negotiation:&nbsp;</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ul><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Preparing negotiations</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Conducting negotiations&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Closing negotiations&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Exploring techniques and strategies for effective negotiation of contractual clauses&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Strategies and best practices for effective management of contacts&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Discussing conflict resolution strategies in contract management&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Case studies and real-world examples&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Course review and certification delivery </span></li></ul>"]',
                'related_courses' => '[]',
                'category_id' => 12,
                'online' => 0,
                'created_at' => '2025-04-03 12:55:02',
                'updated_at' => '2025-04-03 12:55:02',
            ),
            487 => 
            array (
                'id' => 2339,
                'lang_code' => 'en',
                'name' => 'IFRS Sustainability Disclosure Standards',
            'description' => '<p><strong style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">IFRS Sustainability Disclosure Standards</strong><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">, introduced by the International Sustainability Standards Board (ISSB), provide a structured framework for disclosing sustainability-related financial information. These&nbsp;</span><strong style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">IFRS sustainability disclosure standards</strong><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">&nbsp;</span><strong style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">s1 and s2</strong><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">, are crucial in helping businesses address the increasing demand for transparency in how they manage climate-related risks and opportunities. By implementing these standards, organizations can ensure consistent, reliable reporting, giving investors and decision-makers insight into sustainability impacts on business performance and resilience. This course offers a comprehensive overview of these standards, covering core requirements for disclosures in governance, strategy, risk management, and key metrics.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Participants in this course will develop practical skills to assess materiality, recognize sustainability opportunities, and create a tailored sustainability reporting plan. Ideal for ESG professionals, corporate reporting teams, and financial officers, the course equips attendees with tools for producing decision-useful disclosures that meet global standards. By the end, participants will be prepared to apply&nbsp;</span><strong style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">ISSB IFRS sustainability disclosure standards</strong><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">&nbsp;effectively, helping their organizations enhance transparency and align with best practices in sustainability reporting.</span></p>',
                'duration' => '5',
            'days_content' => '["<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Introduction to International Sustainability Standards Board (ISSB)</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\\">Definition of sustainability and the impact of climate change on businesses</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\\">Recognizing the growing demand for sustainability information</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\\">Understanding the purpose of ISSB and its methodology</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\\">Defining IFRS Sustainability Disclosure Standards and their purpose:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\\"> IFRS S1: General Requirements for Disclosure of Sustainability-related Financial Information</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\"> </span><span style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\\">IFRS S2: Climate-related Disclosures</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\\">Exploring the benefits and challenges of applying ISSB standards</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\\">Discussing the interconnection between IFRS and other standards and frameworks</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">IFRS S1 vs. IFRS S2</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Exploring IFRS S1 requirements and applications</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Exploring IFRS S2 requirements and applications</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Determining the intended users of IFRS disclosures</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Understanding industry-specific disclosure requirements</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Identifying the relationship between IFRS S1 and IFRS S2</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Techniques for ensuring consistency and achieving fair and faithful presentations</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">IFRS Sustainability-Related Financial Disclosures</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Definition of sustainability-related risks and opportunities and identifying their sources</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Identifying types of opportunities and risks ISSB standards focus on</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Discussing types of disclosures required for each sustainability-related risk and opportunity</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Exploring disclosure requirements for different content areas:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">        Governance</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">        </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Strategy</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">        </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Risk Management</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">        </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Metrics and Targets</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Understanding location and timing requirements for sustainability-related financial disclosures</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Exploring transitional relief components and determining when they are applicable</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Producing Decision-Useful Sustainability Disclosers</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Identifying the characteristics of decision-useful disclosures</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">The application of IFRS Sustainability Disclosure Standards and guidance in identifying risks and opportunities</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Definition and characteristics of material information</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">The application of IFRS Sustainability Disclosure Standards and guidance in identifying information about risks and opportunities</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Exploring ISSB standards related to decision-useful information for investors</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Discovering judgment process of assessing whether the information is material</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Development of a Reporting Plan</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Phases of developing a reporting plan: Preparation, Alignment, Implementation, and communication</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Understanding the process of building collective capacity and identifying resorbable people for disclosure</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Techniques to evaluate existing disclosures and plan for the future:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">        Gap analysis</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">        </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Additional reporting requirements</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Discussing best implementation practices that help in achieving disclosure objectives</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Exploring communication methods and techniques and the best ways to include information in general-purpose reporting</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Activity: Developing a sustainability reporting plan</span></li></ul>"]',
                'related_courses' => '[]',
                'category_id' => 34,
                'online' => 1,
                'created_at' => '2025-04-03 12:55:03',
                'updated_at' => '2025-04-03 12:55:03',
