            'name' => 'Preparation for The Fundamentals of Sustainability Accounting (FSA) Credential: Level II',
            'description' => '<p><span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(24, 3, 44);">The Fundamentals of Sustainability Accounting</span><strong style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(24, 3, 44);"> (FSA) Credential</strong><span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(24, 3, 44);">: Level II is a key certification for professionals seeking to deepen their expertise in sustainability and its financial implications. This advanced credential focuses on assessing the value of sustainability issues by examining a company’s environmental, social, and governance (</span><strong style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(24, 3, 44);">ESG</strong><span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(24, 3, 44);">) factors, normalizing sustainability data, and understanding specific impacts. Level II provides rigorous training in evaluating sustainability risks and opportunities and how these factors influence financial performance, making it an essential qualification for professionals aiming to bridge the gap between sustainability performance and financial valuation.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(24, 3, 44);">This course offers a practical approach to prepare participants for the Level II exam, equipping them with skills to analyze ESG data, normalize industry performance, and integrate sustainability into financial valuation methods. By mastering techniques such as discounted cash flow (DCF) analysis, scenario planning, and performance benchmarking, participants will be able to provide valuable insights into sustainability impacts on long-term financial growth. The FSA Level II Credential is highly valued by companies, investors, and consultants, positioning those who earn it as leaders in today’s sustainability-focused financial landscape.</span></p>',
