            'days_content' => '["<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Identifying Sustainability Issues</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Introduction to FSA curriculum content</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Definition and nature of sustainability issues</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Discussing the differences between industries\' sustainability profiles</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Analyzing the impact of the company’s circumstances on material sustainability issues</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Recognizing the impact of governance and management practices on material sustainability</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Understanding the interrelated impacts of sustainability issues</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Evaluating Sustainability Issues</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Understanding the importance of assessing the relevance between sustainability issues and the company’s financial position and future performance</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Describing the five-factor approach and its usage in evaluating sustainability issues</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Determining the importance of contextualizing sustainability topics</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Best ways to make use of sustainability issues evaluation findings</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Case studies about contextualizing sustainability issues for specific industries</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Evaluating the Comparability of Sustainability Information</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Introduction to data normalizing and its role in comparison effectiveness</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Exploring normalization measures and understanding the criteria of selecting the appropriate one</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Understanding the ways of using normalizing in comparative analysis</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Steps of analyzing the spread of industry performance:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">        Understating your ESG data</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">        </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Analyzing data distribution</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">        </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Outliners and non-normal distribution</span></li><li><span style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">        </span><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Considering data quality</span></li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Identifying the importance of considering company-specific context during evaluation</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">The Connection Between Sustainability Performance and Valuation</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Introduction to the link between sustainability performance and channels of financial impact</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Understanding the process of characterizing the financial impacts of sustainability risks and opportunities</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Tools and techniques for assessing the likelihood, timing and magnitude of impacts</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Understanding the process of identifying metrics types and categories</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Utilizing discounted cash flow (DCF) analysis in financial valuation</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Integration of Sustainability into Financial Valuation</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Discovering the integration of ESG performance into the evaluation of returns and profitability&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Steps of using scenario analysis as a financial valuation tool&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Best practices for managing sustainability-related risks and opportunities</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Tips to prepare for the FSA credential level II exam</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Recap and Q&amp;A session</span></li></ul>"]',
