            499 => 
            array (
                'id' => 2351,
                'lang_code' => 'en',
                'name' => 'Filmmaking and Video Production',
            'description' => '<p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Filmmaking and video production are dynamic and captivating fields that combine creativity, storytelling, and technical expertise to produce compelling visual content. Whether crafting a cinematic masterpiece, a short film, or a corporate video, the process involves several stages from scripting and storyboarding to shooting and editing. These skills are essential in today\'s digital age, where video is a powerful medium for communication, marketing, and entertainment. By enrolling in film making courses, participants can explore the art and science of this industry and its significance across various domains.&nbsp;</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Our video production course offers a comprehensive learning journey, blending theoretical knowledge with experience. Participants will master skills in short film making courses and advanced videography techniques, equipping them with the tools to succeed in the competitive film and media landscape. Whether you’re an aspiring filmmaker or seeking to elevate your production expertise, this course provides a solid foundation in the essentials of storytelling, shooting, editing, and more, making it one of the most sought-after videography courses available today.</span></p>',
                'duration' => '5',
            'days_content' => '["<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\\">Introduction to Filmmaking&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Introduction to filmmaking and production: Key concepts and terms&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Stages of production and filmmaking&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Key skills and competencies necessary for filmmaking&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Understanding pre-production procedures&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">How to create shooting schedules and call sheets&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Risk assessment techniques for filmmaking and production</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Fundamentals of continuity filmmaking:</span></li></ul><p><br></p><ul><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Eye line</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">The 180-degree rule</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Screen direction&nbsp;</span></li></ul><p><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">﻿</span></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Best practices to manage filming projects&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Activity: Developing a complete plan for a filmmaking production&nbsp;</span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Fundamentals of Videography&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Exploring various types of cameras and lenses and their uses&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Discovering the basic settings and controls of the camera</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Techniques of shot composition and framing</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Understanding camera movements&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">How to capture high-quality audio?</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Techniques and tools for directing actors&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Audio production tools: Mixer, boom pole, shotgun microphone&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Activity: Practicing using production equipment, including cameras and audio tools&nbsp; </span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Storyboarding and Pre-Visualization&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">How to develop a film story?&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Basics of writing and refining a script&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Techniques to treat and format a screenplay&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">How do storyboards guide the production process?</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Techniques for creating and sketching storyboards</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Tools and software for storyboarding&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">How to translate a script into visuals?&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Activity: Writing a film story and translating it into storyboards &nbsp; </span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\\">Lighting Techniques for Interviews</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Basics of lighting&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">How to set lighting for interviews&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Exploring righting equipment&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Natural vs. artificial light</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Techniques for creating visual effects using lights&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Understanding the three-point lighting&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Activity: Practicing using lighting tools and equipment </span></li></ul>","<p><strong style=\\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\">Video Editing Techniques&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Exploring video editing software</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Navigating the interface and key tools of Adobe Premiere&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Understanding how Adobe Premiere works&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Understanding colour grading and correction&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Discovering video editing trends:</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Motion graphics&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Transitions&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\\"ql-indent-1\\"><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Effects&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Final Project and Presentation&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Lesson learned and recap</span></li><li><span style=\\"background-color: transparent;\\">Course evaluation </span></li></ul>"]',
                'related_courses' => '[]',
